        id: "3-purpose",
        title: "2\\. Purpose",
        level: 2,
        order: 3,
        body: "This policy mandates completion of a comprehensive patient assessment — including all required OASIS data elements at applicable time points — for every patient admitted to home health services at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. The comprehensive assessment is the clinical foundation upon which every other clinical activity in the home health episode depends. It is simultaneously: the clinical document that establishes the patient's eligibility for the Medicare home health benefit (homebound status, need for skilled services); the data source for all OASIS items that drive PDGM payment classification; the basis for the individualized plan of care; the baseline against which all clinical progress is measured; and the primary document that CMS surveyors and ADR auditors examine when evaluating whether the patient legitimately required — and received — skilled home health services. An inadequate, incomplete, or inaccurate comprehensive assessment cascades failure across the entire episode: an inaccurate OASIS produces the wrong PDGM payment group; an incomplete clinical picture produces a plan of care that does not reflect the patient's actual needs; missing homebound status documentation creates billing vulnerability; and inadequate assessment documentation fails to justify the skilled services billed. This policy implements 42 CFR § 484.55 — Condition of Participation: Comprehensive Assessment of Patients — which requires that a registered nurse complete a comprehensive assessment for each patient admitted to home health care that accurately reflects the patient's current health status and includes information that may be used to inform the individualized plan of care.\n\n---",
