        id: "6-definitions",
        title: "5\\. Definitions",
        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Comprehensive Assessment | The full, multidimensional clinical assessment of a home health patient required by 42 CFR § 484.55, incorporating all required OASIS data elements and all clinical domains specified in this policy. Only a registered nurse may complete this assessment. |\n| OASIS (Outcome and Assessment Information Set) | The standardized data collection instrument mandated by CMS for Medicare-certified home health agencies, used to measure patient outcomes and clinical characteristics and to inform PDGM payment classification. The current version is OASIS-E2. |\n| OASIS Assessment Time Points | The specific clinical events that trigger a required OASIS assessment: Start of Care (SOC), Resumption of Care (ROC), Recertification (RECERT), Follow-Up (FU), Transfer to Inpatient Facility (TRN), and Discharge from Agency (DC). |\n| Start of Care (SOC) | The first billable visit to a patient for a new home health episode. The comprehensive assessment shall be initiated at this visit. |\n| Resumption of Care (ROC) | The first billable visit following a patient's return to home health services after an inpatient facility stay of ≥24 hours. A new comprehensive assessment is required. |\n| Recertification (RECERT) | The comprehensive assessment conducted between Day 56 and Day 60 of each certification period to evaluate continued eligibility and update the plan of care. |\n| Follow-Up (FU) | An OASIS assessment conducted between the SOC and RECERT time points, triggered by a significant change in the patient's condition (SCIC assessment), as defined by CMS criteria. |\n| Transfer (TRN) | An OASIS assessment completed at the time of transfer to an inpatient facility, documenting the patient's status at the point of transfer. |\n| Discharge (DC) | An OASIS assessment completed at the time of discharge from the agency (other than transfer to an inpatient facility), documenting the patient's final status. |\n| Assessment Accuracy | The degree to which each OASIS item response correctly reflects the patient's actual functional status, symptoms, and clinical characteristics at the time of the assessment, as determined by direct observation, clinical evaluation, patient and caregiver report, and review of available documentation. |\n| Homebound Status | The condition in which the patient has a normal inability to leave home due to an illness or injury, and leaving home requires a considerable and taxing effort — as defined in 42 CFR § 409.42(a). |\n| Skilled Services Need | The clinical requirement for services that require the training, skills, and judgment of a licensed nurse, physical therapist, occupational therapist, or speech-language pathologist — the qualifying condition for Medicare home health eligibility. |\n| Point-in-Time Assessment | The assessment principle that each OASIS assessment reflects the patient's status at the time of the specific assessment encounter — not a historical average or a projection. |\n\n---",
