        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.55 | Condition of Participation: Comprehensive Assessment of Patients | Primary regulatory basis for this policy |\n| 42 CFR § 484.55(a) | Standard: Completion of the comprehensive assessment | RN requirement; 5-day window; content requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 484.55(b) | Standard: Content of the comprehensive assessment | Required content including OASIS items |\n| 42 CFR § 484.55(c) | Standard: Update of the comprehensive assessment | Requirements for updating the assessment at OASIS time points |\n| 42 CFR § 409.42 | Homebound status | Definition of homebound status for Medicare home health |\n| 42 CFR § 484.60 | Condition of Participation: Care Planning | Assessment forms the basis of the plan of care |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual (current edition) | Item-specific guidance for all OASIS data collection decisions |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B, Tag G140 | Survey guidance for comprehensive assessment |\n| CMS Home Health Benefit Manual, Chapter 7 | Eligibility criteria — homebound status, skilled need |\n\n### 9.3 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to CL-CA-001 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| CL-CP-001 | Plan of Care Development & Approval | Comprehensive assessment is the clinical basis of the plan of care |\n| CL-CA-002 | OASIS Data Collection & Accuracy | OASIS accuracy standards for all items collected during the comprehensive assessment |\n| CL-CA-003 | OASIS Transmission & Correction | Submission of the completed OASIS data set |\n| CL-CA-004 | Recertification Assessment & Process | Comprehensive assessment at RECERT |\n| CL-CA-005 | Homebound Status Determination & Documentation | Homebound assessment as a required component |\n| CL-CA-006 | Face-to-Face Encounter Compliance | F2F requirement linked to comprehensive assessment |\n| CL-CA-007 | Face-to-Face Encounter Tracking & Expiration Monitoring | F2F tracking integration with assessment workflow |\n| CL-SD-014 | Pain Assessment & Management | Pain assessment domain |\n| CL-SD-015 | Fall Risk Assessment & Prevention | Fall risk domain |\n| CL-SD-016 | Infection Prevention & Control | Infection risk domain |\n| CL-SD-018 | Diabetic Management & Monitoring | Diabetic assessment domain |\n| CL-SD-019 | Cardiac Care & Monitoring | Cardiac assessment domain |\n| CL-SD-020 | Respiratory Care & Management | Respiratory assessment domain |\n| CL-SD-022 | Behavioral Health Screening & Referral | PHQ-2/PHQ-9, BIMS administration |\n| CL-SD-023 | Palliative & End-of-Life Care | Advance directive assessment domain |\n| CL-OA-001 through CL-OA-019 | OASIS & Assessment Governance Policies | All OASIS-specific standards applicable to the comprehensive assessment |\n| HR-TD-003 | Clinical Staff Competency Evaluation | Comprehensive assessment competency validation |\n| RM-PS-001 | Environmental Safety Assessment | Home environment domain |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework classification |\n\n---",
