        id: "29-training-acknowledgment-requirements",
        title: "10\\. Training & Acknowledgment Requirements",
        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All RNs shall complete the Comprehensive Assessment Competency Program (Appendix A) before independently conducting comprehensive assessments. The program shall include: (a) didactic content covering all assessment domains in Section 6.2; (b) OASIS item-specific training per the CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual; (c) standardized tool administration (PHQ-2/PHQ-9, BIMS, MAHC-10 as applicable) with validated competency demonstration; (d) homebound status documentation standards; (e) skilled service need documentation standards; (f) pre-submission quality review process; (g) assessment-to-plan of care integration; (h) documentation standards demonstrating individualized, patient-specific assessment content.\n10.2 The Director of Nursing or a designated preceptor RN shall directly supervise and evaluate the first independent SOC assessment of every newly hired or newly authorized RN before adding the RN to the Authorized Assessor Roster.\n10.3 Annual refresher competency for comprehensive assessment and OASIS accuracy shall be completed by all authorized RN assessors, incorporating any changes to the OASIS data set or CMS guidance issued since the prior annual training.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, any revision, or hire/appointment.\n10.5 The Director of Nursing shall maintain the Comprehensive Assessment Competency Program training records and the Authorized Assessor Roster for all RNs and shall report any non-compliance to the Administrator within 7 calendar days of any training deadline.\n\n---",
