        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | Review all SOC assessments within 5 business days of locking, using the OASIS Quality Review Tool (Appendix A). The review shall assess: accuracy of GG functional items; accuracy of wound items (M1311–M1350); accuracy of behavioral health items (M1700–M1750); accuracy of medication management items (M2001–M2010); narrative-OASIS consistency for all reviewed items; homebound documentation adequacy; skilled need documentation adequacy. | Within 5 business days of locking. |\n| 6.4.2 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | Document the review findings in the OASIS Quality Review Log (Appendix B), including: the assessment date, the assessing RN, each item reviewed, the reviewer's determination (Accurate / Inaccurate — requires correction / Insufficient documentation), and any corrective action recommended. | At the time of the review. |\n| 6.4.3 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | If an inaccuracy is identified, communicate the finding to the assessing RN and the Director of Nursing within 24 hours, providing the item number, the assessing RN's response, the reviewer's determination of the correct response, and the clinical evidence supporting the correction. | Within 24 hours of finding. |\n| 6.4.4 | Assigned RN / Director of Nursing | If the assessing RN agrees with the reviewer's finding, initiate the OASIS correction process per CL-CA-003. If the assessing RN disagrees with the reviewer's determination, escalate to the Director of Nursing for clinical adjudication within 24 hours of the disagreement. The Director of Nursing's determination is final. | Within 24 hours of disagreement notification. |\n| 6.4.5 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | Conduct quarterly ROC, RECERT, and DC assessment reviews at a minimum 10% sample rate, using the same review methodology as SOC reviews. | Quarterly. |\n\n---",
