        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All RNs authorized to conduct OASIS assessments shall complete the OASIS Competency Program per CL-CA-001 before independent assessment. The program shall include OASIS-specific training covering all high-risk item categories (GG functional, wound, behavioral health, medication management) with item-level decision-rule training per the OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual.\n10.2 Annual OASIS accuracy refresher training shall be provided to all authorized RN assessors, incorporating: (a) any changes to the OASIS data set or CMS guidance since the prior training; (b) the agency's OASIS accuracy audit findings from the prior year, including the most common errors and corrective guidance; (c) OASIS response selection decision-practice exercises using case scenarios.\n10.3 The OASIS Quality Reviewer shall complete advanced OASIS training (OASIS specialist certification or equivalent) and shall maintain current knowledge of CMS guidance updates. The Director of Nursing shall verify the OASIS Quality Reviewer's qualifications annually.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix D) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, any revision, or hire/appointment.\n\n---",
