        title: "OASIS Transmission Deadlines and Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | Transmit all OASIS assessments to the CMS repository within the following CMS-specified deadlines: (a) SOC assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the SOC date; (b) ROC assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the ROC date; (c) RECERT assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the recertification date; (d) FU (SCIC) assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the assessment date; (e) TRN assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the transfer date; (f) DC assessments — transmitted within 30 calendar days of the discharge date. Note: The 30-day CMS deadline is the regulatory maximum — the agency's operational target is transmission within 10 calendar days of the assessment date to allow time for correction and resubmission before the deadline if needed. | Per CMS deadlines; agency target is 10 calendar days. |\n| 6.2.2 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | Perform OASIS transmissions using the agency's certified OASIS submission software. Transmit records in batch submissions at minimum twice per week (Monday and Thursday), and additionally on any day when an assessment is identified as approaching the transmission deadline. | At minimum twice weekly. |\n| 6.2.3 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | For each transmission batch: (a) document the transmission in the OASIS Submission Log (Appendix A) including: date and time of transmission, number of records transmitted, assessment time points included, and the name of the staff member initiating the transmission; (b) retain the electronic export file and the submission confirmation from the agency's EHR or OASIS submission software; (c) await the CMS response file. | At each transmission; documented in the Submission Log. |\n\n---",
