        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | Retrieve and review the CMS response file within 2 business days of transmission. The response file will identify each submitted record as: accepted, accepted with warnings, or rejected. | Within 2 business days of transmission. |\n| 6.3.2 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | For each accepted record without warnings: update the OASIS Submission Log to reflect the CMS acceptance. No further action required for accepted records. | At the time of response file review. |\n| 6.3.3 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | For each record accepted with warnings: document the warning code and message in the OASIS Submission Log. Notify the Director of Nursing of all warnings within 24 hours of receipt. The Director of Nursing shall assess whether the warning indicates a clinical data quality concern requiring investigation. If the warning indicates a potential accuracy issue, initiate the correction assessment per Section 6.4. | Within 24 hours of response file receipt. |\n| 6.3.4 | OASIS Transmission Coordinator | For each rejected record: document the rejection code and reason in the OASIS Submission Log. Notify the Director of Nursing within 24 hours. Investigate the rejection reason — which may be a data format error, a missing required element, a logical inconsistency, or a system error. Resolve the rejection cause and resubmit within 5 business days of rejection identification. | Within 24 hours of rejection; resubmission within 5 business days. |\n| 6.3.5 | Director of Nursing | For rejections that cannot be resolved within 5 business days due to clinical complexity, notify the Administrator and contact the CMS OASIS Help Desk or the state OASIS coordinator for guidance. Document all contacts and the agency's efforts to resolve the rejection. | By Day 5 if not resolved; escalation immediately. |\n\n---",
