        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Recertification assessment is not completed within the Day 56–60 window | Director of Nursing identifies | Director of Nursing assesses the reason and determines whether services may continue. If the window is narrowly missed (Day 61–62) and the patient continues to require skilled services, consult the Compliance Officer regarding billing implications. Complete the assessment as soon as possible. Do not bill for services after Day 60 without a valid recertification. | Assessment completed immediately; Compliance Officer consultation within 24 hours. |\n| Patient is hospitalized during the Day 56–60 window | Director of Nursing | A recertification assessment cannot be conducted during an inpatient stay. If the patient returns home before Day 60, attempt to complete the recertification visit. If the certification period expires while the patient is hospitalized, a new SOC assessment is required upon the patient's return. | Immediate assessment upon patient's return from hospitalization if within window. |\n| Physician refuses to recertify despite the patient meeting eligibility criteria | Director of Nursing and Administrator | Director of Nursing engages the physician to discuss the clinical basis for the refusal. If the disagreement is substantive, consult the Compliance Officer. Services cannot continue without a physician-signed recertification regardless of the clinical team's assessment of the patient's eligibility. | Resolution within 7 calendar days. |\n| Recertification assessment reveals clinical findings inconsistent with prior documentation | Director of Nursing and OASIS Quality Reviewer | Review the entire episode record for documentation integrity concerns. If the inconsistency suggests prior visit documentation does not accurately reflect the patient's clinical status, notify the Compliance Officer. Assess for potential OASIS correction needs per CL-CA-003. | Compliance Officer notification within 48 hours. |\n\n---",
