        id: "9-f2f-documentation-acquisition",
        title: "F2F Documentation Acquisition",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Clinical Coordinator / Medical Records | Within 5 business days of the SOC date, contact the qualifying practitioner's office to obtain the F2F encounter documentation. The request shall specify: the patient's name and date of birth; the date of the encounter; and the CMS content requirements for the documentation (date of encounter, clinical findings supporting home health, and attestation language). | Within 5 business days of SOC. |\n| 6.2.2 | Medical Records | Acceptable F2F documentation includes: hospital discharge summary containing the encounter date, clinical findings, and physician signature; office visit notes from the qualifying practitioner; specialist consultation notes; or a CMS-compliant F2F encounter form completed and signed by the qualifying practitioner. A certification statement alone (without encounter documentation) is not sufficient. | At the time of documentation receipt. |\n| 6.2.3 | Medical Records | Upon receipt of F2F documentation, verify that it meets all CMS content requirements per Section 4.5. If the documentation is incomplete — missing the encounter date, missing clinical findings, or lacking attestation — return it to the practitioner's office for completion before filing. Document all contacts with the practitioner's office in the F2F tracking system per CL-CA-007. | Within 3 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.2.4 | Medical Records | File the complete, compliant F2F documentation in the patient's clinical record. Update the F2F Tracking System per CL-CA-007 to reflect receipt and verification. | Within 3 business days of receipt. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
