        title: "F2F for Post-SOC Encounters (Encounter After SOC Date)",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Clinical Coordinator | If the F2F encounter occurs after the SOC date (within the 30-day post-SOC window), track the encounter date and monitor its occurrence through the F2F Tracking System per CL-CA-007. | From SOC date until the post-SOC encounter is documented. |\n| 6.3.2 | Clinical Coordinator | If the 30-day post-SOC window is approaching without a qualifying encounter having occurred, notify the Director of Nursing at Day 20 post-SOC. The Director of Nursing shall contact the certifying physician to ensure a qualifying encounter is scheduled before Day 30. | Day 20 post-SOC if no qualifying encounter has occurred. |\n| 6.3.3 | Director of Nursing | If no qualifying F2F encounter occurs within 30 days of the SOC and the F2F window closes without compliance, notify the Compliance Officer. The episode's claims may not be submitted until the F2F requirement is satisfied. If the window has closed without a qualifying encounter, consult the Compliance Officer regarding the disposition of any claims submitted for the episode. | Day 30 post-SOC if no qualifying encounter; Compliance Officer immediately. |\n\n---",
