        id: "12-director-of-nursing-documentation-quality-oversight",
        title: "Director of Nursing Documentation Quality Oversight",
        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Director of Nursing | Conduct a monthly clinical documentation audit per CO-DC-002 covering a random sample of ≥5% of all visit notes from the prior month. The audit shall assess: (a) presence of all required universal elements per Section 6.1.3; (b) individualization — no copy-forward or template language; (c) skilled documentation — clear demonstration of skilled care and medical necessity; (d) goal progress documentation — specific and measurable; (e) authentication completeness; (f) consistency with related clinical record entries; (g) timeliness per CL-CD-004 standards. | Monthly. |\n| 6.5.2 | Director of Nursing | Document audit findings in the Documentation Quality Dashboard (Appendix B) by discipline and by individual clinician. Identify documentation deficiencies by category and frequency. | Within 5 business days of audit completion. |\n| 6.5.3 | Director of Nursing | Provide individual written feedback to each clinician with identified documentation deficiencies, including specific examples from the audited records, the applicable standard, and the required correction. | Within 14 calendar days of audit completion. |\n| 6.5.4 | Director of Nursing | For any clinician with a documentation quality score below 80% on any category in any month, initiate targeted documentation retraining within 14 calendar days and schedule a follow-up audit within 30 calendar days. | Within 14 calendar days of audit completion. |\n| 6.5.5 | Director of Nursing | Present documentation quality audit results to the QAPI Committee quarterly, identifying trends, systemic issues, and improvement actions. | Quarterly QAPI meeting. |\n\n---",
