        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| A visit note is identified as documenting care that the clinician could not have provided (e.g., visit note completed when the patient reports no visit occurred; visit note completed from the office without the visit having occurred) | Director of Nursing and Compliance Officer | Compliance Officer initiates a compliance investigation per CO-CP-007. Do not alter or delete the documentation pending investigation. Document all facts as discovered. If billing has occurred for the falsified visit, assess for overpayment and potential self-disclosure. | Investigation initiated within 24 hours. |\n| Copy-forward documentation identified — visit notes for multiple consecutive visits are identical | Director of Nursing identifies during audit | Director of Nursing directs the clinician to amend all copy-forward notes using the late entry/correction process per CO-DC-003. Provides corrective training. Reports pattern to Compliance Officer if billing has been submitted. | Amendment within 14 calendar days; Compliance Officer notification if billing affected. |\n| Visit note does not support the skilled nature of the service — may not be billable | Director of Nursing identifies during audit | Director of Nursing and Revenue Cycle assess whether the visit can be supported as skilled based on the available clinical record. If the visit cannot be supported, do not bill for it or retract the claim if already submitted. Provide documentation coaching to the clinician. | Assessment within 5 business days; billing decision within 10 business days. |\n| Clinician refuses to authenticate a note | Director of Nursing | Director of Nursing investigates the reason. If the clinician refuses because the note is inaccurate, the note must be corrected before authentication per CO-DC-003. If the clinician refuses for other reasons, document the refusal and initiate HR action per HR-ER-002. | Investigation within 24 hours; HR referral if refusal persists. |\n\n---",
