        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All clinical staff shall receive clinical documentation standards training within 14 calendar days of hire and annually thereafter, including: the universal required elements for visit notes; skilled documentation standards with examples from the agency's own audit findings; prohibited practices (copy-forward, pre-dating, falsification, unapproved abbreviations); the correction and late entry process per CO-DC-003; authentication requirements; and the consequences of documentation failures for billing and compliance.\n10.2 All new clinical hires shall complete a supervised first visit with documentation review by the Director of Nursing or a designated preceptor before independently submitting documentation. The preceptor shall review the first visit note against the standards in this policy and provide written feedback before the new clinician's note is authenticated and locked.\n10.3 The Approved Abbreviation List (Appendix A) shall be distributed to all clinical staff at hire and whenever the list is updated. All clinical staff shall acknowledge receipt and understanding of the approved abbreviations.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix C) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, any revision, or hire/appointment.\n10.5 The Director of Nursing shall maintain training completion records for all clinical staff and shall report non-compliance to the Administrator within 7 calendar days of any training deadline.\n\n---",
