        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Director of Nursing | Ensure that all disciplines providing services to the patient have reviewed the plan of care and that their discipline-specific goals, interventions, and visit frequencies are accurately reflected. No discipline shall provide services that conflict with or exceed what is authorized in the plan of care without a new physician order. | Within 48 hours of the SOC visit. |\n| 6.4.2 | Each Clinical Discipline Provider | Upon receiving a referral for a new patient, review the plan of care within 24 hours of assignment. Confirm that the ordered services are within the discipline's scope of practice, are clinically appropriate based on the OASIS assessment and available records, and are supported by a current physician order. If any ordered service appears clinically inappropriate or outside scope, immediately contact the Director of Nursing. | Within 24 hours of assignment. |\n| 6.4.3 | Assigned RN | Serve as the primary coordinator for the patient's plan of care. Document all clinical communications regarding the plan of care in the patient's clinical record. Any discipline-specific addition, modification, or concern regarding the plan of care shall be communicated to the assigned RN, who will coordinate with the physician per CL-CP-003. | Ongoing throughout the certification period. |\n| 6.4.4 | Director of Nursing | Conduct or ensure that a care coordination communication occurs among all disciplines involved in the patient's care no later than 14 calendar days after SOC for patients receiving three or more disciplines. The communication may occur via telephone, secure messaging, or a documented care conference. Document the date, participants, topics discussed, and any plan of care modifications agreed upon. | Within 14 calendar days of SOC for patients receiving three or more disciplines. |\n\n---",
