        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Discovering Clinician (any discipline) | Any clinician who identifies a significant change in the patient's condition during a visit shall document the clinical findings in the visit note and notify the assigned RN and/or Director of Nursing on the same day. The notification must include: (a) the nature of the change; (b) the patient's current clinical status; (c) the clinician's clinical assessment of the change; (d) any immediate safety concerns. | On the same day the change is identified. |\n| 6.2.2 | Assigned RN | Upon notification or independent identification of a significant change, contact the physician within 24 hours to report the change, obtain clinical guidance, and secure any needed orders for plan modification. Document the physician contact, the information communicated, and the physician's response. | Within 24 hours of identifying the significant change. |\n| 6.2.3 | Assigned RN | Obtain a verbal or written physician order for any change to the plan of care per policy CL-CP-003. For verbal orders, follow the read-back and documentation requirements of CL-CP-004. The order must specifically authorize the type and scope of the plan change before it is implemented. | Order obtained before implementing the plan change; verbal order documented within 24 hours. |\n| 6.2.4 | Assigned RN | Update the plan of care in the EHR to reflect the authorized modification. Update: (a) diagnoses if applicable; (b) service types and frequencies; (c) medications if changed; (d) goals if the change affects the patient's functional status or discharge trajectory; (e) safety measures if new risks are identified. | Within 24 hours of receiving the physician order. |\n| 6.2.5 | Assigned RN | Notify all other disciplines involved in the patient's care of the plan modification and updated orders. Document the notification in the clinical record. | Within 24 hours of updating the plan. |\n| 6.2.6 | Assigned RN | Assess whether the significant change may require an unplanned OASIS assessment (Resumption of Care after an inpatient stay, or significant change assessment per CMS OASIS guidance). Consult the Director of Nursing if the assessment type is uncertain. If a new OASIS is required, initiate per CL-OA-001. | Within 24 hours of the significant change identification. |\n| 6.2.7 | Director of Nursing | Review all mid-episode plan modifications within 7 calendar days of notification. Confirm that: (a) physician orders support all modifications; (b) OASIS data was updated if required; (c) billing reflects the updated plan; (d) all disciplines were notified. Document the supervisory review. | Within 7 calendar days of notification of the modification. |\n\n---",
