        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Medical Records / Assigned RN | Upon receipt of a written order from the physician, verify that the order is: (a) legible; (b) dated; (c) signed by the ordering physician; (d) sufficiently specific to authorize the intended service without clinical interpretation. If any element is missing, return the order to the physician for correction before it is entered into the EHR as active. | Within 24 hours of receipt. |\n| 6.2.2 | Medical Records / Assigned RN | Enter the written order into the EHR Order Management Record. Mark the order as \"Written — Signed\" and document the date received and the date entered. | Within 24 hours of receipt and verification. |\n| 6.2.3 | Medical Records / Clinical Coordinator | File the original written order (or a verified electronic copy if received via fax or portal) in the patient's clinical record. Ensure the order is accessible to all treating clinicians. | Within 3 calendar days of receipt; original retained minimum 7 years. |\n| 6.2.4 | Assigned RN | Verify that every service delivered to the patient is covered by a current, active written or authenticated verbal order. If a service is delivered before a written order is received (under an authorized verbal order), confirm that the verbal order is being tracked for authentication per CL-CP-004. | Before each visit; continuous. |\n\n---",
