        title: "Verbal Order Documentation in the EHR",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Receiving RN / LVN | Document the verbal order in the patient's EHR Order Management Record within 24 hours of receipt. The EHR entry shall include all elements from Section 6.1.2 plus: (a) notation that the order was given verbally (e.g., \"V.O. — per Dr. [Name]\"); (b) the receiving clinician's name, credential, and date/time of transcription; (c) \"Read back confirmed by [physician name]\" notation; (d) authentication status: \"Pending authentication — due by [date 7 calendar days from verbal order date].\" | Within 24 hours of receipt; before the end of the clinical shift in which the order was received. |\n| 6.2.2 | Receiving RN / LVN | If the verbal order initiates a new service or modifies the existing plan of care, also update the plan of care in the EHR to reflect the new or modified order, and transmit the updated plan of care to the physician for co-signature along with the verbal order for authentication per Section 6.3. | Within 24 hours of the verbal order. |\n| 6.2.3 | Receiving RN / LVN | Send a copy of the transcribed verbal order to the ordering physician for authentication by the method preferred by the physician (fax, secure portal, or electronic signature request). Document the date and method of transmission in the EHR. | Within 24 hours of transcription. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
