        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Director of Nursing | LVNs at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. may receive and transcribe verbal orders only for: (a) changes to existing medication orders (dose adjustments, discontinuations) that have been directly communicated by the physician; (b) orders for routine treatments within the LVN's scope of practice. LVNs shall not receive verbal orders for new medications, new skilled services, changes in the plan of care, or orders that require clinical judgment beyond the LVN scope. | Ongoing; enforced through orientation training. |\n| 6.4.2 | LVN Receiving a Verbal Order | If an LVN receives a verbal order that appears to exceed the LVN scope limitations defined in 6.4.1, the LVN shall not accept or document the order. The LVN shall immediately contact the assigned RN or Director of Nursing to receive the order. Document the referral to the RN. | Immediately upon identification of a scope-exceeding order. |\n| 6.4.3 | Director of Nursing | Provide explicit training to all LVNs on verbal order receipt limitations at hire and annually. Maintain training completion records in each LVN's personnel file. | At hire; annually; training documented. |\n\n---",
