        id: "9-physician-communication",
        title: "Physician Communication",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Assigned RN | Notify the attending physician within 24 hours of identifying any of the following: (a) significant change in the patient's condition per CL-CP-002; (b) a new clinical diagnosis or finding; (c) a medication concern, adverse reaction, or potential interaction; (d) a patient safety risk identified during the home assessment per RM-PS-001; (e) a patient refusal of ordered services; (f) a missed visit that affects the patient's clinical care continuity. | Within 24 hours of the identified event. |\n| 6.2.2 | Assigned RN | At a minimum of every 30 calendar days, provide the attending physician with a clinical status update including: (a) the patient's current functional status and progress toward goals; (b) any concerns about the patient's trajectory; (c) the estimated discharge timeline and criteria; (d) any community resources or referrals provided. The update may be transmitted via fax, secure messaging, or telephone with documentation. | Every 30 calendar days; documented in the clinical record. |\n| 6.2.3 | Assigned RN | Document all physician communications in the clinical record, including: (a) the date and time of the communication; (b) the name of the physician or physician office contact; (c) the method of communication; (d) the information communicated; (e) the physician's response or any orders received; (f) any follow-up actions agreed upon. | Within 24 hours of each communication. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
