        title: "Transition from Inpatient Setting",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Assigned RN | For all patients transitioning from a hospital or SNF to home health, obtain from the sending facility: (a) the discharge summary (or, if not yet available, a transfer summary or face sheet); (b) the current medication reconciliation list; (c) any pending laboratory or diagnostic test results; (d) follow-up physician appointments scheduled; (e) any pending specialist referrals; (f) a list of all care providers seen during the inpatient stay. If documentation is not available at the time of the SOC visit, contact the facility directly and document the request. | Obtained before or at the SOC visit; if unavailable, requested within 24 hours of SOC. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assigned RN | At the SOC visit, compare the patient's current status, current medications, and current home environment against the discharge documentation. Document any discrepancies identified and notify the attending physician within 24 hours of any clinically significant discrepancies per CL-OA-013. | At the SOC visit; physician notification within 24 hours of clinically significant discrepancies. |\n| 6.3.3 | Assigned RN | Confirm that the patient has a scheduled follow-up appointment with the attending physician within 7–14 days of discharge (or within the timeframe recommended by the discharging facility or CMS). If no appointment is scheduled, assist the patient and caregiver in scheduling and document the appointment date. | At the SOC visit; documented in the clinical record. |\n\n---",
