        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Discharge | The formal termination of a patient's enrollment in home health services at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. |\n| Discharge Criteria | The specific clinical, functional, and support-system conditions that must be met before a patient is determined to be appropriate for discharge from home health services. |\n| Goal-Achieved Discharge | A discharge that occurs because the patient has met the clinical and functional goals established in the plan of care and no longer requires skilled home health services. |\n| Physician-Ordered Discharge | A discharge that occurs at the direction of the attending physician, who has determined that home health services are no longer indicated. |\n| Patient-Initiated Discharge | A discharge requested by the patient or their legal representative, which may occur at any time regardless of whether the patient has met discharge criteria. |\n| Discharge Against Medical Advice (AMA) | A patient-initiated discharge that occurs when the patient chooses to stop home health services despite the clinical team's recommendation to continue. |\n| Safety-Related Discharge | A discharge initiated by the agency due to threats, violence, or unresolvable safety hazards in the patient's home that make it unsafe for agency staff to provide care. |\n| Discharge OASIS | The OASIS assessment completed at the time of discharge (other than transfer to inpatient facility), documenting the patient's clinical and functional status at the end of the episode. |\n| Discharge Summary | A written document provided to the patient at discharge summarizing the patient's progress, final status, discharge instructions, and community resource referrals. |\n| Transfer | A move from home health services to an inpatient setting (hospital, SNF, IRF) — governed by policy CL-CP-007. Transfer is distinct from discharge for OASIS and billing purposes. |\n\n---",
