        title: "Discharge Planning Throughout the Episode",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assigned RN | At SOC, identify and document in the plan of care: (a) the patient's anticipated discharge date (a realistic target based on clinical trajectory, visit frequency, and functional goals); (b) the specific discharge criteria — what the patient must achieve or demonstrate to be safely discharged; (c) the patient's and caregiver's discharge goals and preferences; (d) any anticipated barriers to discharge (caregiver limitations, community resource gaps, chronic conditions requiring ongoing management). | During the SOC visit; documented in the plan of care within 24 hours. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assigned RN | At every 30-day plan of care review, reassess and update: (a) the estimated discharge date based on the patient's current progress; (b) the status of each discharge criterion — met, partially met, or not yet met; (c) barriers to discharge and the plan to address them; (d) referrals needed for community services post-discharge. | At each 30-day review; documented in the Plan of Care Review Note. |\n| 6.1.3 | MSW | When community resources are needed to support discharge, initiate referrals no later than 14 calendar days before the anticipated discharge date, to allow sufficient time for services to be established before the patient is discharged. Document all referrals per CL-CP-005. | At least 14 calendar days before the anticipated discharge. |\n| 6.1.4 | Assigned RN | Begin formal discharge education with the patient and caregiver at least 7 calendar days before the anticipated discharge date, covering: (a) management of the patient's primary condition(s) after discharge; (b) medication management — including all medications, doses, schedules, and adverse effects to report; (c) diet and activity restrictions; (d) signs and symptoms that require physician contact or emergency services; (e) scheduled follow-up physician appointments; (f) community resources established; (g) how to access care if needed after discharge. | At least 7 calendar days before anticipated discharge; final reinforcement at the last visit. |\n\n---",
