        body: "CMS surveyors conducting a standard survey under SOM Appendix B will specifically verify under Tag G160 (42 CFR § 484.60):\nEvidence that transfers are coordinated with receiving facilities. Surveyors will select patients who have been transferred to inpatient facilities and verify that a clinical summary was transmitted, that a warm handoff occurred, and that the physician was notified. Missing transfer documentation is a care coordination deficiency.\nEvidence that the transfer OASIS is completed. Surveyors will compare transfer dates with OASIS completion dates. Missing or late transfer OASIS assessments affect quality measure accuracy and are a documentation compliance deficiency.\nEvidence that ROC assessments are comprehensive and timely. Surveyors will select patients who returned from inpatient stays and verify that a full ROC assessment was completed, medications were reconciled, and the plan of care was updated to reflect post-facility status.\nEvidence that medication reconciliation occurs at ROC. Surveyors and ADR auditors will specifically examine whether the agency compared the inpatient discharge medication list against the prior home health medication list and the patient's actual medications. Medication discrepancies not identified and resolved at ROC are a patient safety failure.\nEvidence that patients who visit the ED without admission are clinically followed up. Surveyors will verify that ED visits are documented and that the agency assessed the patient's status and medications following the ED visit.\n\n---",
