        title: "Tracking System Entry and Initial Transmission",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assigned RN / Clinical Coordinator | At the time any document requiring physician signature is transmitted to the physician's office, enter the document into the Tracking System with all required data fields per Section 4.2. | At the time of transmission. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assigned RN / Clinical Coordinator | Verify the physician's preferred method of receiving documents (fax, secure portal, mail) and ensure the document is transmitted via the preferred method. Document the fax confirmation number, portal submission receipt, or mailing tracking number. | At the time of transmission. |\n| 6.1.3 | Clinical Coordinator | Confirm the accuracy of the physician's fax number, portal address, or mailing address before each transmission. Incorrect contact information is a leading cause of delayed signatures. | Before each transmission. |\n\n---",
