        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Clinical Coordinator | Day 5 — First Follow-Up: If the signed document has not been received by Day 5, initiate first follow-up contact with the physician's office by telephone or fax. Document the contact: date, time, method, person contacted, and response. | Day 5 after transmission. |\n| 6.2.2 | Clinical Coordinator / Director of Nursing | Day 7 — Second Follow-Up + Director of Nursing Notification: If the signed document has not been received by Day 7, the Clinical Coordinator initiates a second follow-up contact and formally notifies the Director of Nursing via the Tracking System alert. For verbal orders, Day 7 is the authentication deadline per CL-CP-004 — unresolved verbal orders at Day 7 require Director of Nursing direct contact with the physician. | Day 7 after transmission. |\n| 6.2.3 | Director of Nursing | Day 14 — Director of Nursing Direct Contact: The Director of Nursing shall contact the physician directly by telephone. Document the conversation including the physician's stated reason for delay and the committed return date. If the physician is unreachable, contact the physician's office manager or practice administrator. | Day 14 after transmission. |\n| 6.2.4 | Administrator | Day 21 — Administrator Escalation: If the signed document has not been received by Day 21 despite documented follow-up, the Administrator shall contact the physician's practice administration in writing, outlining the document(s) outstanding, the regulatory and billing implications, and requesting immediate resolution. The Administrator and Director of Nursing shall assess whether the document is disputed by the physician (in which case, consult the Compliance Officer). | Day 21 after transmission. |\n| 6.2.5 | Revenue Cycle | At any point where a document deadline has passed without signature, Revenue Cycle shall implement a billing hold for the affected episode or service. The billing hold shall remain in place until the signature is received and filed. | Upon expiration of the applicable deadline. |\n\n---",
