        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Assigned RN | Upon completion of an assessment visit (SOC, ROC, RECERT, or FU), the assessing RN shall begin OASIS completion in the EHR at the earliest possible opportunity — ideally at or immediately after the visit using the EHR mobile application, or within 2 hours of returning to the office. The operational target deadline for most time points is 3 calendar days, but same-day or next-day completion is strongly preferred and consistently expected. | At or immediately after each assessment visit; no later than the operational target. |\n| 6.5.2 | Assigned RN | Before locking any OASIS assessment, complete the pre-submission quality review per CL-OA-019. If the quality review reveals items requiring correction or clarification, resolve all issues before locking. Document the quality review completion in the EHR per CL-OA-019. | Before locking each assessment. |\n| 6.5.3 | Assigned RN | If completing the OASIS assessment within the operational target is not feasible due to a documented clinical circumstance (active patient emergency, high caseload day with multiple complex visits), notify the Director of Nursing on the same day and document the reason in the EHR. The Director of Nursing may authorize a 24-hour extension to the operational target — not the regulatory deadline — for documented clinical reasons. No extension is available beyond the regulatory deadline. | Same day if operational target cannot be met. |\n| 6.5.4 | Assigned RN | For TRN assessments when the clinician was not present at the transfer: complete the TRN OASIS as soon as the agency is notified, using all available clinical sources. Clearly document the information sources used and the reason for retrospective completion in the assessment narrative per CL-OA-012. | As soon as the agency is notified of the transfer. |\n\n---",
