        order: 13,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.6.1 | Director of Nursing | Calculate and document monthly OASIS completion timeliness rates: (a) percentage of SOC assessments completed within 3 days (operational target); (b) percentage of SOC assessments completed within 5 days (regulatory deadline); (c) percentage of RECERT assessments completed within 5 days; (d) percentage of all OASIS time points completed within regulatory deadline; (e) number of missed regulatory deadlines by time point and by individual assessor. | Monthly; included in the Documentation Quality Dashboard per CL-CD-001. |\n| 6.6.2 | Director of Nursing | Present OASIS completion timeliness data to the QAPI Committee quarterly. Identify any time point or individual assessor with below-standard performance. Identify systemic barriers contributing to late completions (scheduling failures, EHR usability issues, caseload concentration). | Quarterly QAPI Committee meeting. |\n| 6.6.3 | QAPI Coordinator | If the agency-wide OASIS completion rate falls below 95% within the regulatory deadline for any time point in any quarter, initiate a Performance Improvement Project per QA-PI-001 targeting the specific failure point. | PIP initiation within 14 calendar days of the quarterly data review. |\n\n---",
