        level: 3,
        order: 16,
        body: "CMS surveyors under Tag G140 (42 CFR § 484.55) and OASIS validation survey protocols will:\nRequest OASIS lock dates for a sample of episodes and compare them to the trigger event dates. A pattern of assessments locked after the 5-day regulatory deadline is a direct CoP compliance deficiency.\nExamine RECERT assessments specifically to verify that the assessment was conducted between Day 56 and Day 60 — not before Day 56 and not after Day 60. An assessment conducted on Day 55 is as non-compliant as one conducted on Day 61.\nLook for evidence of an active timeliness monitoring program — a tracking dashboard, escalation documentation, and QAPI reporting demonstrating that the agency actively monitors and addresses timeliness failures.\nRequest the agency's corrective counseling records for any assessors with documented late completions, to verify that the agency holds individual assessors accountable.\n\n---",
