        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assessing RN | Before locking any OASIS assessment, complete the Pre-Submission Quality Review Checklist per CL-OA-019. The checklist systematically verifies: all applicable time point items are completed; no items are at default values without clinical justification; internal consistency is verified across related item groups (functional items, wound items, behavioral health items, medication items, clinical severity items); narrative documentation supports all OASIS responses; homebound status documentation meets the standards of CL-CA-005; and skilled service need documentation is present per CL-CA-001. | Before locking every OASIS assessment. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assessing RN | If the self-review identifies any item that is not supported by documentation, any internal inconsistency, or any response the assessor is uncertain about, do not lock the assessment. Review the clinical record to resolve the issue, consult the Director of Nursing or OASIS Quality Reviewer if needed, and correct the response before locking. Document the self-review completion in the EHR per CL-OA-019. | Before locking. |\n| 6.1.3 | Assessing RN | If any item requires clinical consultation to determine the correct response, contact the Director of Nursing or OASIS Quality Reviewer before locking. Document the consultation, the guidance received, and the final coding decision with the clinical rationale per CL-OA-012. | Before locking. |\n\n---",
