        body: "CMS OASIS validation survey teams will independently assess a sample of patients and compare their clinical findings to the submitted OASIS data. They will:\nRequest the agency's Quality Review Program documentation — including the Quality Review Tool, Quality Review Log, Accuracy Dashboard, and corrective action records. An agency without a documented, active quality review program cannot demonstrate survey readiness.\nCross-reference OASIS responses with clinical record narrative — for every item in their sample, surveyors will verify that the clinical record contains objective documentation supporting the coded response. An OASIS response unmoored from clinical documentation is an accuracy deficiency.\nReview the Correction Log — to assess whether corrections appear clinically justified or financially motivated. A pattern of corrections that consistently move PDGM payment groups upward is a red flag for upcoding.\nInterview the OASIS Quality Reviewer — to verify that the person understands their role, has appropriate OASIS expertise, and can describe the quality review process.\n\n---",
