        id: "8-oasis-competency-program-initial-authorization",
        title: "OASIS Competency Program — Initial Authorization",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Director of Nursing | Upon hire of any new RN who will be assigned OASIS assessments, enroll the RN in the OASIS Competency Program. No OASIS assessments shall be assigned to the RN until enrollment is confirmed. If the new hire has prior OASIS experience from another agency, grant provisional authorization per Section 4.6 while the program is being completed. | Within 5 business days of hire. |\n| 6.1.2 | Director of Nursing / Designated OASIS Trainer | Deliver the OASIS Competency Program in the following sequence: (Module 1) Regulatory and Financial Framework: 42 CFR § 484.55; OASIS purpose; PDGM payment linkage; quality measure linkage; billing compliance implications (3 hours). (Module 2) OASIS-E2 Data Set — Structure and Time Points: assessment time point definitions, triggers, and deadlines; item applicability by time point; look-back period rules; point-in-time vs. look-back items (4 hours). (Module 3) Item-Level Coding — GG Functional Items: GG0130 (self-care), GG0170 (mobility); response option definitions; observation vs. report; activity-specific coding rules; the 6-point functional independence scale; internal consistency requirements (4 hours). (Module 4) Item-Level Coding — Wound and Skin Items: M1311–M1350 series; NPIAP staging system; reverse-staging prohibition; wound type classification; OASIS wound item navigation logic; documentation requirements (4 hours). (Module 5) Item-Level Coding — Behavioral Health Items: M1700 cognitive function; BIMS administration protocol (validated, complete); M1730 depressive feelings; PHQ-2/PHQ-9 administration (validated, complete); M1710–M1750 series (4 hours). (Module 6) Item-Level Coding — Medication, Clinical Severity, and Remaining Items: M2001–M2010 medication management items; M-series clinical severity items; MAHC-10 items; remaining applicable items (3 hours). (Module 7) Homebound Status and Skilled Need Documentation: two-part homebound criteria; patient-specific documentation standards; skilled need justification per discipline; common documentation failures (2 hours). (Module 8) Pre-Submission Quality Review: the three-level review structure; CL-OA-019 checklist process; internal consistency verification; documentation-to-OASIS alignment (2 hours). (Module 9) EHR OASIS Workflow: navigating the OASIS module in the agency's specific EHR; completing and locking assessments; mobile assessment workflow; the OASIS Completion Tracking Dashboard (2 hours). Total program: minimum 28 didactic hours; supplemented with case-based exercises for each item category. | Completed before authorization. |\n| 6.1.3 | Director of Nursing / Designated Assessor | Administer the OASIS Competency Validation Assessment (Appendix A), which consists of three components: (a) Written Knowledge Assessment — 50-item multiple-choice exam covering all module content; minimum passing score: 85%; assessors who score between 80–84% may remediate and retest once; assessors who score below 80% must complete Module remediation and retake the full exam; (b) Standardized Tool Administration Demonstration — the assessor demonstrates administration of the complete BIMS (all three components in correct sequence, per validated protocol) and the PHQ-2/PHQ-9 to a simulated patient (or role-play partner); rated on a pass/fail basis by the Director of Nursing or OASIS Quality Reviewer; (c) Supervised First SOC Assessment — the assessor conducts their first OASIS assessment at a real patient's SOC in the physical presence of a current authorized assessor or the Director of Nursing, who observes the entire assessment, reviews all coding decisions, and provides real-time feedback; the supervised assessment is co-authenticated by both the trainee and the supervisor. | Completed before authorization. |\n| 6.1.4 | Director of Nursing | Upon successful completion of all three components of the Competency Validation Assessment: (a) add the RN to the OASIS Authorized Assessor Roster with the authorization date; (b) notify IT Director to grant OASIS module access in the EHR; (c) file the completed Competency Validation Assessment and all scores in the RN's personnel file per HR-WM-007; (d) provide written authorization notification to the RN. | Within 5 business days of completing all three components. |\n\n---",
