        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Director of Nursing | Maintain the OASIS Authorized Assessor Roster (Appendix B) with the following fields for each authorized assessor: full legal name; RN license number; initial authorization date; most recent annual re-competency date; authorization expiration date (12 months from most recent re-competency); current authorization status (Active / Provisional / Lapsed); OASIS Quality Reviewer designation (if applicable). | Maintained continuously; updated within 5 business days of any change. |\n| 6.2.2 | Director of Nursing | Generate a monthly Roster Currency Report that identifies: assessors whose authorization will expire within the next 60 days; assessors with lapsed authorization; and any change to the Roster in the prior month. Distribute to Medical Records, OASIS Transmission Coordinator, and Revenue Cycle. | Monthly. |\n| 6.2.3 | Director of Nursing | When an assessor's authorization lapses (annual re-competency not completed by the expiration date): (a) immediately update the Roster status to \"Lapsed\"; (b) notify IT Director to suspend OASIS module access; (c) notify Clinical Coordinator that the assessor is not available for OASIS assessment assignments; (d) initiate contact with the assessor to schedule immediate re-competency. No OASIS assessment conducted by an assessor with lapsed authorization after the expiration date is valid — each such assessment must be reviewed and, if necessary, re-conducted by an authorized assessor. | On the expiration date if re-competency is not completed. |\n| 6.2.4 | IT Director | Configure and maintain EHR access controls that restrict OASIS assessment module access to the individuals currently listed as Active or Provisional on the Authorized Assessor Roster. Update access within 5 business days of any Roster change. | Within 5 business days of any Roster change. |\n\n---",
