        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Director of Nursing | Generate an annual re-competency alert 60 days before each assessor's authorization expiration date. Notify the assessor and schedule the re-competency process. | 60 days before expiration. |\n| 6.3.2 | Director of Nursing | Conduct annual re-competency for every authorized assessor before their authorization expiration date. Annual re-competency consists of: (a) OASIS Updates Review: review of any changes to the OASIS data set, CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual, or assessment time point requirements issued since the prior re-competency (minimum 1 hour if changes are present; 30 minutes if no changes); (b) Accuracy Feedback Review: structured review with the Director of Nursing of the assessor's OASIS accuracy audit results from the prior 12 months — specific items with errors, correct responses, CMS guidance citations; (c) Annual Written Assessment: abbreviated 25-item written assessment focusing on items where the assessor had identified errors in the prior year and any new or revised CMS guidance; minimum passing score 85%; (d) Standardized Tool Re-Demonstration: if the assessor had a documented BIMS or PHQ-2/PHQ-9 administration error in the prior year, re-demonstration is required; if no prior error, annual BIMS re-demonstration is still required to maintain proficiency. | Before authorization expiration; completed re-competency updates the expiration date. |\n| 6.3.3 | Director of Nursing | Document the annual re-competency completion and all scores in the assessor's personnel file. Update the Authorized Assessor Roster with the new re-competency date and new authorization expiration date. Notify IT Director to update EHR access as applicable. | Within 5 business days of re-competency completion. |\n\n---",
