        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual | The current, definitive, CMS-published document providing item-specific guidance for all OASIS data collection decisions, including definitions of response options, look-back periods, time points at which items are collected, and special circumstances. The authoritative source for all coding decisions. |\n| Item-Level Guidance | The specific instructions, definitions, response option descriptions, special circumstances guidance, and coding rules provided in the CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual for a specific OASIS item. |\n| Agency-Created Coding Interpretation | Any OASIS coding rule, convention, shortcut, or guidance document developed by the agency, its management, its revenue cycle team, or any third party that is not grounded in or consistent with the current CMS Guidance Manual. Prohibited by this policy. |\n| Guidance Ambiguity | A situation where the CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual does not clearly and unambiguously resolve the correct coding response for a specific clinical scenario. Requires clinical reasoning documentation per CL-OA-012. |\n| CMS OASIS Guidance Update | A revision to the OASIS data set, the OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual, the OASIS Q&A database, or associated CMS guidance documents that changes item definitions, response options, collection rules, or coding instructions. |\n| Quick Reference Material | Any abbreviated coding guide, summary document, or reference card used by assessors to support OASIS completion — permissible only if grounded in and consistent with the current CMS Guidance Manual and clearly labeled as a supplement to the Guidance Manual. |\n| OASIS Contractor | The CMS-contracted organization responsible for providing training, technical assistance, and Q&A resolution for OASIS-related questions. The official channel for submitting questions about OASIS coding not resolved by the Guidance Manual itself. |\n\n---",
