        id: "8-access-control-configuration-and-maintenance",
        title: "Access Control Configuration and Maintenance",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | IT Director | Configure role-based access controls in the EHR to restrict the OASIS assessment module to the authorized roles specified in Section 4.2. The configuration shall prevent: (a) read access to OASIS assessment data by any role not listed in Section 4.2; (b) write access (creating or modifying OASIS data) by any user not on the current OASIS Authorized Assessor Roster per CL-OA-003; (c) deletion of any OASIS assessment or audit trail record by any user. | EHR configuration established at implementation; verified at each annual security review per IT-SC-002. |\n| 6.1.2 | IT Director | Generate a monthly OASIS access control report showing: all users who have OASIS module access by role; any access granted in the prior month; any access revoked in the prior month. Distribute to the Director of Nursing and Compliance Officer. | Monthly. |\n| 6.1.3 | IT Director | When an individual leaves the agency or changes roles, revoke or modify their OASIS access within 4 hours of notification of the separation or role change. This is a HIPAA-mandated security control — delayed revocation creates unauthorized access liability. | Within 4 hours of notification. |\n| 6.1.4 | Director of Nursing | Verify the accuracy of the OASIS access control list monthly, by comparing the IT access control report against the current OASIS Authorized Assessor Roster per CL-OA-003. Notify IT Director of any discrepancy for immediate correction. | Monthly; correction within 24 hours of identification. |\n| 6.1.5 | IT Director | Conduct a formal OASIS access control audit annually, reviewing all user access permissions against current authorized roles and identifying any excessive permissions, stale accounts, or access granted to non-authorized users. Present findings to the Compliance Officer. | Annually. |\n\n---",
