        level: 3,
        order: 16,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 7.2.1 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | For every SOC assessment reviewed, specifically evaluate substantiation adequacy using the Substantiation Assessment Matrix (Appendix A). For each item reviewed, rate the substantiation as: Adequate; Inadequate — specific deficiency noted; Insufficient documentation — narrative does not contain enough detail to evaluate. | Within the timeline specified in CL-OA-002. |\n| 7.2.2 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | When an item is rated Inadequate or Insufficient, document: the specific item; the specific documentation gap or inadequacy; the coded response; and the corrective action recommendation (additional documentation needed; field assessment needed; correction of coded response needed). | At the time of each review. |\n| 7.2.3 | OASIS Quality Reviewer | Assess the overall substantiation quality of each reviewed assessment using a three-tier rating: (a) Fully Substantiated — all reviewed items meet adequate substantiation standards; (b) Substantially Substantiated — minor gaps but no material accuracy risk; (c) Inadequately Substantiated — one or more items with material substantiation gaps; requires action before submission. | At the time of each review; documented in the OASIS Quality Review Log. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
