        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assessing RN | Before each SOC or ROC visit, review the available referral documentation to understand the patient's clinical history, but do not use this review to pre-populate any functional or clinical severity OASIS responses. Pre-visit documentation serves the purpose of clinical preparation — identifying which assessments to perform, which standardized tools to administer, which conditions to evaluate — not the purpose of OASIS pre-coding. | Before the assessment visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assessing RN | Note the interval between the patient's hospital or SNF discharge date and the SOC/ROC assessment date. Intervals greater than 48 hours represent a meaningful \"status drift\" window — clinical conditions may have changed substantially. Document the interval in the assessment narrative. | Before or at the beginning of the assessment visit. |\n| 6.1.3 | Assessing RN | Remind yourself of the point-in-time principle before beginning the assessment: you are assessing the patient's status today, in this home, at this moment in time. You are not confirming the hospital's assessment findings. You are not extending the hospital stay's clinical picture into the home. You are conducting an independent, original clinical assessment. | Before beginning the assessment. |\n\n---",
