        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Assessing RN | When the SOC/ROC assessment reveals a functional or clinical status that differs materially from the discharge documentation, document both: the discharge-documented status (as historical context) and the currently observed status (as the coding basis). This documentation structure provides the reconciliation narrative required by CL-OA-008 for the specific point-in-time conflict between the prior facility's documentation and the current assessment findings. | In the assessment narrative; before locking. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assessing RN | When the SOC assessment reveals material functional improvement from discharge status: code from the SOC observation; document the improvement as clinically expected and consistent with post-acute recovery trajectory; include this as a positive clinical finding that may affect plan of care goal-setting; do not infer that the improvement means the patient does not qualify for home health or does not need skilled services. | In the assessment narrative. |\n| 6.3.3 | Assessing RN | When the SOC assessment reveals material functional decline or new clinical findings not present in the discharge documentation: code from the SOC observation; treat the new findings as a clinical priority; notify the physician per CL-CP-005; update the plan of care per CL-CP-001 to reflect the actual clinical presentation. | At the assessment; physician notification per CL-CP-005 timelines. |\n\n---",
