        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "Scenario 1 — SOC Assessment 3 Days After Hospital Discharge:\nSOC assessment date: July 10. Hospital discharge date: July 7. For items with a 7-day look-back, the window is July 3–July 10. Four of those seven days (July 3–7) occurred during the hospital stay. Incontinence episodes, behavioral symptoms, and ADL assistance levels that occurred during the hospital stay between July 3 and July 7 are within scope for the look-back items. The assessor shall ask the patient and caregiver about those hospital days, and may contact the discharging facility for information if necessary. Document: \"7-day look-back for M1700 covers July 3–10. Patient hospitalized July 3–7. Patient and caregiver interviewed regarding cognitive function during both the hospital stay (July 3–7) and at home (July 7–10). Hospital nursing notes reviewed for the July 3–7 period.\"\nScenario 2 — RECERT Assessment at Day 58:\nRECERT assessment date: October 28 (Day 58 of the certification period beginning September 1). For 7-day look-back items, the window is October 21–28. For 14-day items, the window is October 14–28. Events from earlier in the certification period (September 1–October 13) are outside the look-back window for 7 and 14-day items and shall not be used to code those items. Document: \"RECERT OASIS at Day 58. 7-day look-back window: October 21–28. 14-day look-back window: October 14–28. Information from earlier in the certification period not applicable to look-back items.\"\nScenario 3 — FU/SCIC Assessment Following Hospitalization:\nFU (SCIC) assessment date: August 15. Patient was hospitalized August 5–12 and returned home August 12. For 7-day look-back items, the window is August 8–15. Three days of this window (August 8–12) were inpatient days. The inpatient-period behavioral, functional, and clinical information from August 8–12 is within scope for the look-back items. Document: \"7-day look-back for FU OASIS: August 8–15. Patient hospitalized August 5–12. August 8–12 falls within the look-back window. Hospital records and patient/caregiver report used for the inpatient portion of the window.\"\n\n---",
