        id: "24-cms-look-back-period-reference-table",
        title: "5\\. CMS Look-Back Period Reference Table",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "The following table summarizes look-back periods for key OASIS-E2 items. This table is based on the current CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual. When CMS updates the Guidance Manual, this table shall be updated within 30 calendar days per CL-OA-004. In all cases, the current CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual governs over this table.\n\n| Look-Back Period | Applicable OASIS Items (Representative) | Data Collection Notes |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Point-in-Time (Assessment Day) | GG0130 (Self-Care — SOC/ROC), GG0170 (Mobility — SOC/ROC), M1830 (Bathing — SOC/ROC/DC), M1840–M1860 (Toileting, Transferring — SOC/ROC/DC), M1870 (Eating — SOC/ROC/DC) | Reflects the patient's performance or status at the time of the assessment encounter. Activities should be directly observed during the visit when feasible. |\n| Past 24 Hours | Some clinical symptom items per OASIS-E2 Guidance | Covers the 24-hour period immediately before the assessment. Patient and caregiver report are the primary sources for the preceding hours not directly observed. |\n| Past 7 Days (7-calendar-day look-back) | M1700 (Cognitive Function), M1710 (When Confused), M1720 (When Anxious), M1740 (Behavioral Symptoms), M1745 (Frequency of Disruptive Behaviors), M1800–M1870 (ADL assistance items at applicable time points), GG0130/GG0170 items at RECERT/DC | Covers the 7 calendar days prior to and including the assessment date. Patient and caregiver report supplement direct observation for the full 7-day window. |\n| Past 14 Days (14-calendar-day look-back) | M1730 (Depressive Feelings — PHQ-2/PHQ-9 covers \"past 2 weeks\"), M2001 (Drug Regimen Review), M2010 (High-Risk Medication Education), M2020 (Management of Oral Medications), M2030 (Management of Injectable Medications) | Covers the 14 calendar days prior to and including the assessment date. PHQ-2/PHQ-9 use the phrase \"past 2 weeks\" — this is equivalent to the 14-day look-back. |\n| Since the Last Home Health SOC or RECERT | M1311 (Pressure Injury — number) | Tracks events or conditions since the start of the current certification period or since the last SOC if no prior certification occurred. |\n| During the Current Certification Period | Certain wound-tracking and outcome items | Reflects cumulative status across the certification period. |\n| Current/Active (no look-back — present status) | M0110 (Episodic Information), M1000–M1023 (Prior Care History), M1030 (Therapies at Home), M1033–M1036 (Risk Assessment items), M1200–M1242 (Integumentary Status — current), diagnoses | Coded based on current status or current history — not limited by a look-back window. |\n\n---",
