        id: "9-escalation-for-unresolvable-judgment-questions",
        title: "Escalation for Unresolvable Judgment Questions",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 7.2.1 | Assessing RN | If a judgment-based coding question cannot be resolved by the assessor after applying the evidence hierarchy, reviewing the CMS Guidance Manual, and attempting to document the reasoning, escalate to the Director of Nursing for clinical adjudication before locking the assessment. Describe the specific item, the triggering condition, the available evidence, and the response options being considered. | Before locking; within the OASIS completion deadline. |\n| 7.2.2 | Director of Nursing | Provide clinical adjudication guidance. If the Director of Nursing also cannot resolve the ambiguity through clinical judgment and Guidance Manual review, initiate the question submission process to the state OASIS contractor per CL-OA-004. Document the adjudication guidance in the patient's clinical record. | Within 24 hours of escalation; within OASIS completion deadline. |\n| 7.2.3 | Director of Nursing | Compile all recurring judgment-based coding questions in the agency's Item-Level Ambiguity Log per CL-OA-004 Section 6.2.3. Use recurring patterns to develop pre-emptive guidance for common scenarios and to identify training needs. | Log updated at each recurring question identification; reviewed quarterly. |\n\n---",
