        title: "Core Verification Comparisons",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Assessing RN | Functional Status Verification: Compare all GG functional item responses (GG0130, GG0170) against: (a) the referral's discharge functional summary; (b) any PT or OT evaluation reports available; (c) the physician's functional status notation in the discharge summary or office notes; (d) visit notes from the look-back period that describe the patient's functional performance. Identify any response where the OASIS reflects a significantly different functional level than any of these documents without a documented clinical reason for the difference. Document any inconsistency identified and its resolution in the checklist. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.2 | Assessing RN | Diagnosis and Clinical History Verification: Compare the diagnoses coded in the plan of care and the diagnoses referenced in OASIS clinical severity items against: (a) the referring physician's diagnosis list; (b) the hospital discharge diagnosis list; (c) the medication list (medications should be consistent with the documented diagnoses — a patient on insulin should have a diabetes diagnosis; a patient on anticoagulants should have a relevant diagnosis explaining the anticoagulation). Flag any diagnosis referenced in the OASIS that does not appear in the physician record, and any diagnosis in the physician record that appears clinically relevant but is not reflected in the OASIS. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.3 | Assessing RN | Medication Verification: Compare the medication list used for M2001 (Drug Regimen Review) and M2010 (High-Risk Medication Education) against: (a) the physician's current medication orders; (b) the medication reconciliation worksheet per CL-SD-013; (c) the patient's medication bottles (as documented during the assessment visit). Verify that the medication list used for OASIS coding reflects the actual medications at the time of assessment — not the pre-discharge medication list without modification per the reconciliation findings. Flag any medication in the OASIS list not supported by a current physician order, and any physician-ordered medication not in the OASIS list. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.4 | Assessing RN | Wound Status Verification: Compare all wound item responses (M1311–M1350) against: (a) the wound assessment documentation from the SOC/ROC visit; (b) the most recent wound care visit note from the look-back period; (c) the wound photographs if obtained per CL-SD-011; (d) the referral's wound description from the discharging facility. Verify that wound stage, measurements, and character are consistent across the OASIS coding and the narrative wound documentation. Any discrepancy between the OASIS wound response and the concurrent wound narrative documentation is a material inconsistency requiring resolution before locking. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.5 | Assessing RN | Behavioral Health Verification: Compare behavioral health item responses (M1700–M1750) against: (a) the BIMS component scores and total score documented in the assessment narrative; (b) the PHQ-2/PHQ-9 item scores documented in the assessment narrative; (c) the physician's notes regarding the patient's cognitive status; (d) the caregiver's report of the patient's behavioral patterns from the look-back period as documented in the assessment narrative. Verify that M1700 responses are consistent with BIMS scores, and that M1730/M1750 responses are consistent with PHQ-2/PHQ-9 scores. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.6 | Assessing RN | Homebound Status Verification: Compare the homebound status narrative against: (a) the GG functional item responses — the homebound documentation must be consistent with the functional levels coded in GG items (e.g., a patient coded as independent in all GG mobility items would be difficult to document as homebound without specific clinical justification); (b) the physician's clinical notes documenting the patient's functional status; (c) the patient's stated activity patterns as documented in the assessment narrative. Flag any homebound documentation that is inconsistent with GG functional responses or physician documentation. | During verification. |\n| 6.2.7 | Assessing RN | Physician Order Consistency Verification: Compare the services and disciplines listed in the developing plan of care and the OASIS items reflecting services ordered (where applicable) against the current physician order set. Verify that: (a) every discipline ordered has a corresponding physician order; (b) every physician order for a service is reflected in the plan of care; (c) no service is documented as ordered in the OASIS or plan of care without a supporting physician order. | During verification. |\n\n---",
