        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Assessing RN | Document the drug regimen review in the assessment narrative with the following elements: (a) the review methodology (physical inventory conducted, interview conducted, pharmacy profile accessed); (b) the number of medications reviewed; (c) any medications present in the home but not on the prescribed list; (d) any prescribed medications not present in the home; (e) any adherence concerns identified; (f) any potential clinically significant issues identified with specific description; (g) physician notification status (date, time, method, outcome) if issues were found. | In the assessment narrative; before locking. |\n| 6.4.2 | Assessing RN | For M2020 and M2030, document: (a) what was directly observed or reported about the patient's medication management behavior; (b) whether the patient manages medications independently, with assistance, or requires full administration by another; (c) if the patient uses a medication organizer — who fills it and how frequently; (d) for injectables — who prepares and who administers. The documentation must be specific enough that the response option selected is the only defensible choice given the documented evidence. | In the assessment narrative; before locking. |\n| 6.4.3 | Assessing RN | For M2010 (High-Risk Drug Education), document: (a) which high-risk medications as defined by CMS are in the patient's regimen; (b) that education specific to those medications was provided; (c) the specific educational content delivered; (d) the patient's/caregiver's demonstrated understanding. M2010 requires that education be specific to the patient's high-risk medications — general medication safety education does not satisfy this requirement. | In the assessment narrative; before locking. |\n\n---",
