        order: 12,
        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Patient is unable to produce any medications for review (no medications accessible in the home) | Assessing RN documents and notifies Director of Nursing | Document the specific reason no medications are accessible. Contact caregiver and pharmacy to establish the current medication list. Code M2001 per CMS guidance for the circumstance where medications are not available for review. Director of Nursing assesses whether the patient's medication management situation constitutes a patient safety concern requiring physician notification. | Documentation immediately; Director of Nursing notification within 2 hours. |\n| Patient refuses drug regimen review | Assessing RN documents refusal | Document patient's refusal in the assessment narrative. Code M2001 per CMS guidance for refusal circumstances. Notify physician of refusal and any clinical concerns about medication management. | Documentation immediately; physician notification within 24 hours. |\n| Drug regimen review identifies a medication with immediate patient safety implications (e.g., dangerously elevated INR, suspected opioid overdose risk, severe hypoglycemia) | Assessing RN follows emergency clinical protocols | Treat as a clinical emergency per applicable protocol (CL-SD-012, CL-SD-014, CL-SD-019). Physician notification is immediate — not \"within one calendar day.\" Code M2003 as physician contacted (the emergency notification satisfies the M2003 requirement when it occurs on the same day or the following calendar day). | Immediately per emergency protocol. |\n| M2020 OASIS response is inconsistent with medication management OASIS from prior certification period without documented clinical change | OASIS Quality Reviewer identifies during Level 2 review | Quality Reviewer assesses whether the change in M2020 coding reflects a genuine clinical change or a coding inconsistency. If a genuine change, the clinical record should reflect the change. If a coding inconsistency, initiate correction per CL-OA-002. Director of Nursing provides targeted coaching. | Correction within 5 business days; coaching within 7 calendar days. |\n\n---",
