        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assessing RN | Upon completing an assessment visit (SOC, ROC, RECERT, FU), initiate OASIS documentation immediately — at the visit using mobile EHR access, or within 2 hours of returning to the office/home. The goal is same-day or next-day completion; the operational target of 3 calendar days is the maximum, not the expectation. | At or immediately after each assessment visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assessing RN | Monitor personal OASIS completion status in the OASIS Completion Tracking Dashboard daily. Each assessor is responsible for ensuring their assigned assessments are on track to meet operational targets. Do not wait for the coordinator alert at the operational target date — self-monitor and complete assessments proactively. | Daily. |\n| 6.1.3 | Assessing RN | When an assessor identifies that they will be unable to complete a scheduled assessment within the operational target due to a clinical or personal circumstance, notify the Director of Nursing on the same business day. The Director of Nursing may authorize a 24-hour extension to the operational target (not the regulatory deadline) for documented valid reasons and may arrange reassignment if needed. | On the business day the barrier is identified. |\n| 6.1.4 | Assessing RN | Document any external circumstance that affects assessment completion timing contemporaneously — in the EHR with a timestamp — at the time the circumstance occurs. Do not attempt to document external circumstances after the deadline has passed. | At the time the external circumstance occurs. |\n\n---",
