        id: "8-scoring-process",
        title: "Scoring Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assessing RN | Immediately following tool administration, score each component of the administered tool before moving to the next clinical activity. Do not rely on memory — score while the patient's responses are still immediately available. | Immediately after tool administration. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assessing RN | Calculate the total score by summing the individual component scores per the algorithm in Section 5. Verify the arithmetic by re-adding the component scores. | At the time of scoring. |\n| 6.1.3 | Assessing RN | Apply the score-to-OASIS-response mapping from the CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual. Verify that the coded OASIS item response corresponds to the total score band. | At the time of OASIS item coding. |\n| 6.1.4 | Assessing RN | Document all individual component scores, the total score, the score band, and the OASIS item response in the assessment narrative per CL-OA-011. The documentation sequence (components → total → score band → OASIS response) must be visible in the narrative and must be internally consistent. | Before locking the assessment. |\n| 6.1.5 | Assessing RN | Before locking, perform a final self-check: re-verify that the documented OASIS item response matches the documented total score's score band. If there is any discrepancy between the documented score and the coded OASIS response, do not lock — correct the discrepancy first. | Before locking. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
