        id: "10-remediation-protocol-for-domain-failure",
        title: "Remediation Protocol for Domain Failure",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Director of Nursing | Immediately upon identifying a domain failure during initial or annual validation: (a) suspend the assessor from independent OASIS assessment; (b) notify the assessor in writing of the specific domain failure, the performance standard not met, and the remediation requirements; (c) arrange supervised assessment coverage for the assessor's caseload. | Within 24 hours of domain failure identification. |\n| 6.3.2 | Director of Nursing | Develop a targeted remediation plan for the failed domain: (a) for Domain 1/2 written assessment failure — assign additional reading from the CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual chapters covering the failed areas; re-administer the written assessment or a comparable alternate assessment within 14 calendar days; (b) for Domain 3 tool administration failure — provide direct hands-on coaching with repeat demonstration practice; re-evaluate within 14 calendar days; (c) for Domain 4/5 coding failures — provide focused coding practice exercises with answer key review; re-administer the failed exercise within 14 calendar days; (d) for Domain 6/7 documentation/supervised assessment failure — provide documentation standard review and additional supervised assessments before re-evaluation; re-evaluate supervised assessment within 21 calendar days. | Within 5 business days of domain failure; remediation plan documented. |\n| 6.3.3 | Director of Nursing / Evaluator | Re-administer the failed domain evaluation after remediation. Passing standard is the same as the initial evaluation. If the assessor passes the re-evaluation, restore authorization per CL-OA-003. Document the remediation and re-evaluation in the OASIS Competency Validation Record. | Within 14–21 calendar days of remediation initiation per domain type. |\n| 6.3.4 | Director of Nursing | If the assessor fails the re-evaluation of the same domain: revoke OASIS assessor authorization. The assessor must complete the full initial OASIS Competency Program before re-applying for authorization. Document the revocation in the OASIS Competency Validation Record and update the Authorized Assessor Roster. Notify HR per HR-ER-002 regarding employment implications. | Within 24 hours of second domain failure; HR notification within 5 business days. |\n\n---",
