        id: "13-what-surveyors-and-auditors-will-look-for",
        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 13,
        body: "CMS surveyors conducting OASIS validation surveys will request evidence of the agency's OASIS quality assurance process. The Pre-Submission Quality Review Checklist — when consistently completed and when it demonstrates a pattern of assessors actively identifying and resolving issues before submission — is direct evidence of a functioning OASIS quality governance program. An agency that cannot demonstrate a systematic pre-submission review process has no structural mechanism for preventing OASIS errors that are detectable before submission.\nADR auditors will look for evidence that errors that could have been caught before submission were not caught — particularly internal consistency errors (BIMS score inconsistent with M1700 coding) and substantiation gaps (GG items with no activity-specific observation documentation). These are precisely the errors a properly conducted pre-submission review should catch. When an ADR auditor finds them, the absence of a documented pre-submission review suggests the agency lacked the quality governance to prevent them.\n\n---",
