        body: "#### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102 | Condition of Participation: Emergency Preparedness | Primary regulatory basis for this policy |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102(a) | Emergency Plan | All-hazards risk assessment and emergency plan requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102(b) | Policies and Procedures | Required policies implementing the emergency plan |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102(c) | Communication Plan | Patient communication requirements during emergencies |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102(d) | Training and Testing | Annual training and testing requirements |\n| Section 1135, Social Security Act | Waiver of Requirements During Public Health Emergencies | CMS authority to waive certain CoP requirements during declared emergencies |\n| 45 CFR § 164.510(b) | HIPAA Privacy — Emergency Disclosure | Permitted disclosure of PHI for patient care coordination during emergencies |\n\n#### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS Emergency Preparedness Final Rule (November 2016) | Comprehensive emergency preparedness requirements for Medicare-certified providers |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix A — Emergency Preparedness Interpretive Guidelines | Survey guidance for emergency preparedness CoP |\n| CMS Emergency Preparedness Resources for Home Health Agencies | Agency-specific emergency preparedness guidance |\n\n#### 9.3 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| OP-FM-005 | Emergency Operations & Business Continuity | Parent policy — organizational emergency plan; this policy is the clinical implementation arm |\n| RM-EP-001 | Pandemic & Infectious Disease Response | Specific emergency type with clinical protocols |\n| RM-EP-002 | Emergency Preparedness Training & Testing Program | Annual training and drill requirements |\n| RM-EP-003 | Patient Emergency Communication Plan | Detailed patient communication protocols |\n| CL-SD-009 | Telehealth & Remote Monitoring Services | Telehealth as an alternative to in-person visits during emergencies |\n| CL-SD-020 | Respiratory Care & Management | Technology-dependent patient clinical protocols |\n| CL-CA-005 | Homebound Status Determination & Documentation | Homebound patients are inherently vulnerable during emergencies |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body approval of the emergency plan |\n| CO-HP-001 | HIPAA Privacy Program | Emergency HIPAA disclosure provisions |\n| RM-ER-002 | Incident Reporting & Investigation | Adverse event reporting during emergency periods |\n| QA-AE-001 | Adverse Event Identification & Reporting | Patient harm during emergency period |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework classification |\n\n---",
