        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Director of Nursing | If the suspected abuser is any person employed by or contracted through the agency — including any HHA, clinical staff member, administrative staff, or contracted clinician — remove that individual from all patient contact immediately upon the Director of Nursing becoming aware of the suspicion. Do not wait for confirmation before removing the individual from patient contact. | Immediately upon identification. |\n| 6.4.2 | Director of Nursing / Compliance Officer | Notify the Compliance Officer within 2 hours. The Compliance Officer shall initiate a compliance investigation per CO-CP-007 in parallel with the government's mandatory investigation. The agency's internal investigation shall not interfere with or impede the government investigation. | Within 2 hours. |\n| 6.4.3 | HR Director / Compliance Officer | Place the suspected employee on administrative leave with or without pay per HR-ER-002, pending the outcome of the investigation. The HR Director and Administrator shall determine the employment disposition once the investigation is complete. | Immediately upon identification. |\n| 6.4.4 | Compliance Officer | Assess whether the agency is required to report the suspected employee to the applicable licensing board (California Board of Registered Nursing; Physical Therapy Board of California; etc.) — most California professional licensing boards require reporting of employees who have been found to have committed abuse of a vulnerable adult. File the required board report within the applicable statutory timeframe. | Within the applicable statutory timeframe upon substantiation. |\n| 6.4.5 | Director of Nursing | Assign a replacement clinician to the affected patient immediately to ensure continuity of care during the investigation. | Immediately upon removing the suspected employee. |\n| 6.4.6 | Compliance Officer | Report the incident to the Governing Body at the next quarterly meeting, or sooner if the incident is of sufficient severity. Include the investigation outcome and any corrective actions taken. | At the next quarterly meeting or as soon as clinically and operationally appropriate. |\n\n---",
