        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "CMS surveyors under Tag G167 through Tag G177 (42 CFR § 484.50) will specifically verify:\nEvidence of a zero-tolerance abuse policy. Surveyors will request the agency's abuse policy and will evaluate whether it clearly prohibits all forms of abuse and provides specific reporting requirements.\nEvidence of annual abuse awareness and mandatory reporting training. Surveyors will request training records for all staff. A staff member who cannot describe what constitutes abuse, the mandatory reporting threshold, or the reporting process is a training deficiency citation.\nEvidence that the agency takes prompt action when abuse is suspected. Surveyors may review clinical records and incident reports to verify that identified abuse indicators triggered reports and patient safety assessments. They will look for patterns where abuse indicators were documented in clinical records without corresponding mandatory reports.\nEvidence that employees suspected of abuse are immediately removed from patient contact. Surveyors will review any incidents involving suspected employee abuse and verify the agency's response timeline.\nInterview patients and caregivers about whether they feel safe and whether they know how to report concerns about their care.\nEvidence that the non-retaliation policy is operational. Surveyors may ask staff members whether they know they are protected from retaliation for making a report.\n\n---",
