        id: "9-skilled-nursing-visit-execution",
        title: "Skilled Nursing Visit Execution",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Assigned RN / LVN | Upon arrival, verify patient identity using two patient identifiers per OP-PA-002. Perform hand hygiene per CL-SD-016. | At the start of each visit. |\n| 6.2.2 | Assigned RN / LVN | Conduct a focused clinical assessment appropriate to the patient's diagnoses and current status, including at minimum: (a) vital signs — blood pressure, pulse, temperature, respiratory rate, oxygen saturation (as indicated); (b) pain assessment per CL-SD-014; (c) cardiopulmonary assessment for patients with cardiac or respiratory diagnoses; (d) wound assessment for patients with active wounds per CL-SD-011; (e) neurological assessment for patients with neurological conditions; (f) medication review — compare the patient's actual medication-taking behavior against the prescribed regimen per CL-SD-012; (g) fall risk evaluation per CL-SD-015; (h) home safety assessment per RM-PS-001; (i) psychosocial and behavioral health screening as indicated per CL-SD-022. | During the visit. |\n| 6.2.3 | Assigned RN / LVN | Provide skilled interventions as ordered in the plan of care, including but not limited to: wound care, medication administration, injection administration, IV therapy management, catheter care, ostomy care, diabetic management, cardiac monitoring, respiratory care, and clinical teaching. All interventions shall be performed according to current evidence-based clinical standards and the agency's clinical practice standards. | During the visit. |\n| 6.2.4 | Assigned RN / LVN | Assess and document the patient's response to all interventions provided — the patient's tolerance, clinical outcome, and any adverse reactions. | During the visit. |\n| 6.2.5 | Assigned RN / LVN | Provide individualized patient and caregiver education as indicated by the plan of care and as warranted by the visit findings. Education topics shall include disease process management, medication management, dietary modifications, activity modifications, self-monitoring techniques, and when to contact the physician or call 911. Document the education provided, the teaching method used, and the patient's/caregiver's level of understanding per CL-SD-017. | During the visit. |\n| 6.2.6 | Assigned RN / LVN | Evaluate the patient's progress toward each active goal in the plan of care. Note measurable progress, plateau, or regression for each goal. If the patient is not progressing as anticipated, assess the barriers and determine whether a plan of care modification is needed per CL-CP-002. | During the visit. |\n| 6.2.7 | Assigned RN / LVN | If the assessment reveals a significant change in the patient's condition, a new clinical finding, a medication concern, or a safety risk, notify the attending physician within 24 hours per CL-CP-005 and initiate a plan of care modification as warranted per CL-CP-002. If the finding is urgent or emergent, follow the emergency procedures in CL-CP-003, Section 6.4. | During or immediately following the visit. |\n\n---",
