        title: "Visit Documentation",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Assigned RN / LVN | Document the visit note in the EHR within 24 hours of the visit per CL-CD-004. The visit note shall include, at minimum: (a) date and time of the visit; (b) the clinical purpose of the visit; (c) subjective data — patient and caregiver reports; (d) objective data — all assessment findings including vital signs, physical findings, and clinical observations; (e) assessment — the nurse's clinical assessment and professional judgment regarding the patient's current status and response to care; (f) plan — actions taken, interventions provided, education given, physician notifications made, referrals initiated, and the plan for the next visit; (g) goal progress documentation; (h) the next scheduled visit date and clinical purpose. | Within 24 hours of the visit. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assigned RN / LVN | Ensure that the documentation supports the medical necessity and skilled nature of the visit. CMS requires that each visit note demonstrate why the service required the skills of a licensed nurse and could not have been safely and effectively performed by the patient, caregiver, or unlicensed personnel. Documentation that reads as routine, non-skilled, or maintenance-level does not support billing under Medicare. | At the time of documentation. |\n| 6.3.3 | Assigned RN / LVN | If the visit results in a change to the plan of care, a new physician order, or a referral to another discipline, document the action in the visit note and initiate the appropriate follow-up per CL-CP-002 and CL-CP-003. | Within 24 hours. |\n\n---",
