        id: "6-definitions",
        title: "5\\. Definitions",
        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Physical Therapy Evaluation | The initial comprehensive assessment performed by a licensed physical therapist that establishes the patient's baseline functional status, identifies treatment goals, and develops the PT treatment plan. |\n| Re-evaluation | A focused assessment conducted by the physical therapist at defined intervals to measure progress, adjust goals, and modify the treatment plan. |\n| Physical Therapist Assistant (PTA) | A licensed health care professional who provides physical therapy services under the direction and supervision of a licensed physical therapist. |\n| Maintenance Therapy | Therapy services that do not require the skills of a therapist and are designed to maintain the patient's current functional level rather than achieve improvement. Maintenance therapy is generally not covered under Medicare. |\n| Home Exercise Program (HEP) | An individualized set of exercises prescribed by the physical therapist for the patient and/or caregiver to perform independently between therapy visits and after discharge. |\n| Functional Mobility | The ability to move safely and effectively within the home and community, including bed mobility, transfers, ambulation, stair negotiation, and wheelchair management. |\n\n---",
