        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Physical Therapist | Upon receiving the patient assignment, review the plan of care, physician orders, OASIS assessment, and all available clinical documentation including referral information. | Before the initial evaluation visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | Physical Therapist | Conduct the initial evaluation in the patient's home, completing all elements defined in Section 4.3. Use standardized assessment tools appropriate to the patient's diagnoses (e.g., Timed Up and Go, Berg Balance Scale, 30-Second Sit to Stand, 6-Minute Walk Test, or equivalent validated tools). | Within 48 hours of referral or per physician order. |\n| 6.1.3 | Physical Therapist | Establish measurable, time-bound goals in collaboration with the patient and caregiver. Goals shall address functional deficits identified during the evaluation and shall specify: the target functional outcome, the measurement method, and the anticipated achievement timeframe. | During the evaluation visit. |\n| 6.1.4 | Physical Therapist | Develop a treatment plan that includes: specific interventions (therapeutic exercise, gait training, balance training, transfer training, modality use, manual therapy, patient education); recommended visit frequency and duration; estimated total number of visits; and discharge criteria. | During or within 24 hours of the evaluation visit. |\n| 6.1.5 | Physical Therapist | If the evaluation reveals that the patient does not require skilled PT services, or that the patient's condition is not amenable to PT intervention, document the finding and notify the physician and assigned RN within 24 hours. Do not initiate a treatment plan for a patient who does not meet skilled PT coverage criteria. | Within 24 hours of the evaluation. |\n| 6.1.6 | Physical Therapist | Communicate evaluation findings, goals, and the treatment plan to the assigned RN and all other disciplines involved in the patient's care per CL-CP-005. | Within 48 hours of the evaluation. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
