        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Physical Therapist / PTA | At each treatment visit, document: (a) the specific interventions performed; (b) the patient's response to each intervention including tolerance, exertion level, and pain response; (c) objective measurements (e.g., distance walked, repetitions completed, balance scores) that demonstrate progress toward goals; (d) patient and caregiver education provided; (e) any barriers to progress; (f) the plan for the next visit. | During the visit; documented within 24 hours. |\n| 6.2.2 | Physical Therapist / PTA | Assess and document progress toward goals at each visit using measurable, objective criteria. Avoid subjective or vague progress notations such as \"patient is doing better\" — use quantifiable data. | During each visit. |\n| 6.2.3 | Physical Therapist / PTA | If the patient is not progressing toward goals after a reasonable treatment period (typically 4–6 visits or 2 weeks of treatment), conduct a re-evaluation to determine whether continued PT is appropriate, whether goals should be modified, or whether a different treatment approach is warranted. Notify the physician and assigned RN of the re-evaluation findings. | Re-evaluation within 2 weeks of identified non-progression. |\n| 6.2.4 | Physical Therapist / PTA | Integrate fall prevention education and home exercise program instruction into every treatment visit. Update the HEP as the patient progresses. Document the HEP provided and the patient's demonstrated understanding. | At each visit. |\n\n---",
