        id: "3-purpose",
        title: "2\\. Purpose",
        level: 2,
        order: 3,
        body: "This policy establishes the clinical standards, documentation requirements, competency expectations, and discharge criteria for occupational therapy (OT) services provided by Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. Occupational therapy in the home health setting addresses the patient's ability to perform activities of daily living (ADLs) and instrumental activities of daily living (IADLs), upper extremity function, fine motor skills, cognitive-perceptual function, home safety and adaptive equipment needs, energy conservation, and functional independence training. OT is a qualifying skilled service under Medicare and may be the sole qualifying service for continued home health eligibility after the initial qualifying service (nursing, PT, or SLP) has been discharged. This policy ensures that all OT services comply with 42 CFR § 484.75, the California Occupational Therapy Practice Act, and CMS coverage requirements.\n\n---",
