        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Occupational Therapist | Develop the COTA's treatment instructions at the time of the initial evaluation, specifying authorized interventions, parameters, and criteria requiring immediate OT notification. | At evaluation. |\n| 6.3.2 | Occupational Therapist | Conduct a supervisory review of the COTA's treatment notes at minimum every 30 calendar days or every 6th COTA visit, whichever occurs first. Document the review. | Every 30 days or every 6th visit. |\n| 6.3.3 | Occupational Therapist | Conduct a direct supervisory visit (on-site joint visit with the COTA and patient) at minimum every 60 calendar days or per CBOT requirements if more frequent. | Every 60 calendar days minimum. |\n| 6.3.4 | COTA | Immediately notify the supervising OT if the patient's condition changes significantly, the patient is not responding to treatment, or any clinical situation requires OT-level clinical judgment. | Immediately upon identification. |\n\n---",
