        id: "10-rn-supervisory-visits",
        title: "RN Supervisory Visits",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Clinical Coordinator | Track the 14-day supervisory visit schedule for every patient receiving HHA services. Generate alerts when a supervisory visit is due within 3 calendar days. | Ongoing; alerts generated at Day 11. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assigned RN | Conduct the RN supervisory visit at the patient's home while the HHA is providing care, per the 14-day schedule. Complete all supervisory elements per Section 4.5. | Every 14 calendar days. |\n| 6.3.3 | Assigned RN | Document the supervisory visit in the patient's clinical record using the HHA Supervisory Visit Form (Appendix A). The form shall include: date, patient name, HHA name, tasks observed, patient satisfaction, competency assessment, any corrective guidance provided, and any care plan changes. | Within 24 hours of the supervisory visit. |\n| 6.3.4 | Assigned RN | If the supervisory visit reveals deficiencies in the HHA's performance — including failure to follow the care plan, inadequate infection control, or patient complaints — provide immediate on-site corrective guidance, document the deficiency and the corrective action, and notify the Director of Nursing. If the deficiency is serious, remove the HHA from the patient's care and reassign. | Immediate corrective guidance on-site; Director of Nursing notification within 24 hours; reassignment immediately for serious deficiencies. |\n| 6.3.5 | Director of Nursing | Review HHA supervisory visit documentation monthly. Identify patterns of deficiency across HHAs and initiate targeted retraining or disciplinary action per HR-ER-002 as warranted. | Monthly review. |\n\n---",
