        title: "Initial Competency Evaluation",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | HR Director / Director of Nursing | Upon hire, verify that the HHA has completed a state-approved HHA training program or equivalent per 42 CFR § 484.80(b). Verify training certificate and document in the personnel file. | At hire, before patient care assignment. |\n| 6.1.2 | Director of Nursing / Designated RN Evaluator | Administer the written (or oral) knowledge assessment covering all skill areas in Section 4.1. Score the assessment. A passing score is ≥80%. | At hire, before patient care assignment. |\n| 6.1.3 | Director of Nursing / Designated RN Evaluator | Conduct the return demonstration skills evaluation. The HHA must demonstrate satisfactory performance on each skill area listed in Section 4.1. Use the HHA Competency Evaluation Checklist (Appendix A). Document pass/fail for each skill. | At hire, before patient care assignment. |\n| 6.1.4 | Director of Nursing | Review the evaluation results. If the HHA passes all components, certify the HHA as competent and authorize patient care assignments. If the HHA fails any component, proceed to Section 6.3 (Remediation). | Within 24 hours of evaluation completion. |\n| 6.1.5 | HR Director | File the completed competency evaluation documentation in the HHA's personnel file per HR-WM-007. | Within 5 business days of evaluation. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
