        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Director of Nursing | Maintain a competency evaluation tracking calendar for all HHAs. Generate alerts 30 calendar days before each HHA's annual re-evaluation due date. | Ongoing; alerts at 30 days before due date. |\n| 6.2.2 | Director of Nursing / Designated RN Evaluator | Conduct the annual competency re-evaluation including: (a) written or oral knowledge assessment; (b) direct observation of skills in the home setting during a supervisory visit, or in a simulated clinical setting. Evaluate all skill areas in Section 4.1. | Before the annual evaluation due date. |\n| 6.2.3 | Director of Nursing | Review the re-evaluation results. Certify the HHA as competent if all components are passed. If any component is failed, proceed to Section 6.3. | Within 24 hours of evaluation. |\n| 6.2.4 | HR Director | File the completed annual re-evaluation in the HHA's personnel file. | Within 5 business days. |\n\n---",
