        title: "Remediation Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Director of Nursing | Immediately remove the HHA from patient care responsibilities for any failed skill area. Notify the HHA and document the removal. | Immediately upon evaluation failure. |\n| 6.3.2 | Director of Nursing / Designated RN Trainer | Provide targeted remediation training focused on the failed skill area(s). The remediation shall include: (a) review of the correct procedure; (b) demonstration by the trainer; (c) supervised practice by the HHA. Document the remediation training date, content, and trainer. | Within 7 calendar days of evaluation failure. |\n| 6.3.3 | Director of Nursing / Designated RN Evaluator | Re-evaluate the HHA on the failed skill area(s) using the same evaluation criteria as the initial assessment. | Within 14 calendar days of the original evaluation failure. |\n| 6.3.4 | Director of Nursing | If the HHA passes the re-evaluation, reinstate the HHA for patient care and document the reinstatement. If the HHA fails the re-evaluation a second time, the Director of Nursing and HR Director shall determine whether continued employment is appropriate per HR-ER-002. | Within 24 hours of re-evaluation; employment determination within 7 calendar days of second failure. |\n\n---",
