        level: 2,
        order: 20,
        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Initial competency evaluation completed before patient care | Personnel file audit | 100% — zero HHAs assigned before evaluation |\n| Annual re-evaluations completed within the 12-month window | Competency tracking calendar audit | 100% |\n| Failed evaluations result in immediate removal from affected patient care | Incident and corrective action documentation | 100% |\n| Competency records maintained in personnel files | HR audit per HR-WM-007 | 100% |\n\n### What Surveyors Will Look For\nCMS surveyors under Tag G276 (42 CFR § 484.80(c)) will request HHA personnel files and verify: (a) that an initial competency evaluation was completed before the HHA began patient care; (b) that the evaluation covers all required skill areas; (c) that annual re-evaluations are documented; (d) that failed evaluations resulted in remediation and re-evaluation before return to care. Surveyors may also directly observe HHA skills during the survey and ask HHAs to describe their training and evaluation experience.\n\n---",
