        body: "CMS surveyors conducting a standard survey under SOM Appendix B will specifically verify under Tag G160 and G184:\nEvidence that medication management is a component of the skilled nursing visit. Surveyors will select patient records and verify that the visit note documents a medication review — not merely a notation that \"meds reviewed\" but a substantive assessment of the patient's medication regimen, adherence, and any identified concerns. Superficial medication documentation is a common deficiency.\nEvidence that medication lists are current and consistent. Surveyors will compare the plan of care medication list, the visit note medication documentation, and the OASIS medication items. Inconsistencies across these documents are cited as documentation integrity failures.\nEvidence that medication education is individualized and documented. Surveyors may interview patients about their understanding of their medications. If the patient cannot describe the purpose of their medications and the clinical record does not document education, a deficiency will be cited.\nEvidence that adverse drug reactions are identified and managed. Surveyors will look for clinical records where ADR symptoms are documented in visit notes but there is no corresponding physician notification or follow-up action.\nEvidence that medication errors are reported and investigated. Surveyors will review the agency's incident reporting system for medication error trends and verify that root cause analysis is conducted for significant errors.\n\n---",
