        id: "8-pain-screening-at-every-visit",
        title: "Pain Screening at Every Visit",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | All Clinical Disciplines | At every patient encounter, screen for pain by asking the patient: \"Are you experiencing any pain right now?\" and \"Have you had pain since my last visit?\" If the patient is unable to self-report, use behavioral observation per Section 6.1.3. | At every visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | All Clinical Disciplines | If the patient reports pain, assess intensity using the appropriate validated tool: (a) Numeric Rating Scale (NRS, 0–10) for patients who can self-report; (b) Wong-Baker FACES Scale for patients who prefer a visual scale or have mild cognitive limitations; (c) FLACC Scale for patients unable to self-report. Document the tool used and the score. | At every visit where pain is reported. |\n| 6.1.3 | RN / LVN | For patients unable to self-report pain (severe cognitive impairment, aphasia, advanced dementia), observe for behavioral pain indicators: facial grimacing, guarding, moaning, agitation, restlessness, resistance to care, changes in vital signs. Apply the FLACC scale or equivalent validated behavioral tool. Document the behavioral assessment. | At every visit for non-verbal patients. |\n\n---",
