        title: "Diabetic Assessment at SOC",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Assigned RN | At the SOC visit, complete a comprehensive diabetic assessment per Section 4.1. Document all findings using the Diabetic Assessment Template (Appendix B). | At the SOC visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | Assigned RN | Assess the patient's blood glucose monitoring equipment — verify the meter is calibrated, test strips are not expired, and the patient/caregiver can operate the meter correctly. | At the SOC visit. |\n| 6.1.3 | Assigned RN | Conduct a thorough diabetic foot assessment including visual inspection, palpation of pedal pulses (dorsalis pedis, posterior tibial), and sensory assessment. Document all findings. | At the SOC visit. |\n| 6.1.4 | Assigned RN | Develop the diabetic management plan per Section 4.2. | Within 24 hours of the SOC visit. |\n\n---",
