        title: "PT Respiratory Services Integration",
        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Physical Therapist | When PT is ordered for a respiratory patient, the PT evaluation shall include: baseline 6-minute walk test (or modified version) with SpO2 monitoring throughout; Borg perceived exertion scale assessment; inspiratory muscle strength assessment; breathing pattern assessment; functional activity assessment with SpO2 monitoring during activities. | At the initial PT evaluation. |\n| 6.5.2 | Physical Therapist | Develop a respiratory-specific exercise program that includes: breathing retraining (pursed-lip breathing, diaphragmatic breathing); inspiratory muscle training if indicated; aerobic conditioning at a physician-approved intensity with SpO2 monitoring; functional activity progression; energy conservation strategies. All exercise parameters shall be coordinated with the assigned RN and shall reflect the physician-ordered activity restrictions. | Within 24 hours of the PT evaluation. |\n| 6.5.3 | Physical Therapist | At each PT visit, monitor SpO2 before, during, and after exercise. Document the specific SpO2 values at each point. If SpO2 drops below the physician-defined threshold during exercise, reduce the intensity and notify the physician per the escalation protocol. | At each PT visit. |\n| 6.5.4 | Physical Therapist | Coordinate exercise recommendations with the assigned RN to ensure consistency between PT exercise guidelines and nursing activity instructions. | Ongoing throughout the episode. |\n\n---",
