        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| SpO2 below physician-defined threshold despite supplemental oxygen at prescribed rate | Assigned RN contacts physician within 4 hours | Physician may order increased flow rate, change in delivery device, laboratory evaluation, or emergency transport. If SpO2 is critically low (<85%), call 911 immediately. Document all actions. | Physician contact within 4 hours; 911 immediately for critical values. |\n| Oxygen equipment malfunction (concentrator not producing adequate flow, tubing disconnected, empty tank) | Assigned RN contacts DME vendor immediately; notifies Director of Nursing | DME vendor provides replacement equipment or emergency service. If the patient is in distress, call 911. Document the malfunction, vendor contact, and resolution. | Vendor contact immediately; 911 if patient distress; document within 24 hours. |\n| Patient using higher oxygen flow rate than prescribed without physician order | Assigned RN documents and contacts physician | Physician assessment for appropriateness; order obtained if higher flow is medically indicated. If the patient self-adjusted, provide safety education on not adjusting the flow independently. | Physician contact within 24 hours. |\n| Patient continues to smoke while on supplemental oxygen therapy | Assigned RN documents and contacts physician and Director of Nursing | Safety education provided regarding fire risk. Director of Nursing assesses whether safe home oxygen therapy can continue. Smoking cessation referral per physician order. If the risk is uncontrollable, Director of Nursing assesses for safety-related discharge per CL-CP-006 Section 6.4. | Patient education immediately; Director of Nursing assessment within 24 hours. |\n| Respiratory documentation does not support skilled nursing | Director of Nursing chart review | Documentation coaching with specific examples of analysis-level respiratory documentation. Re-audit within 30 days. | Coaching within 7 calendar days. |\n\n---",
