        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.60 | Condition of Participation: Care Planning, Coordination, and Quality of Care | Respiratory management as part of the plan of care |\n| 42 CFR § 484.75 | Condition of Participation: Skilled Professional Services | Respiratory assessment and management as skilled nursing |\n| 42 CFR § 484.75(a) | Standard: Duties of the registered nurse | RN responsibilities for respiratory assessment and oxygen management |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS Home Health Benefit Manual, Chapter 7, § 40.1 | Respiratory care as a qualifying skilled nursing service |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B, Tag G184 | Survey guidance for skilled professional services including respiratory care |\n| CMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual | Respiratory-related OASIS items |\n\n### 9.3 Clinical Practice Standards\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| GOLD (Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease) — Global Strategy for the Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of COPD (current edition) | Evidence-based COPD management framework |\n| GINA (Global Initiative for Asthma) — Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention (current edition) | Evidence-based asthma management framework |\n| American Association for Respiratory Care (AARC) Clinical Practice Guidelines | Respiratory therapy standards applicable to home care |\n| American Thoracic Society / European Respiratory Society Standards | Respiratory disease classification and management |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to CL-SD-020 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| CL-CP-001 | Plan of Care Development & Approval | Respiratory management plan as part of the plan of care |\n| CL-CP-002 | Plan of Care Review & Update | Exacerbation triggers plan of care modification |\n| CL-CP-003 | Physician Orders & Order Management | Oxygen therapy and respiratory medication orders |\n| CL-SD-001 | Skilled Nursing Assessment & Services | Respiratory assessment integrated into every nursing visit |\n| CL-SD-002 | Physical Therapy Services | PT pulmonary rehabilitation services |\n| CL-SD-009 | Telehealth & Remote Monitoring Services | Remote SpO2 and symptom monitoring |\n| CL-SD-012 | Medication Management & Administration | Respiratory medication management |\n| CL-SD-014 | Pain Assessment & Management | Chest pain and dyspnea-related discomfort |\n| CL-SD-015 | Fall Risk Assessment & Prevention | Fall risk from hypoxemia, dyspnea with exertion |\n| CL-SD-016 | Infection Prevention & Control | Respiratory infection transmission precautions |\n| CL-SD-017 | Patient Education & Self-Management | Respiratory self-management education |\n| RM-EP-001 | Pandemic & Infectious Disease Response | Respiratory disease outbreak protocols |\n| RM-ER-002 | Incident Reporting & Investigation | Respiratory emergency event reporting |\n| OP-SL-004 | Equipment & Supply Management | DME coordination for oxygen equipment |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified |\n\n---",
