        id: "29-training-acknowledgment-requirements",
        title: "10\\. Training & Acknowledgment Requirements",
        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All RNs and LVNs providing care to respiratory patients shall receive competency-validated training within 14 calendar days of hire and annually thereafter, covering: comprehensive respiratory assessment technique; SpO2 measurement and clinical interpretation; inhaler technique assessment for all device types (MDI, DPI, soft-mist, nebulizer) with hands-on device demonstration; oxygen therapy management and equipment assessment; exacerbation recognition and classification; emergency respiratory response; respiratory documentation standards demonstrating skilled care; and oxygen safety education.\n10.2 All PTs providing pulmonary rehabilitation services shall receive training on SpO2 monitoring during exercise, exercise parameter adjustment based on SpO2 findings, and coordination of respiratory exercise programs with the assigned RN.\n10.3 Inhaler technique competency for all respiratory medications used by the agency's patient population shall be validated by the Director of Nursing or designee at hire, using the Inhaler Technique Competency Evaluation Tool (Appendix D), before clinicians independently teach patients inhaler use.\n10.4 All personnel within scope of this policy shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix C) within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new hire/appointment.\n10.5 The Director of Nursing shall maintain training completion and competency records for all clinicians providing respiratory care services and shall report any non-compliance to the Administrator within 7 calendar days of any training deadline.\n\n---",
