        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Director of Nursing | Upon receipt of a pediatric referral, assess the agency's capacity to accept the case before acceptance: (a) verify that a qualified RN with documented pediatric nursing experience is available to conduct the SOC assessment and manage the case; (b) verify that all ordered disciplines can be staffed by clinicians with pediatric experience; (c) verify that appropriate pediatric assessment tools and equipment are available; (d) assess whether the patient's specific clinical complexity (technology-dependent child, medically fragile neonate, pediatric patient with rare diagnosis) is within the agency's clinical capability. If any capability gap is identified, the Director of Nursing shall determine whether the gap can be filled before accepting or whether the referral must be declined. | Before referral acceptance. |\n| 6.1.2 | Director of Nursing | Document the staffing determination, including the names of the assigned clinicians and their pediatric competency status, in the patient's intake record. | At acceptance. |\n| 6.1.3 | HR Director / Director of Nursing | Verify that all assigned pediatric clinicians have current pediatric competency validation in their personnel file per HR-WM-007. If a clinician has not been previously assigned to a pediatric patient and lacks documented pediatric competency, arrange for competency validation before the first pediatric visit. | Before first pediatric visit. |\n\n---",
