        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | All Clinical Disciplines | At each pediatric visit, approach the child in a developmentally appropriate manner: (a) Infants and toddlers — speak in a calm, warm tone; include the caregiver in all interactions; explain all procedures to the caregiver before performing them; minimize separation from the caregiver; (b) Preschool and school-age children — explain procedures at an age-appropriate level using simple, concrete language and avoiding threatening words (\"hurt,\" \"cut\"); allow the child to make simple choices when possible (which arm for blood pressure, which room for the visit); acknowledge the child's feelings; (c) Adolescents — address the patient directly, not only the caregiver; acknowledge their developing autonomy; provide age-appropriate health information directly to the patient; respect their privacy within legal limits. | At each visit. |\n| 6.4.2 | All Clinical Disciplines | At each visit, assess developmental milestone progress using observation and caregiver report. Document any milestone delay, regression, or newly identified developmental concern. Notify the physician if a new developmental concern is identified. | At each visit. |\n| 6.4.3 | Assigned RN | Provide structured caregiver training at each visit. The caregiver training shall be documented with the same specificity as patient education: what skill was taught, what method was used (demonstration, return demonstration, written materials), the caregiver's demonstrated competency level, and the plan for the next training session. Caregiver training shall progress from observation to guided practice to independent supervised performance to independent competency. | At each visit. |\n| 6.4.4 | Assigned RN | Assess the caregiver's stress and coping at each visit. If signs of caregiver burnout, exhaustion, or emotional distress are identified, document the assessment and initiate an MSW referral per CL-SD-005. | At each visit. |\n\n---",
