        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | All Clinical Disciplines | At each visit, observe the child and the home environment for indicators of potential abuse, neglect, or exploitation, including: unexplained injuries or bruising; injuries inconsistent with the explanation provided; multiple injuries in different stages of healing; fearful or avoidant behavior toward caregivers; inadequate supervision; signs of physical neglect (hunger, inadequate clothing, poor hygiene, failure to thrive without a medical explanation); signs of emotional abuse (extreme behavior, withdrawal, low self-esteem); caregiver behavior suggesting abuse potential (hostile, dismissive, excessively controlling, intoxicated). | At every pediatric visit. |\n| 6.5.2 | Any Clinician | If reasonable suspicion of child abuse or neglect is identified, the clinician shall: (a) immediately ensure the child's immediate safety at the visit site; (b) report to the Director of Nursing within 2 hours; (c) call the California Child Protective Services (CPS) hotline at 1-800-540-4000 or the local CPS office and make a verbal report within the timeframe required by California Penal Code § 11166 — the report is due immediately upon forming reasonable suspicion, or within 36 hours for non-emergency written report; (d) complete the Suspected Child Abuse Report (SCAR — SS 8572 form) within 36 hours; (e) notify the Compliance Officer per HR-ER-009. The clinician shall NOT investigate the suspected abuse or confront the caregiver — the reporting obligation is triggered by reasonable suspicion alone. | Verbal report immediately upon forming reasonable suspicion; written report within 36 hours. |\n| 6.5.3 | Director of Nursing | Upon notification of a suspected child abuse report, immediately ensure the child's safety assessment, coordinate with the Compliance Officer, contact the agency's legal counsel if warranted, and document all actions. Do not interfere with the CPS investigation. | Within 2 hours of notification. |\n\n---",
