        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All clinicians assigned to pediatric patients shall receive competency-validated pediatric-specific training before their first independent pediatric patient visit, covering: age-appropriate vital sign reference ranges and assessment technique; developmental milestone surveillance; family-centered care principles; caregiver training documentation; pediatric weight-based medication dosing and verification; mandatory reporting obligations and reporting thresholds; age-appropriate communication techniques; and pediatric-specific clinical documentation standards.\n10.2 Pediatric competency shall be validated through: (a) written knowledge assessment (≥80% passing score) covering pediatric vital sign ranges, developmental milestones, and mandatory reporting requirements; (b) clinical skills demonstration or simulation for pediatric assessment technique.\n10.3 Annual refresher training on mandatory reporting obligations shall be provided to all clinical staff per HR-ER-009 regardless of whether they currently serve pediatric patients.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix C) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, any revision, or hire.\n\n---",
