        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | All Clinical Disciplines | At every patient visit, screen for behavioral health changes using clinical observation: (a) Is the patient's affect congruent with their situation? (b) Has the patient's mood changed since the last visit (more withdrawn, tearful, hopeless, agitated, confused)? (c) Is the patient's sleep pattern disturbed? (d) Is the patient's appetite changed? (e) Has the patient expressed any statements suggesting hopelessness, worthlessness, or thoughts of self-harm? (f) Is the patient's cognition at baseline or declining? (g) Is the patient exhibiting new or worsening behavioral symptoms (agitation, wandering, combativeness, paranoia)? | At every visit by all disciplines. |\n| 6.2.2 | Any Clinical Discipline | When a behavioral health change is identified during any visit, document the specific observation and report it to the assigned RN within 24 hours. | Within 24 hours of identification. |\n| 6.2.3 | Assigned RN | When any behavioral health change is reported or identified, conduct a focused behavioral health reassessment using the appropriate validated tool (PHQ-9 for depression, GAD-7 for anxiety, cognitive assessment for cognitive change). Document the reassessment findings and compare to the SOC baseline. | Within 48 hours of the reported change. |\n| 6.2.4 | Assigned RN | Administer the PHQ-9 at each OASIS assessment time point (recertification) for all patients, regardless of the SOC screening result, to track depression status over the episode. | At each OASIS time point. |\n\n---",
