        title: "Physician Notification and Plan of Care Integration",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Assigned RN | Notify the physician within 24 hours of any of the following behavioral health screening findings: (a) PHQ-2 ≥3 (positive depression screen); (b) PHQ-9 ≥5 (any level of depression); (c) BIMS score <8 (severely impaired cognition); (d) GAD-7 ≥10 (moderate to severe anxiety); (e) Any new or significantly worsening behavioral health finding identified during the episode. Document the physician notification, the information communicated, and the physician's response. | Within 24 hours of the finding. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assigned RN | Incorporate behavioral health findings and the planned response into the plan of care per CL-CP-001, including: the specific screening results; the physician's guidance; any ordered behavioral health medications; the referral plan; and the behavioral health monitoring plan for the episode. | Within 24 hours of physician notification. |\n\n---",
