        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All RNs shall receive competency-validated training on behavioral health screening within 14 calendar days of hire and annually thereafter, covering: PHQ-2 and PHQ-9 administration, scoring, and clinical interpretation; BIMS administration and scoring per CMS OASIS-E2 guidance; GAD-7 administration and scoring; suicidality assessment using the C-SSRS; safety plan development; behavioral health referral pathways; OASIS behavioral health item coding; and documentation standards.\n10.2 BIMS administration competency shall be validated by observation — the RN must demonstrate correct administration of all three BIMS components before independently conducting OASIS assessments. This shall be assessed at hire and annually.\n10.3 All clinical disciplines shall receive training on behavioral health observation and reporting responsibilities — specifically, how to identify and report behavioral health changes between RN assessment visits.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, revision, or hire.\n\n---",
