        body: "10.1 All RNs and MSWs shall receive competency-validated training on palliative and end-of-life care within 14 calendar days of hire and annually thereafter, covering: palliative care principles and the distinction between palliative care and hospice; advance directive types, legal requirements under California law, and POLST execution; goals-of-care communication skills using an evidence-based framework (REMAP, SPIKES, or equivalent); end-of-life symptom assessment and management (pain, dyspnea, delirium, constipation, secretions); opioid use for dyspnea in comfort-focused patients; hospice referral coordination per CL-CP-007; bereavement support; and documentation standards for palliative care visits demonstrating skilled nursing.\n10.2 All clinical disciplines shall receive training on advance directive status awareness — they must be able to identify whether a patient has an advance directive and know where to find it in the clinical record.\n10.3 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within 14 calendar days of the effective date, revision, or hire.\n\n---",
