        id: "13-escalation-and-exception-handling",
        title: "Escalation and Exception Handling",
        level: 3,
        order: 13,
        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Clinician missed the visit due to scheduling error | Clinical Coordinator and Director of Nursing | Reschedule immediately. Assess whether the scheduling error was systemic. Director of Nursing provides corrective guidance to scheduling staff. | Rescheduling within 24 hours; root cause assessment within 5 business days. |\n| Patient not found and cannot be reached — high risk | Director of Nursing calls 911 | Emergency welfare check. Physician notification. Incident report per RM-ER-002 if patient is found to have experienced a clinical emergency. | 911 immediately for high-risk; incident report within 24 hours. |\n| Missed visits are creating LUPA risk | Revenue Cycle and Director of Nursing | Per QA-PI-006 and CL-SD-025 — clinical review, scheduling adjustment, physician contact if additional visits are warranted. | Immediate review; action within 24 hours. |\n| Clinician documents a missed visit more than 24 hours after the scheduled visit | Director of Nursing chart review | Director of Nursing provides corrective guidance. Clinician completes a late-entry notation per CO-DC-003. | Documentation completed within 24 hours of identification. |\n\n---",
