        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Clinical Coordinator | Generate a daily Visit Frequency Compliance Report from the Visit Frequency Monitoring System for all active patients. The report shall display: (a) patient name and MR#; (b) each active discipline; (c) the ordered visit frequency for the current certification period; (d) the delivered visit count to date in the current certification period; (e) the remaining ordered visits in the current certification period; (f) the current variance (ordered minus delivered); (g) LUPA risk status — flagged if the episode is at risk of not meeting the LUPA threshold. | Daily; by 9:00 AM. |\n| 6.1.2 | Clinical Coordinator | Review the daily report for any new variances and classify each using the tier system per Section 4.3. For Tier 1 variances, take immediate rescheduling action and document in the patient's record. For Tier 2 or Tier 3 variances, notify the Director of Nursing immediately. | Immediately upon generating the daily report. |\n| 6.1.3 | Clinical Coordinator | Update the Visit Frequency Monitoring System as visits are completed, missed, or rescheduled throughout each day. The system shall reflect the current delivery status in real time. | Continuously throughout each business day. |\n\n---",
