        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Requesting Department | Submit an AI System Approval Request to the IT Director / CISO and Compliance Officer. Request must include: (a) system name and vendor; (b) intended use; (c) data inputs required (PHI, de-identified, non-health); (d) deployment model (cloud, on-premise, hybrid); (e) clinical vs. non-clinical use. | Prior to any use. |\n| 6.1.2 | IT Director / CISO | Conduct technical security assessment including: (a) data storage and encryption; (b) access controls; (c) audit logging capability; (d) data retention/deletion practices; (e) vendor security posture (SOC 2 or equivalent for Category A). | Within 30 calendar days of request. |\n| 6.1.3 | Compliance Officer | Conduct privacy impact analysis including: (a) PHI exposure assessment; (b) minimum necessary evaluation; (c) BAA requirement determination; (d) HIPAA compliance evaluation; (e) California law compliance evaluation. | Within 30 calendar days of request. |\n| 6.1.4 | IT Director / Compliance Officer | Assign category (A, B, or C) based on assessment results. Category A requires Administrator approval. Category C systems are prohibited. | Upon assessment completion. |\n| 6.1.5 | IT Director | Add approved systems to the Approved AI Systems Registry with: (a) system name; (b) vendor; (c) category; (d) approved use cases; (e) PHI exposure level; (f) BAA status; (g) responsible department; (h) approval date; (i) next review date. | Within 7 calendar days of approval. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
