        id: "9-ai-use-in-clinical-documentation",
        title: "AI Use in Clinical Documentation",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | All Clinical Staff | When using AI-assisted documentation tools, review every element of the generated output against actual clinical observations, patient interview responses, and objective findings. Modify all inaccurate or fabricated content before signing. | At each AI-assisted documentation event. |\n| 6.2.2 | All Clinical Staff | Never copy AI-generated clinical content into the clinical record without independent verification. The clinician's authentication constitutes professional attestation that the content is accurate. | Continuous. |\n| 6.2.3 | Director of Nursing | Conduct quarterly review of AI-assisted documentation quality. Sample a minimum of 10% of AI-assisted clinical documents per quarter and evaluate for: (a) accuracy; (b) completeness; (c) absence of fabricated content; (d) alignment with clinician observations. | Quarterly. |\n\n---",
