        title: "Identification and Risk Classification",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | All Department Heads | Identify all vendors, contractors, and service providers who access, create, receive, maintain, or transmit PHI in the course of providing services to the agency. Submit identified entities to the Compliance Officer. | Ongoing; comprehensive review annually. |\n| 6.1.2 | Compliance Officer | Review each identified entity to determine if the entity meets the definition of a business associate under 45 CFR § 160.103. Document the determination. | Within 14 calendar days of identification. |\n| 6.1.3 | Compliance Officer | Assign a risk tier (Tier 1, 2, or 3) based on the nature, scope, and volume of PHI access. Document the classification rationale. | At the time of determination. |\n\n---",
