        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Patient Intake / Clinical Staff | Upon intake, provide the patient with: (a) HIPAA Notice of Privacy Practices (CO-HP-001); (b) Agency CMIA Confidentiality Statement identifying California-specific rights; (c) explanation that certain categories of information receive heightened protection under California law. Obtain patient acknowledgment. | At or before first billable visit. |\n| 6.1.2 | Clinical Staff / Compliance Officer | Before disclosing any medical information upon request, determine whether the request falls within a CMIA permitted disclosure (Civil Code §56.10(b)/(c)) or requires a valid CMIA authorization. Use the CMIA Disclosure Decision Tree (Appendix A). | Before each disclosure — no retroactive authorization accepted. |\n| 6.1.3 | Clinical Staff / Compliance Officer | If the requested information is Sensitive Category Information (see Section 4), require a signed CMIA authorization even if the disclosure would otherwise be permitted under HIPAA. Do not release Sensitive Category Information based on HIPAA authorization alone. | Before disclosure of any Sensitive Category Information. |\n| 6.1.4 | Compliance Officer / Administrator | Review all CMIA authorization forms at least annually to confirm they meet the requirements of Civil Code §56.11. Update forms within 30 calendar days of any legislative change affecting required elements. | Annual review; update within 30 days of legislative change. |\n| 6.1.5 | Releasing Staff Member | Log all disclosures of medical information (consistent with CO-HP-006 Accounting of Disclosures procedures) including: (a) date and recipient of disclosure; (b) description of information disclosed; (c) authorization or permitted exception basis; (d) whether information includes a Sensitive Category. | At time of each disclosure. |\n\n---",
