        level: 2,
        order: 3,
        body: "This policy establishes the Corporate Compliance Program (\"Program\") for Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. The Program is the agency's formal, systematic commitment to conducting all operations with integrity, in full conformity with applicable federal and state laws, regulations, and the standards issued by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS), the Office of Inspector General (OIG), and all other regulatory bodies having jurisdiction over the agency's operations. The Program satisfies the requirements set forth in the OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies and supports compliance with 42 CFR § 484.100 (Condition of Participation: Compliance with Federal, State, and Local Laws) and the agency's obligation to maintain Medicare certification. The Program provides the structural foundation upon which all other compliance-related policies in the CO domain operate.\n\n---",
