        title: "4\\. Policy Statement",
        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. shall maintain a fully operational Corporate Compliance Program that satisfies the seven foundational elements of an effective compliance program as defined by the OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies.\n4.2 The seven required elements of the Program are:\nWritten policies, procedures, and standards of conduct\nDesignation of a Compliance Officer and Compliance Committee\nEffective training and education\nEffective lines of communication\nInternal monitoring and auditing\nEnforcement of standards and well-publicized disciplinary guidelines\nPrompt response to detected offenses and development of corrective action\n4.3 The Governing Body shall maintain ultimate accountability for the effectiveness of the Program and shall receive compliance reports at no less than quarterly intervals per policy GV-GB-001.\n4.4 The Program shall be operationally independent. The Compliance Officer shall have direct reporting access to the Governing Body and shall not be subject to retaliation, pressure, or interference in performing compliance functions.\n4.5 Participation in compliance training and adherence to the Code of Conduct (CO-CP-004) are conditions of continued employment and/or contract with Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc.\n4.6 The agency shall not employ or contract with any individual or entity that appears on the OIG List of Excluded Individuals/Entities (LEIE) or the System for Award Management (SAM) exclusion database, per policy HR-TA-003.\n4.7 All known or suspected violations of law, regulation, agency policy, or the Code of Conduct shall be reported promptly through mechanisms established in policy CO-CP-006 and investigated per policy CO-CP-007.\n4.8 Only the most current approved version of this policy shall be considered valid. Any revision requires re-acknowledgment by all workforce members within scope within 14 calendar days.\n\n---",
