        body: "This policy is maintained under the agency's enterprise policy lifecycle management system per policy EN-LC-001.\nOnly the most current approved version of this policy is valid for any operational, compliance, or regulatory purpose.\nAny substantive revision requires: (a) Governing Body approval documented in meeting minutes; (b) re-acknowledgment by all applicable workforce members within 14 calendar days; (c) update to the enterprise policy index per EN-TG-001.\nNon-substantive revisions (formatting, typographical corrections) may be approved by the Compliance Officer with notification to the Governing Body at the next regular meeting.\n## Appendix A — Corporate Compliance Program Seven-Element Reference Chart\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. Policy Reference: CO-CP-001 | Version: 1.0 | Effective: 2025-07-10\n\n| Element | OIG Requirement | Care Indeed Implementation | Policy Reference | Responsible Party |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1. Written Policies & Standards | Code of Conduct; written policies for all compliance areas | Full CO-domain policy suite (CO-CP-001 through CO-DC-004) | CO-CP-001, CO-CP-004 | Compliance Officer |\n| 2. Designated Compliance Officer & Committee | Designated CO with authority; Compliance Committee | Compliance Officer designated by Governing Body; Committee chaired by CO | CO-CP-002, CO-CP-003 | Governing Body; Compliance Officer |\n| 3. Training & Education | Initial and annual compliance training for all staff | Compliance orientation at hire; annual refresher; role-specific training | CO-CP-008 | Compliance Officer |\n| 4. Effective Communication Lines | Hotline; anonymous reporting; open-door | Compliance hotline; email; anonymous reporting option; non-retaliation policy | CO-CP-005, CO-CP-006 | Compliance Officer |\n| 5. Auditing & Monitoring | Internal audit program; risk-based annual work plan | Annual audit work plan; quarterly monitoring; CO-RA-002 audit program | CO-RA-002 | Compliance Officer |\n| 6. Enforcement & Discipline | Consistent disciplinary standards; publicized | Code of Conduct enforcement; progressive discipline; no exceptions by seniority | CO-CP-004, HR-ER-002 | Compliance Officer; HR Director |\n| 7. Response to Detected Offenses | Prompt investigation; corrective action; repayment | 7-day investigation initiation; 60-day repayment; CAP development | CO-CP-007, FN-BC-004, QA-AE-003 | Compliance Officer |\n\n## Appendix B — Annual Compliance Audit Work Plan Template\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. Policy Reference: CO-CP-001 / CO-RA-002 | Version: 1.0 | Date: 2025-07-10\nCalendar Year: _______________ Approved By: _______________ Date: _______________ Compliance Committee Approval Date: _______________\nInstructions: Complete this template at the first Compliance Committee meeting of each calendar year. Distribute to Administrator and Governing Body Chair. Retain in compliance file for minimum 7 years.\n\n| # | Audit Area | Regulatory / Policy Basis | Risk Level (H/M/L) | Sample Size | Planned Quarter | Responsible Auditor | Status | Findings Summary | CAP Required? |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1 | Billing & Claims Accuracy | FN-BC-001; 42 CFR §484.100 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 2 | OASIS Data Integrity | CL-OA-001 through CL-OA-019 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 3 | Medical Necessity Documentation | FN-CM-003; CL-CA-001 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 4 | OIG/SAM Exclusion Screening Currency | HR-TA-003 | H | All | Monthly |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 5 | Policy Acknowledgment Completion | CO-CP-008; GV-PM-003 | M | All | Q1 |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 6 | Conflict of Interest Disclosures | GV-GB-003 | M | All | Q1 |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 7 | Fraud, Waste & Abuse Indicators | CO-FA-003; FN-FP-007 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 8 | HIPAA Privacy & Security Compliance | CO-HP-001; CO-HP-002 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 9 | Face-to-Face Encounter Compliance | CL-CA-006; CL-CA-007 | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 10 | Clinical Documentation Completeness | CL-CD-001 through CL-CD-004 | M | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 11 | Hotline Report Follow-Up Timeliness | CO-CP-006; CO-CP-007 | H | All | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 12 | OIG Work Plan Priority Area (specify): _____________ | OIG Work Plan | H | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 13 | Additional Focus Area (specify): _____________ |  |  | _____ | Q_____ |  |  |  | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n\nSignature — Compliance Officer: ________________________________ Date: _______________ Signature — Administrator: ________________________________ Date: _______________\n## Appendix C — Policy Acknowledgment Form\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. Policy Reference: CO-CP-001 | Version: 1.0 | Effective: 2025-07-10\nI, the undersigned, acknowledge that:\nI have received and read Policy CO-CP-001 — Corporate Compliance Program, Version 1.0, effective 2025-07-10.\nI understand the responsibilities, requirements, and expectations described in this policy as they apply to my role at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc.\nI understand that participation in the compliance program, including completing required training and reporting suspected violations, is a condition of my continued employment or contract.\nI understand that I am accountable for complying with this policy and that non-compliance may result in corrective action up to and including termination.\nI have had the opportunity to ask questions and receive clarification regarding any aspect of this policy.\n\n| Field | Entry |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Full Name (Printed) |  |\n| Title / Role |  |\n| Department |  |\n| Signature |  |\n| Date Signed |  |\n| Type: | ☐ New Hire ☐ Annual Renewal ☐ Policy Revision |\n\n---",
