        order: 3,
        body: "This policy establishes the structure, composition, responsibilities, meeting requirements, and documentation standards for the Compliance Committee of Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. The Compliance Committee is the multi-disciplinary operational body that supports the Compliance Officer in implementing, monitoring, and evaluating the Corporate Compliance Program (CO-CP-001). The Committee provides the mechanism by which compliance risk, audit findings, regulatory changes, and corrective actions are reviewed at a cross-functional level and escalated to the Governing Body as appropriate.\n\n---",
