        title: "4\\. Policy Statement",
        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. shall maintain a functioning Compliance Committee, chaired by the Compliance Officer.\n4.2 The Compliance Committee shall meet at minimum quarterly and shall maintain formal meeting minutes.\n4.3 The Compliance Committee shall serve as the primary operational body for reviewing audit findings, monitoring corrective actions, evaluating training compliance, and preparing compliance reports to the Governing Body.\n4.4 The Compliance Committee shall not have authority to override Governing Body directives or the Compliance Officer's independent compliance determinations.\n4.5 Attendance at Compliance Committee meetings is a professional obligation for all designated members. Absence without advance notice and a designated alternate is not acceptable.\n\n---",
