        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "### 5.1 Patient-Centered Care and Dignity\nAll workforce members shall:\nTreat every patient with dignity, respect, and compassion regardless of diagnosis, age, race, color, national origin, sex, disability, religion, or ability to pay.\nProtect patient privacy and confidentiality at all times per policies CO-HP-001 and CO-HP-002.\nHonor patient rights as defined in policy CL-PR-001.\nNever exploit, abuse, neglect, or mistreat a patient. All suspected abuse, neglect, or exploitation shall be reported immediately per policies CL-PR-006 and HR-ER-009.\nProvide only services that are ordered, medically necessary, and within their scope of practice.\n### 5.2 Integrity in Billing and Documentation\nAll workforce members shall:\nDocument clinical services accurately, completely, and truthfully.\nNever document services not actually rendered, alter clinical records to support billing, or fail to document care that was provided.\nNever submit or participate in the submission of a false claim to Medicare, Medicaid, or any other payer.\nReport suspected billing irregularities or documentation falsification through CO-CP-006.\n### 5.3 Conflict of Interest\nAll workforce members shall:\nDisclose any personal, financial, or professional interest that could conflict with the agency's interests or their professional obligations.\nNever allow a conflict of interest to influence a patient care decision, business decision, or compliance determination.\nGoverning Body members shall comply with the full conflict of interest management requirements of policy GV-GB-003.\n### 5.4 Gifts, Gratuities, and Kickbacks\nAll workforce members shall:\nNever accept or offer gifts, meals, entertainment, or gratuities that exceed $25 per occurrence or $50 annually from any patient, vendor, referral source, or competitor.\nNever offer, pay, solicit, or receive anything of value in exchange for patient referrals, in violation of the Anti-Kickback Statute (42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7b).\nReport any solicitation of a kickback or improper referral arrangement immediately to the Compliance Officer.\n### 5.5 Confidentiality and Privacy\nAll workforce members shall:\nNever access, use, or disclose patient health information beyond the minimum necessary for their assigned duties.\nNever discuss patient information in non-private settings (hallways, vehicles, social settings).\nNever share login credentials, access patient records on behalf of another, or circumvent system access controls.\nReport any known or suspected breach of patient information per policy CO-HP-003.\n### 5.6 Workplace Respect and Anti-Harassment\nAll workforce members shall:\nTreat colleagues, supervisors, and subordinates with respect and professionalism at all times.\nNever engage in harassment, discrimination, or hostile conduct based on any protected characteristic.\nReport harassment or discrimination per policy HR-ER-004.\n### 5.7 Compliance with Laws and Regulations\nAll workforce members shall:\nComply with all applicable federal and state laws, regulations, and agency policies relevant to their role.\nNever perform, authorize, or conceal any act that they know or reasonably believe violates applicable law.\nCooperate fully with all internal compliance audits and investigations.\n### 5.8 Stewardship of Agency Resources\nAll workforce members shall:\nUse agency resources (equipment, supplies, technology, time) only for legitimate agency business purposes.\nNever misappropriate, steal, or misuse agency property.\nReport waste, misuse, or misappropriation of agency resources through CO-CP-006.\n### 5.9 Social Media and Public Communications\nAll workforce members shall:\nNever post patient information, clinical photographs, or identifiable patient details on any social media platform.\nNever make public statements that misrepresent the agency's services, credentials, or compliance status.\nComply with policy IT-UP-003 for all social media and public communications.\n\n---",
