        title: "Non-Retaliation Enforcement",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Compliance Officer | Upon receipt of an allegation of retaliation, open a formal retaliation investigation within 5 calendar days, separate from any underlying compliance investigation. | Within 5 calendar days of allegation. |\n| 6.3.2 | Compliance Officer | Notify the Governing Body Chair in writing within 24 hours of receiving a retaliation allegation. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 6.3.3 | Compliance Officer | If the Compliance Officer is the subject of the retaliation allegation, the Governing Body Chair shall designate an independent investigator (may be external legal counsel or independent HR professional). | Within 5 calendar days of allegation. |\n| 6.3.4 | Compliance Officer / Investigator | Conduct retaliation investigation per CO-CP-007 standards. Interview the reporter, the alleged retaliator, and relevant witnesses. Document all findings. | Within 30 calendar days of initiation. |\n| 6.3.5 | Governing Body / Administrator | If retaliation is substantiated, impose disciplinary action per CO-CP-004 severity scale, up to and including immediate termination. Any substantiated retaliatory termination shall be subject to an offer of reinstatement with back pay. | Upon conclusion of investigation. |\n| 6.3.6 | Compliance Officer | Document investigation findings, disciplinary action, and corrective measures. Report to Governing Body at next quarterly meeting. | At meeting following investigation conclusion. |\n\n---",
