        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| 31 U.S.C. § 3730(h) | FCA anti-retaliation provision. |\n| California Labor Code § 1102.5 | California whistleblower protection statute. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Compliance with laws — includes whistleblower statutes. |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for HHAs | Non-retaliation is a required Program element. |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program. |\n| CO-CP-004 | Code of Conduct — disciplinary standards for retaliation. |\n| CO-CP-006 | Reporting mechanisms. |\n| CO-CP-007 | Investigation process. |\n| HR-ER-002 | Progressive discipline — applied to retaliatory conduct. |\n\n## Appendix A — Non-Retaliation Notice (for Posting)\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc.\n# YOUR RIGHTS AS A REPORTER — WHISTLEBLOWER PROTECTION NOTICE\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. is committed to full compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.\nYou have the right to report any suspected violation of law, regulation, or agency policy — including suspected fraud, waste, or abuse — without fear of retaliation.\nNo one at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. — including supervisors, managers, the Administrator, or the Governing Body — may retaliate against you for making a good-faith compliance report.\nRetaliation includes: termination, demotion, reduction in pay or hours, harassment, intimidation, or any other adverse action taken because of your report.\nHow to Make a Report:\nCompliance Officer: [Name & Contact — see agency directory]\nCompliance Hotline (Anonymous Available): [Number — see agency directory]\nGoverning Body Chair (for concerns about Compliance Officer or Administrator): [Contact — see agency directory]\nOIG Hotline (External): 1-800-HHS-TIPS (1-800-447-8477)\nYour identity will be protected to the maximum extent practicable.\nIf you experience retaliation for making a report, contact the Compliance Officer or Governing Body Chair immediately.\nThis notice is issued pursuant to Policy CO-CP-005 and the False Claims Act (31 U.S.C. § 3730(h)) and California Labor Code § 1102.5.\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | HCAI License No. 406412878\n## Appendix B — Workforce Non-Retaliation Rights Acknowledgment\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. Policy Reference: CO-CP-005 | Version: 1.0\nI acknowledge that I have been informed of my rights under Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc.'s Whistleblower Protection & Non-Retaliation Policy (CO-CP-005, Version 1.0) including:\nMy right to report suspected violations in good faith without fear of retaliation\nThe reporting mechanisms available to me\nThe prohibition on retaliation by any member of agency leadership or staff\nMy right to contact external regulatory authorities\n\n| Field | Entry |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Full Name (Printed) |  |\n| Title / Role |  |\n| Signature |  |\n| Date |  |\n| Type: | ☐ New Hire ☐ Annual Renewal |\n\n---",
