        title: "Report Receipt and Logging",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Compliance Officer (or designee) | Log every report received through any channel in the Compliance Report Log (Appendix A) within 1 business day of receipt. Assign a unique tracking number to each report. | Within 1 business day. |\n| 6.2.2 | Compliance Officer | Acknowledge receipt of non-anonymous reports within 5 business days. Anonymous hotline reports: no acknowledgment (to protect anonymity). | Within 5 business days. |\n| 6.2.3 | Compliance Officer | Conduct initial triage of the report to determine: (a) urgency (immediate patient safety risk vs. standard investigation); (b) whether interim protective action is required pending investigation; (c) referral to appropriate investigation process per CO-CP-007. | Within 5 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.2.4 | Compliance Officer | For reports involving immediate patient safety: notify the Administrator and Director of Nursing within 2 hours and initiate emergency response as required. | Within 2 hours of identification of immediate patient safety risk. |\n\n---",
