        title: "Shadow System Prevention",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | IT Director / CISO | Implement controls to detect and prevent shadow systems including: (a) USB port restrictions on agency devices; (b) cloud storage blocking (personal Dropbox, Google Drive, etc.); (c) periodic endpoint scans for PHI files outside approved systems; (d) DLP monitoring where feasible. | Continuous. |\n| 6.4.2 | All Workforce Members | Do not store, process, or transmit PHI using any system, device, account, or application not approved by the agency's IT and Compliance functions. This includes personal email, personal devices (unless enrolled in approved BYOD per IT-UP-001), personal cloud storage, and non-approved communication platforms. | Continuous. |\n| 6.4.3 | IT Director / CISO | Report all detected shadow systems to the Compliance Officer. Treat shadow system violations as security incidents per CO-IR-101. | Within 24 hours of detection. |\n\n---",
