        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Compliance Officer | Maintain and enforce the agency's FWA prevention program as an element of the Corporate Compliance Program per CO-CP-001. | Continuously. |\n| 6.1.2 | Compliance Officer | Ensure FWA training is included in orientation and annual compliance training per CO-CP-008. Training must include: (a) FWA definitions with home health-specific examples; (b) applicable laws (FCA, AKS, Stark); (c) detection red flags; (d) reporting mechanisms; (e) consequences; (f) whistleblower protections. | At hire; annually. |\n| 6.1.3 | All workforce members | Comply with all billing, documentation, and operational standards. Never participate in, conceal, or fail to report suspected FWA. | Continuously. |\n\n---",
