        id: "5-policy-statement",
        title: "4\\. Policy Statement",
        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 The agency shall maintain a HIPAA Privacy Program that protects all PHI in any form (oral, written, electronic).\n4.2 The Compliance Officer shall serve as the Privacy Officer (or designate a qualified individual).\n4.3 The agency shall maintain a current Notice of Privacy Practices (NPP) and provide it to all patients at the start of care.\n4.4 PHI shall be used and disclosed only as permitted by the HIPAA Privacy Rule, with the minimum necessary standard applied to all uses and disclosures.\n4.5 Patient rights under HIPAA shall be honored including: access, amendment, accounting of disclosures, restrictions, and confidential communications.\n4.6 All workforce members shall receive HIPAA privacy training at orientation and annually.\n\n---",
