        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1 | Compliance Officer | Maintain a BAA Registry (Appendix A) listing all business associates with BAA status. | Maintained continuously; reviewed annually. |\n| 6.2 | Compliance Officer | Ensure all new business associate relationships have an executed BAA before PHI disclosure. | Before PHI disclosure. |\n| 6.3 | Compliance Officer | Review all BAAs annually for compliance with current HIPAA requirements. | Annually. |\n| 6.4 | Compliance Officer | If a business associate breaches the BAA: (a) investigate per CO-CP-007; (b) cure the breach if feasible; (c) terminate the agreement if not cured; (d) report to HHS if necessary. | Per BAA terms; investigation within 7 days. |\n\n### Appendix A — Business Associate Agreement Registry\n\n| # | Business Associate Name | Service Provided | BAA Executed Date | BAA Expiration/Renewal | Contact Person | Last Review Date | Status | Notes |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  | ☐ Active ☐ Expired ☐ Terminated |  |\n\n### Appendix B — BAA Compliance Checklist\n\n| Required BAA Element (per 45 CFR § 164.504(e)(2)) | Present? |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Permitted and required uses/disclosures | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall not further use/disclose except as permitted | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall implement appropriate safeguards | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall report breaches to covered entity | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall ensure subcontractors agree to same restrictions | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall make PHI available to individuals per §164.524 | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall make PHI available for amendment per §164.526 | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall make information available for accounting per §164.528 | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall make practices available to HHS | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| BA shall return or destroy PHI upon termination | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| Termination provisions for material breach | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n\n### Appendix C — Policy Acknowledgment Form\n(Standard format)\n\n---",
