        id: "9-destruction-procedures",
        title: "Destruction Procedures",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Compliance Officer | Approve all record destruction. No records shall be destroyed without written Compliance Officer authorization. | Before destruction. |\n| 6.2.2 | Compliance Officer | Verify no litigation hold or investigation applies to records scheduled for destruction. | Before destruction. |\n| 6.2.3 | Designated staff | Destroy paper records containing PHI by cross-cut shredding. Destroy electronic records by secure wiping or physical destruction of media. | Per schedule. |\n| 6.2.4 | Compliance Officer | Maintain a Record Destruction Log (Appendix A) documenting: record type, date range, destruction method, destruction date, and authorizer. | Updated at each destruction event; log retained permanently. |\n\n### Appendix A — Record Destruction Log\n\n| # | Record Type | Date Range of Records | Destruction Method | Destruction Date | Authorized By | Witness | Litigation Hold Verified Clear? |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| RD-2025-001 |  | From: ___ To: ___ | ☐ Cross-cut shred ☐ Secure wipe ☐ Physical destruction |  |  |  | ☐ Yes |\n\n### Appendix B — Record Retention Quick Reference Card\n(Wallet-sized reference card for distribution to department heads summarizing retention periods by record type)\n### Appendix C — Policy Acknowledgment Form\n(Standard format)\n\n---",
