        title: "Privacy Program Governance",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Governing Body | Designate or confirm the designation of a Privacy Officer with documented authority to develop, implement, and enforce the agency's privacy program. | Prior to agency operation; confirmed annually at the first quarterly meeting. |\n| 6.1.2 | Privacy Officer | Maintain a current, written privacy program document that addresses all HIPAA Privacy Rule requirements, CMIA requirements, and 42 CFR Part 2 requirements applicable to the agency. | Continuous; reviewed and updated annually or upon regulatory change. |\n| 6.1.3 | Privacy Officer | Conduct an annual privacy risk assessment evaluating: (a) adequacy of current privacy policies; (b) workforce training compliance; (c) incident/complaint trends; (d) regulatory changes; (e) adequacy of safeguards for sensitive data categories. | Annually; completed within 90 calendar days of the start of each fiscal year. |\n| 6.1.4 | Privacy Officer | Report privacy program status to the Compliance Officer quarterly and to the Governing Body per CO-CP-002 and GV-GB-001 reporting requirements. Report shall include: (a) privacy incidents; (b) complaint status; (c) training rates; (d) regulatory changes; (e) audit findings. | Quarterly. |\n\n---",
