        title: "Patient Rights Fulfillment",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "#### 6.3.1 Right to Access\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1.1 | Patient | Submit a written request to access PHI using the agency's Access Request Form or in any written format identifying the patient and the information requested. | N/A (patient-initiated). |\n| 6.3.1.2 | Privacy Officer / Health Information Designee | Log the request in the Patient Rights Request Tracker with: (a) date received; (b) patient name; (c) information requested; (d) response deadline. | Within 2 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.3.1.3 | Privacy Officer / Health Information Designee | Verify identity of the requestor per agency identity verification procedures. If the request is submitted by a personal representative, verify authority per 45 CFR § 164.502(g). | Within 5 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.3.1.4 | Privacy Officer / Health Information Designee | Provide the requested information in the form and format requested by the patient, if readily producible. If not readily producible, provide in hard copy or other mutually agreed format. Fees, if any, shall not exceed the cost of labor for copying, supplies, and postage, per 45 CFR § 164.524(c)(4). Under CMIA, the first copy must be provided at no charge. | Within 30 calendar days of receipt; one 30-day extension permitted with written notice to patient stating the reason and expected completion date. |\n| 6.3.1.5 | Privacy Officer | If access is denied in whole or in part (only grounds permitted under 45 CFR § 164.524(a)(2)–(3)), provide the patient with a written denial that includes: (a) the basis for denial; (b) a statement of the patient's right to have the denial reviewed; (c) the process for requesting review; (d) complaint filing instructions. | Within the 30-day response period. |\n\n#### 6.3.2 Right to Amendment\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.2.1 | Patient | Submit a written request to amend PHI including the reason for the requested amendment. | N/A (patient-initiated). |\n| 6.3.2.2 | Privacy Officer | Log the request and review the amendment request in consultation with the clinician(s) responsible for the relevant record entries. | Within 10 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.3.2.3 | Privacy Officer | Grant or deny the amendment. If granted: append the amendment to the record and notify the patient and any persons/entities the patient identifies who received the original information. If denied (only grounds permitted under 45 CFR § 164.526(a)(2)): provide written denial including: (a) basis; (b) right to submit a statement of disagreement; (c) process for complaint. | Within 60 calendar days; one 30-day extension permitted with written notice. |\n\n#### 6.3.3 Right to Accounting of Disclosures\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.3.1 | All Workforce Members | Document all disclosures of PHI that are not for TPO, not authorized by the patient, and not otherwise excluded under 45 CFR § 164.528(a) in the Disclosure Log. Documentation must include: (a) date of disclosure; (b) name and address of recipient; (c) brief description of PHI disclosed; (d) purpose of disclosure or copy of request. | At the time of each qualifying disclosure. |\n| 6.3.3.2 | Privacy Officer | Upon receipt of a patient request for accounting of disclosures, compile the accounting from the Disclosure Log for the period requested (up to 6 years prior to the date of request). | Within 60 calendar days; one 30-day extension permitted with written notice. First accounting in any 12-month period is provided at no charge. |\n\n#### 6.3.4 Right to Request Restrictions and Confidential Communications\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.4.1 | Privacy Officer | Evaluate all patient requests to restrict uses or disclosures. The agency is not required to agree to a restriction, except that the agency must agree to restrict disclosure to a health plan if: (a) the disclosure is for payment or health care operations; (b) the PHI pertains solely to a service for which the patient has paid in full out of pocket (45 CFR § 164.522(a)(1)(vi)). | Within 10 business days of receipt. |\n| 6.3.4.2 | Privacy Officer | Document all agreed-upon restrictions in the patient's record and communicate the restriction to all workforce members with access to the record. Ensure EHR system flags are applied if technically feasible. | Within 5 business days of agreeing to the restriction. |\n| 6.3.4.3 | Privacy Officer | Honor all reasonable requests for confidential communications (e.g., alternative address or phone number for receiving communications). | Upon receipt; implemented within 5 business days. |\n\n---",
