        body: "| Failure Point | Risk | Mitigation |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Audit work plan exists but no audits are actually conducted. | OIG and CMS treat a non-functional audit program as equivalent to no program. | Compliance Officer must demonstrate active audit operations through documented Audit Initiation Notices, Findings Worksheets, and Reports. |\n| Audit sample sizes are too small to support conclusions. | Findings may be unreliable; surveyors may cite inadequate monitoring. | Use minimum sample sizes defined in Section 6.3 consistently. |\n| Findings are identified but no CAP is developed. | Undiscovered or unaddressed deficiencies constitute knowing non-compliance. | Mandatory 14-day CAP development for all High and Moderate findings; Compliance Committee tracks at each meeting. |\n| Re-audits are not conducted to validate CAP effectiveness. | Agency cannot demonstrate that corrective action was effective. | 90-day re-audit requirement with documented comparison to baseline. |\n\n---",
