        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Administrator | Upon receipt of survey findings (Statement of Deficiencies / Form CMS-2567): notify the Governing Body Chair and Compliance Officer within 24 hours. Convene an emergency leadership meeting within 48 hours. | Within 24 hours of receipt; meeting within 48 hours. |\n| 6.4.2 | Compliance Officer | Analyze each cited deficiency. Classify as: (a) Condition-level; (b) Standard-level; (c) Immediate Jeopardy. Determine root cause for each finding. | Within 5 calendar days of receipt. |\n| 6.4.3 | Compliance Officer / Administrator | Develop the Plan of Correction (POC) per CMS requirements. Each POC element must include: (a) what corrective action will be accomplished; (b) how the agency will identify other residents/patients with the same deficiency; (c) what systemic changes will be implemented; (d) how the agency will monitor effectiveness; (e) completion date. | Within CMS-required timeframe (typically 10 calendar days). |\n| 6.4.4 | Governing Body | Review and approve the POC at a special or regular meeting. Document review and approval in meeting minutes. | Before POC submission to CMS. |\n| 6.4.5 | Compliance Officer | Monitor POC implementation. Conduct focused re-audit of corrected areas within 60 calendar days to validate effectiveness. Report to Governing Body. | Re-audit within 60 days; report to Governing Body at next meeting. |\n| 6.4.6 | Compliance Officer | If Immediate Jeopardy is cited: implement immediate corrective measures to remove the jeopardy within the CMS-required timeframe (typically 23 calendar days). Notify Governing Body within 24 hours. Engage legal counsel. | Per CMS IJ timeline. |\n\n---",
