        body: "Per EN-LC-001 standards. Only the most current approved version is valid. Substantive revision requires Governing Body approval and re-acknowledgment within 14 calendar days.\n### Appendix A — Survey Readiness Binder Monthly Verification Checklist\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | Policy Reference: CO-RA-003 | Version: 1.0\nInstructions: Complete monthly. Verify each item is current and accessible. Report any gaps to the Compliance Officer within 5 business days.\n| Month/Year: _______________ | Verified By: _______________ | Date: _______________ |\n\n| # | Binder Item | Current? | Location Verified | Notes / Gap Identified | Corrected By (Date) |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1 | California HCAI License (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 2 | Medicare Certification (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 3 | Governing Body Roster (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 4 | Governing Body Minutes (last 12 months) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 5 | Organizational Chart (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 6 | Scope of Services (current, approved) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 7 | QAPI Plan (current, approved) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 8 | QAPI Committee Minutes (last 12 months) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 9 | Compliance Program Description | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 10 | Compliance Committee Minutes (last 12 months) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 11 | Emergency Preparedness Plan (current, approved) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 12 | Infection Control Plan (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 13 | Patient Rights Notice (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 14 | Advance Directive Policy (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 15 | Employee Roster with License Verification Dates | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 16 | OIG/SAM Screening Log (last 12 months) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 17 | Policy Index with Review Dates | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 18 | Training Completion Summary (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n| 19 | Last Survey Results / POC (if applicable) | ☐ Yes ☐ No ☐ N/A |  |  |  |\n| 20 | Conflict of Interest Disclosures (current) | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |  |  |\n\nTotal Items Current: _____ / 20 Gaps Identified: _____ All Gaps Resolved? ☐ Yes ☐ No\nCoordinator Signature: ________________________________ Date: _______________\n### Appendix B — Mock Survey Findings Report\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | Policy Reference: CO-RA-003 | Version: 1.0 | CONFIDENTIAL\n\n| Field | Entry |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Mock Survey Type | ☐ Comprehensive (Annual) ☐ Focused (Quarterly) |\n| Mock Survey Date(s) |  |\n| Focus Area(s) |  |\n| Conducted By | ☐ Internal Team ☐ External Consultant — Name/Firm: _______________ |\n| Survey Protocol Used | ☐ CMS SOM Appendix B ☐ State Licensure Protocol ☐ Other: _______________ |\n| Report Prepared By |  |\n| Report Date |  |\n\nFINDINGS:\n\n| Finding # | CMS Tag / Regulation | Condition / Standard | Finding Description | Severity (Condition / Standard / Low) | Comparable Real Survey Risk | CAP Required? |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1 |  |  |  |  | ☐ High ☐ Moderate ☐ Low | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 2 |  |  |  |  | ☐ High ☐ Moderate ☐ Low | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 3 |  |  |  |  | ☐ High ☐ Moderate ☐ Low | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 4 |  |  |  |  | ☐ High ☐ Moderate ☐ Low | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n| 5 |  |  |  |  | ☐ High ☐ Moderate ☐ Low | ☐ Yes ☐ No |\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n| Metric | Count |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Total Findings |  |\n| Condition-Level Equivalent |  |\n| Standard-Level Equivalent |  |\n| Low-Level |  |\n| CAPs Required |  |\n\nSTRENGTHS IDENTIFIED: _______________\nRECOMMENDATIONS: _______________\nCompliance Officer Signature: ________________________________ Date: _______________\n### Appendix C — Survey Interaction Guidelines for Staff\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | Policy Reference: CO-RA-003 | Version: 1.0\nDISTRIBUTE TO ALL WORKFORCE MEMBERS\nWHAT TO DO WHEN A SURVEYOR ARRIVES:\nStep 1 — Greet and Verify\nGreet the surveyor professionally.\nRequest official identification and badge.\nNote the surveyor's name and agency (CMS, State, accreditation body).\nStep 2 — Notify Immediately\nNotify the Administrator AND Compliance Officer immediately — by phone, not email.\nIf neither is available, notify the designated alternate per the agency's chain of command.\nDo NOT delay notification for any reason.\nStep 3 — Provide Access\nProvide the surveyor access to any area they request.\nDo NOT block, delay, or restrict surveyor access to any part of the agency or any patient record.\nDURING THE SURVEY — YOUR INTERVIEW:\n\n| DO | DO NOT |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Be polite, calm, and professional at all times. | Do NOT argue with the surveyor. |\n| Answer only the question that was asked — directly and honestly. | Do NOT volunteer extra information beyond the question. |\n| Say \"I don't know\" if you genuinely do not know. Offer to find the answer. | Do NOT guess or speculate. |\n| Provide only the specific document requested. | Do NOT provide documents that were not requested. |\n| Speak only about your own role and responsibilities. | Do NOT speak about others' responsibilities or areas outside your expertise. |\n| If you are unsure, ask the surveyor to clarify the question. | Do NOT make excuses or blame others. |\n| Document the questions you were asked as soon as the interview ends. | Do NOT alter, destroy, or hide any document during a survey. |\n\nAFTER THE SURVEY:\nDocument any questions you were asked and your responses.\nReport to the Administrator or Compliance Officer immediately.\nDo NOT discuss survey findings or speculate about results with patients or external parties.\nREMEMBER: Surveyors are not adversaries. They are ensuring patient safety. Your honest, calm, and professional cooperation is the best survey response.\nQuestions? Contact the Compliance Officer: [Contact per agency directory]\n### Appendix D — External Audit Log\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | Policy Reference: CO-RA-003 | Version: 1.0 | CONFIDENTIAL\n\n| Tracking # | Date Received | Requesting Entity | Audit Type | Records / Information Requested | Response Deadline | Response Coordinator | Date Response Submitted | Outcome | Appeal Filed? | Notes |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| EA-2025-001 |  | ☐ MAC ☐ ZPIC/UPIC ☐ OIG ☐ RAC ☐ State ☐ Other: | ☐ ADR ☐ Medical Record ☐ Pre-Payment ☐ Post-Payment ☐ Other: |  |  |  |  | ☐ Favorable ☐ Unfavorable ☐ Partial ☐ Pending | ☐ Yes ☐ No |  |\n\n(Rows continue as needed)\nQuarterly Summary:\n\n| Quarter | Total Audit Requests | Responded On Time | Favorable Outcomes | Appeals Filed | Overpayment Demands |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $ _______________ |\n\n### Appendix E — Policy Acknowledgment Form\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. | Policy Reference: CO-RA-003 | Version: 1.0 | Effective: 2025-07-10\nI, the undersigned, acknowledge that:\nI have received and read Policy CO-RA-003 — External Audit & Survey Readiness, Version 1.0, effective 2025-07-10.\nI understand the survey interaction protocols and my responsibilities during external surveys.\nI understand that I am accountable for complying with this policy and that non-compliance may result in corrective action.\nI have had the opportunity to ask questions and receive clarification.\n\n| Field | Entry |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Full Name (Printed) |  |\n| Title / Role |  |\n| Department |  |\n| Signature |  |\n| Date Signed |  |\n| Type: | ☐ New Hire ☐ Annual Renewal ☐ Policy Revision |\n\n---",
