        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Compliance Officer | Conduct a comprehensive annual CoP compliance assessment using the Annual CoP Assessment Checklist (Appendix B). The assessment must evaluate compliance with each Condition and Standard by reviewing: (a) current implementing policies and their review dates; (b) operational evidence of compliance; (c) training records; (d) audit findings related to each Condition; (e) prior survey findings. | Annually; completed by end of Q1. |\n| 6.2.2 | Compliance Officer | Classify each Condition as: (a) Compliant — documented evidence supports full compliance; (b) Partially Compliant — one or more Standards not fully met; (c) Non-Compliant — Condition not met. | During assessment. |\n| 6.2.3 | Compliance Officer | For any Condition classified as Partially Compliant or Non-Compliant: develop corrective action per QA-AE-003 within 14 calendar days. | Within 14 calendar days of assessment completion. |\n| 6.2.4 | Compliance Officer | Present the annual CoP assessment to the Governing Body at the Q1 quarterly meeting with findings, compliance status by Condition, and corrective action plans. | Q1 Governing Body meeting. |\n\n---",
