        title: "2\\. Purpose",
        level: 2,
        order: 3,
        body: "This policy establishes the rules governing the complete lifecycle of every policy document at Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc., from inception through active use, revision, and final archival or sunset. Effective lifecycle control ensures:\n\n- Only currently approved policy versions are in active use — never expired or superseded versions\n- All policy reviews are completed on schedule, meeting CMS, OIG, and California regulatory expectations for maintained, current policies\n- Version control prevents reliance on outdated procedures that may not reflect current regulatory requirements\n- The agency can demonstrate to CMS surveyors, OIG reviewers, CDPH/HCAI inspectors, and accreditation bodies that every policy in its library is current, approved, and has a documented review history\n- The policy approval process is appropriately controlled with required executive oversight per GV-PM-001\n\nThis policy is the lifecycle management companion to EN-TG-001 (Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance). The taxonomy defines what a policy IS; this policy defines how a policy moves through its stages of existence.\n\n---\n\n---",
