        title: "4\\. Definitions",
        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Lifecycle | The complete arc of a policy document: Creation → Draft → Review → Approval → Active → Scheduled Review → Revision or Reaffirmation → Active (updated) → [Sunset Pending] → Archived. |\n| Draft | The initial or revised state of a policy that has not yet been approved. Draft documents shall not be distributed to staff as authoritative guidance. |\n| Active | A policy that has been formally approved by the appropriate authority, assigned an effective date, and published for staff use. Only Active policies are operative. |\n| Reaffirmation | The formal documentation that a policy has been reviewed on schedule and no changes are required. The policy retains its Policy ID and increments its version number by 0.1 (e.g., v1.0 → v1.1 after reaffirmation). |\n| Revision | A change to any substantive element of a policy through the full review and approval process. Revisions increment the version number by a full integer (e.g., v1.0 → v2.0 for significant changes) or 0.1 for minor corrections. |\n| Sunset | The intentional termination of a policy, with full documentation of the reason, regulatory basis for termination, and handling of any downstream cross-references. A sunset policy is moved to Archived status. |\n| Review Cycle | The maximum interval between scheduled reviews of a policy, based on its Tier and regulatory requirements: REQUIRED-tier policies — Annual; ESSENTIAL-tier — Annual or Biennial; RECOMMENDED-tier — Biennial; GOOD TO HAVE-tier — Triennial. |\n| Triggered Review | An out-of-cycle review initiated by: regulatory change, survey finding, incident, significant process change, or Compliance Officer determination. |\n| Version History | A permanent record of every version of a policy — the document text at each version, the date, approver, and nature of changes. Retained permanently. |\n| Controlled Distribution | The management of which staff receive policy notifications and acknowledgments, and the tracking of policy distribution to ensure no staff member is working with an superseded version. |\n\n---\n\n---",
