        id: "5-policy-statement",
        title: "5\\. Policy Statement",
        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "5.1 Every policy of Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. must be actively maintained through a documented lifecycle. No policy shall remain Active without a completed scheduled review at the interval defined by its Review Cycle.\n\n5.2 Only Active-status policies shall be distributed to staff or referenced as current agency policy. Draft policies are for internal development use only. Archived policies are permanently inaccessible to staff except for historical audit reference.\n\n5.3 All policy revisions must be approved by the appropriate authority per GV-PM-001 (Policy Development & Approval Process) before the revised version becomes Active. The prior version does not expire until the revised version's effective date.\n\n5.4 The effective date of a revised policy shall not precede the approval date. Retroactive policy effective dates are prohibited.\n\n5.5 When a policy is revised or reaffirmed, the prior version is immediately retired to Archived status. The system shall not permit access to a prior version as if it were current.\n\n5.6 Every revision of every policy shall be accompanied by a complete version history entry identifying the nature of changes, the person who approved the revision, and the date.\n\n5.7 Policies overdue for review shall be flagged in the Policy Registry and reported in the monthly summary per EN-TG-001 Section 6.5.2. A REQUIRED-tier policy overdue by more than 60 calendar days beyond its scheduled review date is elevated to a compliance risk requiring Administrator notification.\n\n5.8 This policy itself, as a REQUIRED-tier Enterprise Control policy, shall be reviewed and reaffirmed or revised annually.\n\n---\n\n---",
