        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.6.1 | Compliance Officer or Domain Steward | Initiate a sunset action when: (a) the regulatory basis for a REQUIRED-tier policy is eliminated; (b) the policy is redundant due to consolidation into another policy; (c) the policy covers a service or function the agency has formally discontinued. Document the sunset rationale in the Sunset Request Form (Appendix D). | At identification; submit form to Compliance Officer. |\n| 6.6.2 | Compliance Officer | Review the sunset request: (a) verify no active regulatory requirement still mandates the policy; (b) verify all cross-references to the policy are updated or will be updated to remove the reference; (c) verify no downstream controlled documents (checklists, job aids) depend solely on the sunsetted policy. | Within 14 calendar days of receiving sunset request. |\n| 6.6.3 | Administrator | Approve the sunset action. The Governing Body shall be notified at the next scheduled meeting for any REQUIRED-tier policy sunset. | Administrator approval within 14 days; Governing Body notification at next meeting. |\n| 6.6.4 | Compliance Officer | Upon approval of sunset: (a) remove the Active policy from staff access; (b) update Policy Registry status to \"Archived\"; (c) retain the archived policy (all versions) permanently in the policy archive; (d) update any other policies that cross-reference the sunsetted policy within 30 days. | Within 3 business days of approval; cross-reference updates within 30 days. |\n\n---",
