        body: "CMS surveyors and OIG reviewers will specifically assess:\n\n1. Whether the agency's policies are current — they will request the most recent version of key policies and compare effective dates and version numbers against internal records. A policy unchanged for 5+ years without a reaffirmation memo is suspect.\n2. Whether the agency has a documented process for identifying when policies need revision — co-RA-001 regulatory monitoring tied to policy lifecycle triggers is essential.\n3. Whether a superseded version of a policy was in use at the time of a care episode in question. This is critical in deficiency investigations where surveyors ask \"what was your policy at the time?\"\n4. Whether significant changes (like a new regulation) were promptly incorporated into policy documents.\n5. Whether staff were notified of policy changes (acknowledgment records per GV-PM-003).\n\n---",
