        title: "Policy ID Assignment",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Policy Drafter / Domain Steward | Before drafting a new policy, submit a Policy ID Request Form (Appendix B) to the Compliance Officer specifying: (a) proposed domain; (b) proposed subdomain (existing or new); (c) brief description of the policy scope; (d) intended Tier classification. | Before commencing policy draft. |\n| 6.1.2 | Compliance Officer | Review the Policy ID Request Form: (a) confirm the proposed domain and subdomain are consistent with the taxonomy; (b) verify no existing policy already covers the proposed scope (duplication check against the Policy Registry); (c) if a new subdomain is required, create the subdomain record in the Registry and assign the next available 3-digit sequence number within that subdomain; (d) assign and return the Policy ID in writing. | Within 5 business days of receiving the request form. |\n| 6.1.3 | Compliance Officer | Record the new Policy ID assignment in the Policy Registry (Appendix A) with status \"Draft\" and the date of assignment, before the policy document is complete. | At assignment. |\n| 6.1.4 | Compliance Officer | Reserve retired Policy IDs permanently in the Registry with status \"Archived\" or \"Sunset.\" Do not reassign any retired Policy ID to a new policy. | Continuous. |\n\n---",
