        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "CMS surveyors and OIG reviewers will specifically verify:\n\n1. That the agency can produce a complete inventory of its policies (equivalent to the Policy Registry) demonstrating that it knows what policies it has and their status.\n2. That policies referenced in a survey finding are identifiable by unique identifier and version, allowing precise determination of what was in effect at the time of a care episode.\n3. That cross-references between policies are consistent and use specific policy identifiers — not vague references like \"per our privacy policy.\"\n4. That the Governing Body receives reports on the state of the policy library, confirming oversight per GV-GB-001.\n5. That REQUIRED-tier policies have a documented regulatory basis — surveyors may ask \"what requires you to have this policy?\"\n\n---",
