        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR Part 424 | Conditions for Medicare Payment | Primary regulatory basis for Medicare payment requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 424.22 | Requirements for Home Health Services | Physician certification, plan of care, face-to-face requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 484.50 | Condition of Participation: Patient rights | Patient notification of billing rights |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with Federal, State, and local laws | Agency must comply with all applicable billing and payment laws |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration | Governing Body oversight of fiscal operations |\n| 45 CFR Parts 160, 162 | HIPAA Administrative Simplification — Electronic Transactions | 837I claim format, 835 remittance, 277 status inquiry |\n| 31 U.S.C. §§ 3729–3733 | False Claims Act | Liability for false or fraudulent Medicare claims |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7k(d) | 60-Day Overpayment Rule (ACA) | Obligation to identify and return overpayments within 60 days |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7b | Anti-Kickback Statute | Prohibition on billing for services induced by kickbacks |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Source | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS IOM Publication 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual, Chapter 10 (Home Health Agency Billing) | Detailed instructions for home health billing including claim form completion, billing codes, and submission requirements |\n| CMS IOM Publication 100-02, Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter 7 (Home Health Services) | Coverage criteria, medical necessity, homebound status |\n| CMS MLN Fact Sheets — Home Health PPS / PDGM | Education materials on PDGM classification and payment |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B | Survey guidance for 42 CFR § 484.100 compliance with federal laws |\n\n### 9.3 OIG Guidance\n\n| Source | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies (63 FR 42410) | Establishes expectation that billing processes include pre-submission review, coding accuracy controls, and compliance program integration |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| FN-BC-002 | Claims Denial Management & Appeals | Denied claims routed to denial management process |\n| FN-BC-003 | Patient Billing & Financial Responsibility | Patient financial obligations and ABN process |\n| FN-BC-004 | Overpayment Identification & Refund | Overpayments identified through billing reconciliation |\n| FN-BC-005 | Pre-Claim Review Compliance | PCR submission when required by CMS |\n| FN-BC-006 | RAP / NOA Management | NOA submission required before final claim |\n| FN-BC-007 | Payment & Reimbursement Reconciliation | Post-payment reconciliation process |\n| FN-CM-001 | PDGM Classification & Coding Accuracy | PDGM classification verification required before claim |\n| FN-CM-002 | ICD-10 Coding Standards & Accuracy | Diagnosis code accuracy requirements |\n| FN-CM-003 | Medical Necessity Documentation | Documentation supporting medical necessity for billed services |\n| FN-CM-004 | Episode Management & Authorization | Episode tracking and certification management |\n| FN-CM-005 | LUPA Prevention & Monitoring | LUPA threshold verification before final claim |\n| CL-CA-005 | Homebound Status Determination & Documentation | Homebound documentation supporting billing |\n| CL-CA-006 | Face-to-Face Encounter Compliance | F2F requirement for billing |\n| CL-CA-007 | Face-to-Face Encounter Tracking | F2F tracking and expiration monitoring |\n| CL-CD-001 | Clinical Documentation Standards | Documentation standards supporting claim validity |\n| CL-CD-004 | Timely Documentation Completion & Lock | Documentation lock requirements before billing |\n| CL-CP-008 | Physician Recertification Timing Compliance | Physician certification timing for billing |\n| CL-CP-009 | Physician Order Signature Tracking | Signature tracking supporting claim requirements |\n| CL-SD-024 | Missed Visit & Rescheduling | Missed visit documentation affecting billing |\n| CL-SD-025 | Ordered Visit Frequency Compliance | Visit frequency compliance affecting claim validity |\n| CL-OA-001 | OASIS Completion Timeliness | OASIS timeliness required for claim submission |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | Compliance program overseeing billing integrity |\n| CO-CP-005 | Whistleblower Protection & Non-Retaliation | Protections for reporting billing concerns |\n| CO-CP-006 | Compliance Hotline & Reporting Mechanisms | Mechanism for reporting billing concerns |\n| CO-CP-007 | Compliance Investigation Process | Investigation of billing integrity concerns |\n| CO-CP-008 | Compliance Training & Education | Training requirements for billing personnel |\n| CO-DC-002 | Documentation Audit & Monitoring Program | Documentation audits supporting billing accuracy |\n| CO-DC-004 | Clinical, Documentation, and Billing Alignment Audit | Triangulation audit of orders/documentation/billing |\n| CO-FA-001 | Anti-Kickback & Stark Law Compliance | Anti-kickback controls affecting billing relationships |\n| CO-FA-002 | False Claims Act Awareness & Prevention | False Claims Act education for billing staff |\n| CO-FA-003 | Fraud, Waste & Abuse Prevention | FWA prevention integrated with billing |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Retention standards for billing records |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body financial oversight of billing |\n| QA-PI-006 | Visit Utilization & LUPA Risk Management | QAPI integration with billing patterns |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified |\n\n---",
