        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR Part 405, Subpart I | Federal Health Insurance Benefit — Medicare Appeals Process | Complete Medicare administrative appeals framework (5 levels) |\n| 42 CFR § 405.940–405.958 | Redetermination | Level 1 appeal requirements__ |\n| 42 CFR § 405.960–405.978 | Reconsideration | Level 2 appeal requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 405.1000–405.1064 | ALJ Hearing | Level 3 appeal requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 405.1100–405.1140 | Medicare Appeals Council | Level 4 appeal requirements |\n| 42 CFR § 405.1136 | Judicial Review | Level 5 — federal court |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with laws | Agency billing compliance obligation__ |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration | Governing Body financial oversight |\n| 31 U.S.C. §§ 3729–3733 | False Claims Act | Liability for patterns of improper billing |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7k(d__ | 60-Day Rule | Overpayment identification from denial patterns__ |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Source | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS IOM Publication 100-04 (Claims Processing__ | Claims submission and denial handling guidance |\n| CMS IOM Publication 100-20 (Appeals__ | Medicare appeals process manual |\n| CMS MLN Fact Sheet — Medicare Appeals Process | Education reference for appeal levels and deadlines |\n\n### 9.3 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| FN-BC-001 | Medicare Billing & Claims Submission | Claims submission standards; denials originate from submitted claims |\n| FN-BC-004 | Overpayment Identification & Refund | Denial patterns may reveal overpayments requiring 60-day refund |\n| FN-BC-007 | Payment & Reimbursement Reconciliation | Payment variances may indicate denial issues |\n| FN-CM-001 | PDGM Classification & Coding Accuracy | Coding denials routed to coding accuracy review |\n| FN-CM-002 | ICD-10 Coding Standards & Accuracy | ICD-10 coding errors as denial source |\n| FN-CM-003 | Medical Necessity Documentation | Documentation supporting medical necessity appeals__ |\n| FN-FP-003 | Revenue Cycle Performance Monitoring | Denial rate as KPI |\n| FN-FP-007 | Financial Compliance & Fraud Monitoring | Denial patterns as fraud indicators |\n| CL-CA-005 | Homebound Status Determination | Homebound documentation for appeal support__ |\n| CL-CA-006 | Face-to-Face Encounter Compliance | F2F documentation for appeal support |\n| CL-CD-001 | Clinical Documentation Standards | Documentation standards supporting appeals |\n| CO-CP-007 | Compliance Investigation Process | Investigation of systemic denial patterns |\n| CO-DC-002 | Documentation Audit & Monitoring | Audit findings correlating with denials |\n| CO-DC-004 | Clinical/Documentation/Billing Alignment Audit | Triangulation audit revealing denial root causes |\n| CO-FA-003 | Fraud, Waste & Abuse Prevention | FWA investigation from denial patterns |\n| QA-AE-002 | Root Cause Analysis Process | RCA methodology for denial trending__ |\n| QA-AE-003 | Corrective Action Plan Development | CAP process for denial corrective actions |\n| QA-PI-002 | Quality Indicator Monitoring | Denial trending as quality indicator |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Quarterly financial/compliance reporting to GB |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy | Framework classification |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "module",
