        title: "Patient Billing Statements",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Generate monthly billing statements for all patients with an open balance. Statements shall include: (a) patient name and account number; (b) date(s) of service; (c) description of each service; (d) charge for each service; (e) insurance payments applied; (f) adjustments applied; (g) patient balance due; (h) payment due date; (i) accepted payment methods; (j) agency billing inquiry contact name, phone number, and hours of availability. | Billing Coordinator | Monthly — generated within 30 days of service or balance activity |\n| 6.4.2 | Deliver statements by mail or, with documented patient consent, by secure electronic delivery. | Billing Coordinator | Within 5 business days of generation |\n| 6.4.3 | Respond to all patient billing inquiries within 3 business days of receipt. Document the inquiry, the response, and the resolution. | Billing Coordinator | Within 3 business days |\n| 6.4.4 | If a patient requests an itemized statement, provide it within 10 business days. | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 10 business days of request |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
