        id: "12-billing-disputes",
        title: "Billing Disputes",
        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Upon receipt of a patient billing complaint or dispute (verbal or written), log the dispute in the Patient Billing Dispute Log (Appendix C) and acknowledge receipt to the patient within 2 business days. | Billing Coordinator | Log immediately; acknowledge within 2 business days |\n| 6.5.2 | Investigate the dispute — review the claim, documentation, remittance, and patient account. | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 10 calendar days of receipt |\n| 6.5.3 | Resolve the dispute and communicate the resolution to the patient in writing within 14 calendar days of receipt. If the balance is adjusted, update the patient account. | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 14 calendar days |\n| 6.5.4 | If the patient is not satisfied with the resolution, inform them of their right to file a grievance per OP-PA-001 and their right to contact Medicare (1-800-MEDICARE) or the QIO. | Revenue Cycle Director | At time of resolution communication |\n| 6.5.5 | No collection activity shall be initiated or continued while a billing dispute is pending. | Revenue Cycle Director | Ongoing |\n\n---",
