        title: "Patient Collection Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 13,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.6.1 | Patient collection shall follow this defined sequence: |  |  |\n|  | 30 days: First billing statement (per §6.4.1) | Billing Coordinator | At 30 days from service |\n|  | 60 days: Second billing statement with \"Past Due\" notation and payment request letter | Billing Coordinator | At 60 days |\n|  | 90 days: Final notice — written notification that the balance will be referred for collection if not paid or payment arrangement made within 30 days. | Revenue Cycle Director | At 90 days |\n|  | 120 days: Collection referral (if balance unresolved, no dispute pending, no charity care application pending) | Revenue Cycle Director + CFO authorization | At 120 days |\n| 6.6.2 | Before any collection referral, verify that: (a) no billing dispute is pending; (b) no charity care application is under review per FN-FP-004; (c) no Medicare appeal is open that could affect patient liability; (d) all billing statements were sent to the patient's current address. | Revenue Cycle Director | Before referral |\n| 6.6.3 | Collection referral requires written authorization from the Revenue Cycle Director and CFO using the Collection Referral Authorization Form (Appendix D). | Revenue Cycle Director + CFO | Before referral |\n| 6.6.4 | Any external collection agency used by the agency shall comply with: (a) FDCPA requirements; (b) California debt collection laws; (c) HIPAA minimum necessary standard (limited to information necessary for collection). The agency shall maintain a current Business Associate Agreement with any collection agency per CO-HP-005. | Revenue Cycle Director / Compliance Officer | Before engagement and ongoing |\n| 6.6.5 | Patient balances of $25 or less shall not be referred to external collection. Balances under $25 after 120 days shall be written off as small balance adjustments with Revenue Cycle Director approval. | Revenue Cycle Director | At 120 days |\n\n---",
