        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7k(d) | Reporting and Returning of Overpayments | Primary statutory basis — 60-day rule |\n| 42 CFR § 401.305 | Requirements for Reporting and Returning of Overpayments | Implementing regulation — definitions, deadlines, lookback period |\n| 31 U.S.C. §§ 3729–3733 | False Claims Act | Reverse false claim liability for retained overpayments |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7b | Anti-Kickback Statute | Overpayments resulting from kickback arrangements |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1395nn | Physician Self-Referral (Stark Law) | Overpayments resulting from Stark violations |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with laws | Agency obligation to comply with overpayment rules |\n\n### 9.2 CMS and OIG Guidance\n\n| Source | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS Final Rule: Reporting and Returning of Overpayments (81 FR 7654, February 12, 2016) | Establishes the 60-day rule implementing regulations, reasonable diligence standard, and 6-year lookback |\n| OIG Self-Disclosure Protocol (Updated 2013) | Process for voluntary disclosure of fraud-related overpayments |\n| CMS Self-Referral Disclosure Protocol | Process for voluntary disclosure of Stark Law violations |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies | Expectation for overpayment identification and refund processes |\n\n### 9.3 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| FN-BC-001 | Medicare Billing & Claims Submission | Billing accuracy prevents overpayments |\n| FN-BC-002 | Claims Denial Management & Appeals | Denial patterns revealing overpayments |\n| FN-BC-007 | Payment & Reimbursement Reconciliation | Monthly reconciliation identifying payment anomalies |\n| FN-CM-001 | PDGM Classification & Coding Accuracy | Coding errors causing overpayments |\n| FN-CM-002 | ICD-10 Coding Standards & Accuracy | Coding accuracy preventing overpayments |\n| FN-FP-007 | Financial Compliance & Fraud Monitoring | Billing pattern analysis identifying overpayments |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | Compliance program overseeing overpayment processes |\n| CO-CP-005 | Whistleblower Protection & Non-Retaliation | Protection for staff reporting overpayments |\n| CO-CP-006 | Compliance Hotline & Reporting Mechanisms | Reporting channel for overpayment concerns |\n| CO-CP-007 | Compliance Investigation Process | Investigation of fraud-related overpayments |\n| CO-DC-002 | Documentation Audit & Monitoring | Audits identifying documentation-driven overpayments |\n| CO-DC-004 | Clinical/Documentation/Billing Alignment Audit | Triangulation audits identifying billing mismatches |\n| CO-FA-001 | Anti-Kickback & Stark Law Compliance | Kickback/Stark overpayment referrals |\n| CO-FA-002 | False Claims Act Awareness & Prevention | FCA education relevant to overpayments |\n| CO-FA-003 | Fraud, Waste & Abuse Prevention | FWA investigation integrated with overpayment process |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Retention standards for overpayment records |\n| QA-AE-002 | Root Cause Analysis Process | RCA methodology for overpayment causes |\n| QA-AE-003 | Corrective Action Plan Development | CAP process for overpayment corrective actions |\n| QA-PI-002 | Quality Indicator Monitoring | Overpayment trending as quality indicator |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body notification of material overpayments |\n| HR-ER-002 | Disciplinary Action & Progressive Discipline | Personnel action for deliberate overpayment conduct |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy | Framework classification |\n\n---",
