        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | For every new home health episode (SOC, ROC, or Recertification) that is not excepted from PCR requirements, the PCR Coordinator shall initiate the PCR submission process by compiling the required documentation package. | PCR Coordinator | Within 5 calendar days of SOC/ROC/Recert date |\n| 6.2.2 | The required PCR documentation package shall include all items specified by the active CMS PCR program, which typically include: (a) PCR request form (per CMS specification); (b) signed Plan of Care (485) with valid certification; (c) face-to-face encounter documentation; (d) OASIS assessment; (e) clinical notes demonstrating homebound status, skilled care need, and medical necessity; (f) physician orders. | PCR Coordinator (compilation); Director of Nursing (clinical documentation verification); Revenue Cycle Director (billing elements) | Compiled within 5 calendar days of episode start |\n| 6.2.3 | The Director of Nursing (or clinical designee) shall review the clinical documentation package for completeness and quality before PCR submission. The clinical review shall verify: (a) homebound status narrative is specific and compliant; (b) skilled care need is clearly documented; (c) medical necessity is supported; (d) OASIS is complete and consistent; (e) physician certification is signed and dated appropriately; (f) F2F documentation is present and valid. | Director of Nursing / Clinical Designee | Within 2 business days of package compilation |\n| 6.2.4 | Submit the PCR request to the designated CMS review contractor via the method specified by the PCR program (typically electronic portal). | PCR Coordinator | Within the CMS-specified submission window (per program rules) |\n| 6.2.5 | Log the submission in the PCR Decision Tracking Log (Appendix B) including: patient name, Medicare number, episode dates, submission date, and documentation included. | PCR Coordinator | Same day as submission |\n| 6.2.6 | Monitor for PCR determination (affirmation, provisional affirmation, or non-affirmation) within the CMS-specified response window (typically 10–15 business days). | PCR Coordinator | Per CMS timeline |\n\n---",
