        body: "10.1 When a PCR program is activated, all billing, coding, and clinical documentation staff shall receive PCR-specific training within 30 calendar days of program activation. Training shall cover: (a) PCR program requirements and submission process; (b) required documentation elements; (c) clinical documentation quality standards specific to PCR; (d) non-affirmation response procedures; (e) the prohibition on billing non-affirmed episodes; (f) patient care continuity obligations.\n10.2 The Director of Nursing shall conduct targeted clinical documentation training focused on homebound status, medical necessity, and skilled care need documentation — the three most common PCR non-affirmation drivers nationally.\n10.3 Annual refresher training while PCR is active, including review of non-affirmation patterns and corrective actions.\n10.4 All personnel within scope shall sign Appendix D within 14 calendar days.\n\n---",
