        title: "NOA Submission Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Upon completion of the first billable visit (SOC or ROC), the clinical staff shall confirm the SOC/ROC date in the EHR and notify the billing department that the visit has been completed. | Admitting Clinician / Director of Nursing | Same day as first visit |\n| 6.1.2 | The Billing Coordinator shall verify the following data elements for NOA submission: (a) patient Medicare number — validated through eligibility verification; (b) correct SOC or ROC date; (c) agency NPI and CCN; (d) attending physician NPI; (e) type of admission (SOC or ROC). | Billing Coordinator | Within 24 hours of first visit |\n| 6.1.3 | Submit the NOA electronically to the MAC through the agency's designated clearinghouse using the appropriate electronic transaction format per CMS specifications. | Billing Coordinator | Within 24 hours of data verification — never later than day 5 from SOC/ROC |\n| 6.1.4 | Log the NOA submission in the NOA Submission Tracking Log (Appendix A) including: patient name, Medicare number, SOC/ROC date, NOA submission date, days from SOC to submission, and submission status. | Billing Coordinator | Same day as submission |\n| 6.1.5 | Confirm clearinghouse and MAC acceptance of the NOA through 999/277CA transaction acknowledgments within 2 business days. If the NOA is rejected, identify the rejection reason, correct the error, and resubmit immediately. | Billing Coordinator | Within 2 business days |\n| 6.1.6 | Log the acceptance confirmation in Appendix A. If rejected and resubmitted, log the rejection reason, correction, resubmission date, and final acceptance date. | Billing Coordinator | Same day as confirmation |\n\n---",
