        title: "Payment Receipt and Initial Processing",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Upon receipt of each Medicare Remittance Advice (835 transaction), the Billing Coordinator shall download and import the remittance data into the billing system. | Billing Coordinator | Within 1 business day of receipt |\n| 6.1.2 | The Billing Coordinator shall verify that each claim listed on the remittance matches a submitted claim in the Claims Submission Log (FN-BC-001 Appendix C). Any claim on the remittance that does not match the submission log shall be flagged for investigation. | Billing Coordinator | Within 2 business days |\n| 6.1.3 | Post all payments, adjustments, denials, and offsets to the patient accounts in the billing system. | Billing Coordinator | Within 2 business days |\n| 6.1.4 | Route all denied claims to the denial management process per FN-BC-002. | Billing Coordinator | Same day as posting |\n\n---",
