        id: "9-payment-reconciliation-process",
        title: "Payment Reconciliation Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | For each paid claim on the remittance, complete the Payment Reconciliation Worksheet (Appendix A). The worksheet shall document: (a) patient name and Medicare number; (b) 30-day period dates; (c) PDGM payment group (clinical grouping, functional level, comorbidity adjustment, timing, admission source); (d) expected PDGM payment amount (calculated using current CMS rate tables and wage index); (e) actual payment amount per 835; (f) sequestration reduction amount; (g) any other adjustments (LUPA, PEP, outlier); (h) net payment variance (actual minus expected after accounting for known adjustments). | Revenue Cycle Director / Billing Coordinator | Within 10 business days of remittance receipt |\n| 6.2.2 | Calculate the expected PDGM payment using the following: Base Payment Rate × Case-Mix Weight × Wage Index Adjustment = Expected Payment. Apply sequestration reduction percentage. Apply any applicable LUPA, PEP, or outlier adjustment. | Revenue Cycle Director / Certified Coder | As part of reconciliation |\n| 6.2.3 | Compare actual payment to expected payment. If the net variance is within $100 (positive or negative), the claim is reconciled — log as \"Reconciled\" in Appendix A. | Revenue Cycle Director | Per claim |\n| 6.2.4 | If the net variance exceeds $100 (positive or negative), the claim requires investigation per §6.3. Log as \"Variance — Investigation Required\" in Appendix A. | Revenue Cycle Director | Per claim |\n\n---",
