        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | For each claim with a variance exceeding $100, investigate the cause. Common variance causes include: | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 10 business days of identification |\n\n\n| Variance Type | Common Cause | Investigation Action |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Underpayment — lower than expected | MAC applied different PDGM group than billed; LUPA applied unexpectedly; PEP applied; sequestration rate changed; wage index adjustment | Verify PDGM classification on claim vs. MAC determination on 835; check for LUPA/PEP indicators; verify current sequestration rate |\n| Underpayment — partial payment | Portion of claim denied; adjustment applied | Review adjustment reason codes on 835; route denied portion to FN-BC-002 |\n| Overpayment — higher than expected | Duplicate payment; MAC applied higher PDGM group; outlier payment received; prior adjustment reversed | Verify no duplicate claim; verify PDGM classification; check for outlier indicator; review prior adjustments |\n| Zero payment | Full denial | Route to FN-BC-002 |\n| Offset applied | Prior overpayment recouped; demand letter offset | Verify offset against known overpayment or demand; cross-reference FN-BC-004 |\n\n\n| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.2 | Document the investigation findings in the Variance Investigation section of Appendix A. | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 10 business days |\n| 6.3.3 | Based on investigation findings, take the appropriate action: | Revenue Cycle Director | Per finding |\n\n\n| Finding | Action | Responsible Party |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| MAC processing error (underpayment) | Contact MAC for correction or file appeal per FN-BC-002 | Revenue Cycle Director |\n| Agency billing/coding error (underpayment) | Submit corrected/replacement claim per FN-BC-001 §6.2.6 | Billing Coordinator |\n| Agency coding error (overpayment) | Report to Compliance Officer per FN-BC-004 | Revenue Cycle Director |\n| Duplicate payment (overpayment) | Report to Compliance Officer per FN-BC-004 | Revenue Cycle Director |\n| Correct CMS adjustment (sequestration, LUPA, PEP, outlier) | Log as reconciled with explanation | Revenue Cycle Director |\n| Offset for prior overpayment/demand | Verify against FN-BC-004 log; log as reconciled | Revenue Cycle Director |\n\n| 6.3.4 | All identified overpayments shall be reported to the Compliance Officer within 24 hours per FN-BC-004 §6.2.1. The 60-day clock starts upon identification. | Revenue Cycle Director | Within 24 hours | | 6.3.5 | All identified underpayments shall be pursued within 30 calendar days. If MAC correction is not received within 60 calendar days, escalate to CFO. | Revenue Cycle Director | Pursuit within 30 days; escalation at 60 days |\n\n---",
