        id: "8-pdgm-classification-process",
        title: "PDGM Classification Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Upon completion of the comprehensive assessment (SOC, ROC, or Recertification), the assessing clinician shall complete all OASIS items accurately per CL-OA policies, including all functional assessment items used in PDGM functional impairment scoring__ | Assessing Clinician | Per CL-OA-015 timeframes |\n| 6.1.2 | The certified coder shall review the clinical record and assign the principal diagnosis (ICD-10-CM code) per FN-CM-002. The principal diagnosis shall reflect the primary reason the patient is receiving home health services as documented by the physician in the Plan of Care. | Certified Coder | Within 5 business days of assessment completion__ |\n| 6.1.3 | The certified coder shall assign all applicable secondary/comorbidity diagnosis codes per FN-CM-002, verifying that each secondary code: (a) is documented by the physician; (b) is actively addressed during the episode; (c) is coded to the highest ICD-10-CM specificity. | Certified Coder | With principal diagnosis assignment |\n| 6.1.4 | The certified coder shall verify the PDGM clinical grouping by confirming that the principal diagnosis ICD-10 code maps to the correct clinical group per the current CMS PDGM Grouper__ | Certified Coder | After diagnosis assignment |\n| 6.1.5 | The certified coder or billing coordinator shall verify the functional impairment level by confirming the OASIS functional item responses produce the correct functional score per the CMS PDGM functional scoring algorithm. The coder shall NOT modify OASIS responses — if a discrepancy is identified, it shall be referred to the Director of Nursing for clinical review per CL-OA-002__ | Certified Coder + Director of Nursing (if discrepancy) | After OASIS completion__ |\n| 6.1.__ | The certified coder shall verify the comorbidity adjustment by confirming that the secondary diagnoses map to the appropriate CMS comorbidity subgroups (None, Low, High) per the current CMS comorbidity interaction list__ | Certified Coder | After secondary diagnosis assignment |\n| 6.1.7 | The billing coordinator shall verify the admission source by reviewing the patient's prior claims history (checking for an institutional claim within 14 days prior to SOC using the CMS claims data or agency intake records). Community vs. Institutional classification shall be documented. | Billing Coordinator | Before claim submission |\n| 6.1.8 | The billing coordinator shall verify the timing (Early vs. Late) based on whether this is the first or subsequent 30-day period within the certification period. | Billing Coordinator | Before claim submission |\n| 6.1.9 | The certified coder shall document the complete PDGM classification on the PDGM Classification Worksheet (Appendix A) including all five elements, the resulting HIPPS code, and the expected case-mix weight. | Certified Coder | Before claim submission |\n| 6.1.10 | The Revenue Cycle Director shall verify the HIPPS code on the final claim matches the PDGM Classification Worksheet before authorizing claim submission per FN-BC-001 §6.1.2.10__ | Revenue Cycle Director | Before claim submission |\n\n---",
