        id: "10-physician-query-process",
        title: "Physician Query Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | When physician documentation is ambiguous, incomplete, conflicting, or insufficient to assign an accurate ICD-10-CM code, the certified coder shall initiate a physician query. | Certified Coder | When deficiency identified |\n| 6.3.2 | The query shall be documented using the Physician Query Form (Appendix B) and shall: (a) reference the specific clinical documentation in question; (b) explain the coding issue requiring clarification; (c) NOT lead the physician toward a specific diagnosis or suggest a particular code; (d) present clinical options when applicable (e.g., \"Is this condition best described as X or Y per your clinical assessment?\"); (e) request the physician's documented response within 7 calendar days. | Certified Coder | At time of query |\n| 6.3.3 | The query shall be transmitted to the physician via the EHR message system, fax, or secure email. The Director of Nursing shall facilitate physician communication if the coder does not have direct physician access. | Certified Coder / Director of Nursing | Same day as query initiation |\n| 6.3.4 | If the physician responds within 7 calendar days, the coder shall assign the code based on the physician's clarification and document the response in the coding record. | Certified Coder | Upon response receipt |\n| 6.3.5 | If the physician does not respond within 7 calendar days, the coder shall: (a) send a second query attempt; (b) notify the Director of Nursing for escalation; (c) if still no response by day 14, assign the code based on the best available documentation and document \"Physician query unanswered — code assigned per available documentation.\" | Certified Coder / Director of Nursing | Day 7 (second attempt); Day 14 (code based on documentation) |\n| 6.3.6 | All queries and responses shall be retained in the coding record as part of the audit trail per CO-DC-001. | Certified Coder | Ongoing |\n\n---",
