        title: "Monthly Medical Necessity Documentation Review",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Action | Responsible Party | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | The Director of Nursing shall review a minimum of 5% of visit notes monthly (minimum 10 notes) for medical necessity documentation compliance. | Director of Nursing | Monthly |\n| 6.3.2 | The review shall evaluate: (a) skilled service documented with clinical rationale; (b) homebound status narrative present and patient-specific; (c) progress toward goals documented (or clinical reasoning for limited progress); (d) visit purpose tied to Plan of Care; (e) no prohibited documentation practices. | Director of Nursing | During review |\n| 6.3.3 | Results shall be documented on the Monthly Medical Necessity Review Log (Appendix A). | Director of Nursing | Monthly |\n| 6.3.__ | Clinicians with documentation deficiency rates >10% shall receive targeted re-training within 14 calendar days. | Director of Nursing | Within 14 calendar days |\n| 6.3.5 | Review results shall be reported to the Revenue Cycle Director (billing impact), Compliance Officer (compliance correlation), and QAPI Coordinator (quality integration). | Director of Nursing | Monthly__ |\n\n---",
