        id: "5-policy-statements",
        title: "4\\. Policy Statements",
        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 Every Medicare home health episode shall have a valid physician certification before any claims are submitted for the certification period per 42 CFR § 424.22.\n4.2 Initial certification requires: (a) physician's order for home health services; (b) face-to-face encounter within the required timeframe per CL-CA-006; (c) signed Plan of Care with certification statement.\n4.3 Recertification is required at least every 60 days for continued Medicare home health eligibility. The recertification process must be completed before the end of the current certification period per CL-CP-008.\n4.4 The Revenue Cycle Director shall maintain an Episode Management Dashboard (Appendix A) tracking all open episodes with: SOC date, current certification period, recertification due date, 30-day period dates, physician signature status, and billing status.\n4.5 For non-Medicare payers (Medicare Advantage, commercial), the agency shall obtain and maintain current prior authorizations per payer-specific requirements. No services shall be provided beyond authorized dates or visit counts without prior authorization renewal.\n4.6 Episode transitions (ROC, transfer, discharge) shall trigger specific billing and clinical documentation actions documented in §6.\n4.7 The agency shall not continue billing for episodes where physician recertification has lapsed without documented evidence that recertification was timely obtained. Lapsed certifications shall be treated as billing holds per FN-BC-001 §6.1.3.\n\n---",
