        id: "8-contract-initiation-and-review",
        title: "Contract Initiation and Review",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Initiating Department Lead / Administrator | Submit a Contract Request Form (Appendix A) to the Administrator for any proposed new contract or agreement. The form must identify: (a) the proposed contractor or partner; (b) the scope of services; (c) estimated annual value; (d) whether the contract involves patient care, PHI access, or regulatory compliance obligations; (e) proposed term and renewal provisions. | Prior to initiating any contract negotiation or commitment. |\n| 6.1.2 | Administrator | Review each proposed contract for: (a) necessity and alignment with agency scope of services; (b) potential Anti-Kickback or Stark Law implications (consult Legal Counsel per GV-EA-003 for referral-related contracts); (c) HIPAA and BAA requirements (coordinate with Compliance Officer per CO-HP-005); (d) OIG/SAM exclusion screening of the proposed contractor per HR-TA-003; (e) adequacy of insurance and liability provisions; (f) record retention and audit rights provisions per CO-HP-007. | Within 10 business days of receiving the Contract Request Form. |\n| 6.1.3 | Compliance Officer | Review all contracts involving patient care delivery, PHI access, billing or coding services, or referral relationships for compliance risk. Provide written compliance clearance or identify required modifications before the contract proceeds to execution. | Within 5 business days of referral from Administrator. |\n| 6.1.4 | Administrator | Engage Legal Counsel (per policy GV-EA-003) for review of: (a) all material contracts; (b) any contract with unusual risk allocation, indemnification, or liability provisions; (c) any contract with regulatory compliance obligations not clearly defined; (d) any interagency agreement with referral implications. | Prior to execution for material contracts; as needed for others. |\n\n---",
