        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Responsible Department Lead | Monitor contractor performance on an ongoing basis, including: (a) quality and timeliness of services; (b) compliance with applicable agency policies; (c) staff competency and credential currency (for clinical contractors); (d) incident and complaint rates. | Ongoing; formal performance documentation quarterly. |\n| 6.4.2 | Administrator | Conduct an annual formal review of all active contracts for: (a) performance against contractual standards; (b) cost and value; (c) compliance with law and agency policy; (d) renewal, modification, or termination decisions. | Annually; within 60 calendar days of each contract's anniversary date. |\n| 6.4.3 | Compliance Officer | Conduct or commission an annual audit of a sample of contractor compliance with applicable requirements, including OIG/SAM screening currency, credential verification (for clinical contractors), and BAA compliance. | Annually; results presented at the compliance report to the Governing Body. |\n| 6.4.4 | Administrator | If a contractor fails to meet performance standards or is found non-compliant with legal or policy requirements, initiate a formal corrective action process: (a) written notice to the contractor; (b) defined remediation timeline; (c) escalation to contract suspension or termination if not resolved. | Written notice within 5 business days of identified deficiency; remediation timeline per contract terms. |\n\n---",
