        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Marketing Staff / Administrator | Develop marketing materials and community outreach content that: (a) accurately represent the agency's services, licensure, and credentials; (b) do not make unsubstantiated quality or outcome claims; (c) include the agency's HCAI license number (406412878) and contact information as required by California state law; (d) comply with CMS guidelines for home health marketing; (e) are reviewed for Anti-Kickback compliance. | During development, prior to finalization. |\n| 6.1.2 | Administrator | Review and approve all marketing materials, press releases, event announcements, and public-facing communications before distribution. Maintain copies of all approved materials with version date. | Prior to distribution; copies retained minimum 3 years. |\n| 6.1.3 | Compliance Officer | Review any materials that could implicate Anti-Kickback or Stark Law compliance (e.g., materials referencing relationships with specific physicians or facilities), or that involve claims about clinical outcomes or Medicare/Medicaid compliance. | Within 5 business days of referral from Administrator. |\n\n---",
