        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Administrator | Serve as the primary liaison between legal counsel and the agency. Coordinate document requests, staff interviews, and information provision to legal counsel, ensuring that: (a) only authorized personnel communicate with external counsel; (b) privileged communications are protected from inadvertent disclosure; (c) legal hold obligations (preservation of records) are implemented when litigation is reasonably anticipated. | Ongoing for each active legal matter. |\n| 6.2.2 | Compliance Officer | Participate in all legal matters with compliance implications and maintain a parallel compliance investigation record per policy CO-CP-007 where applicable. | Ongoing for compliance-related legal matters. |\n| 6.2.3 | Administrator | Provide regular status updates on active legal matters to the Governing Body: (a) routine matters — reported at quarterly meetings; (b) material matters — reported within 5 business days of Administrator awareness, with a special written notification to the Governing Body Chair if a regular quarterly meeting is not imminent. | Quarterly for routine matters; within 5 business days for material matters. |\n| 6.2.4 | Administrator | Review legal invoices for accuracy and reasonableness before authorization for payment. Question any unexplained fees or scope expansions with legal counsel prior to payment. | Upon receipt of each invoice; authorization before payment due date. |\n| 6.2.5 | Administrator | For matters involving government investigations (OIG, DOJ, CMS, HCAI), immediately notify the Governing Body Chair and engage legal counsel before providing any response to the investigating authority. | Immediately upon receipt of any government investigation communication. |\n\n---",
