        title: "Escalation and Exception Handling",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| A renewal application has not been submitted by the 90-day deadline. | Compliance Officer notifies the Administrator in writing and the Governing Body Chair. | Administrator submits the renewal application immediately. If the credential is at risk of lapse, engage legal counsel per GV-EA-003 and the issuing authority to explore expedited processing. Governing Body notified at the next meeting or via special notification. | Renewal submitted within 5 calendar days of notification; Governing Body notified within 24 hours if lapse risk exists. |\n| A credential expires before the renewal is processed (lapse occurs). | Administrator notifies the Governing Body Chair and Compliance Officer immediately. | Administrator contacts the issuing authority immediately to determine: (a) whether the agency may continue to operate under a grace period; (b) what is required to reinstate the credential. Cease admissions of new patients if required by the issuing authority until reinstatement. Notify the MAC if Medicare certification is affected. Governing Body convenes a special meeting within 48 hours. | Immediate notification; special Governing Body meeting within 48 hours; reinstatement pursued on an emergency basis. |\n| A renewal application is denied by the issuing authority. | Administrator notifies the Governing Body Chair, Compliance Officer, and Legal Counsel immediately. | Legal Counsel reviews the denial and advises on appeal rights and remediation. Administrator prepares an appeal or corrective submission per the issuing authority's requirements. Governing Body informed within 24 hours and directs response. | Within 24 hours of denial notification; appeal filed within the issuing authority's appeal deadline. |\n| CMS issues an Immediate Jeopardy finding that threatens Medicare certification. | Administrator notifies the Governing Body Chair, Compliance Officer, and Director of Nursing immediately. | Implement the Immediate Jeopardy corrective action plan per CMS requirements (typically 23 calendar days). Governing Body convenes a special meeting within 48 hours. Director of Nursing implements clinical corrective measures immediately. Daily status updates provided to Governing Body Chair until jeopardy is removed. | Corrective action per CMS timeline; special Governing Body meeting within 48 hours; daily updates until resolution. |\n| HCAI issues a license suspension or revocation notice. | Administrator notifies the Governing Body Chair, Compliance Officer, and Legal Counsel immediately. | Legal Counsel files any available appeal or stay of action within the required timeframe. Administrator implements the patient transition plan (per GV-EA-005 and CL-CP-007) if license suspension or revocation is imminent. Governing Body convenes an emergency meeting. | Within 24 hours; emergency Governing Body meeting within 48 hours. |\n| An accrediting organization issues a notice of adverse accreditation action (probation, denial, revocation). | Administrator notifies the Governing Body Chair within 24 hours. | Administrator and Compliance Officer assess the impact on deemed status and Medicare certification. If deemed status is lost, notify the CMS state survey agency and prepare for a CMS standard survey. Legal Counsel engaged to advise on appeal options. | Within 24 hours of notice; CMS notification per applicable requirements; Governing Body informed at next meeting or special meeting. |\n\n---",
