        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with Federal, State, and local laws | Requires the agency to maintain compliance with all applicable laws, including licensure and certification requirements. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Governing body responsibility for ensuring the agency operates under valid licensure and certification. |\n| 42 CFR Part 489 | Provider Agreements and Supplier Approval | Governs Medicare provider agreements, termination, and change of information requirements. |\n| 42 CFR § 489.13 | Effective date of agreement or approval | Defines effective dates of Medicare provider agreements. |\n| 42 CFR § 489.52 | Termination by CMS | Defines the conditions under which CMS may terminate a Medicare provider agreement. |\n| 42 CFR § 424.510–516 | Medicare enrollment requirements | Governs Medicare enrollment, revalidation, and change of information requirements. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Provides interpretive guidelines for survey of compliance with organizational and administrative requirements, including licensure and certification verification. |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Chapter 2 — The Certification Process | Defines the Medicare certification process, survey protocols, and enforcement actions. |\n| CMS Survey and Certification Policy and Procedures (S&C Memos) | Ongoing guidance on certification, survey, and enforcement procedures applicable to home health agencies. |\n\n### 9.3 State Requirements\n\n| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| California Health and Safety Code, Division 2, Chapter 8 — Home Health Agencies | Establishes the legal requirements for home health agency licensure in California, including renewal, display, and change notification requirements. |\n| California Code of Regulations, Title 22, Division 5 — Home Health Agencies | Defines licensure standards, application and renewal procedures, and reporting obligations for California home health agencies. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-EA-004 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body quarterly verification of credential status (Section 6.2.1.2). |\n| GV-GB-002 | Board Meeting & Minutes Requirements | Credential verification documented in Governing Body minutes. |\n| GV-OG-002 | Administrator Qualifications & Responsibilities | Administrator accountable for credential maintenance. |\n| GV-OG-003 | Scope of Services Definition | Scope of services must align with licensure and certification. |\n| GV-EA-001 | Interagency Agreements & Contracts | Contracts must be consistent with agency licensure. |\n| GV-EA-003 | Legal Counsel Engagement & Oversight | Legal counsel engaged for enforcement actions and appeals. |\n| GV-EA-005 | Agency Closure or Change of Ownership | Change of ownership triggers credential transfer requirements. |\n| CO-RA-001 | Regulatory Change Monitoring & Implementation | Monitoring of regulatory changes affecting licensure and certification requirements. |\n| CO-RA-003 | External Audit & Survey Readiness | Continuous survey readiness supporting certification maintenance. |\n| CO-RA-004 | Medicare Conditions of Participation Compliance | Ongoing CoP compliance supporting Medicare certification. |\n| CO-RA-005 | State Licensure & Regulatory Compliance | State licensure compliance supporting California license maintenance. |\n| CO-RA-006 | Accreditation Standards Compliance | Accreditation compliance supporting deemed status. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Retention standards for all credential documents and correspondence. |\n| CL-CP-007 | Transfer & Referral Procedures | Patient transition procedures if credential lapse requires admission cessation. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n| EN-LC-001 | Policy Lifecycle Management & Version Control | Policy version control and lifecycle management for this policy. |\n\n---",
