        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 The Administrator and all administrative staff responsible for credential maintenance shall receive training on this policy within 14 calendar days of assuming credential-related responsibilities. Training shall cover: (a) the agency's required credentials and their renewal timelines; (b) the Agency Credential Register and how to maintain it; (c) the renewal application process and pre-submission quality review; (d) reporting requirements for changes affecting credentials; (e) the escalation protocol for credential-threatening events; (f) Governing Body reporting obligations.\n10.2 The Compliance Officer shall receive training on the regulatory monitoring obligations defined in this policy, including the requirement to notify the Administrator within 7 calendar days of identifying any new or changed licensure, certification, or accreditation requirement.\n10.3 All personnel within scope (Section 3) shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix C) within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new appointment.\n10.4 The Administrator shall include a credential maintenance compliance update as a standing topic in the annual mandatory training program, informing all staff of the importance of the agency's licenses and certifications to continued operations.\n\n---",
