        title: "Governing Body Decision and Authorization",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Governing Body | The Governing Body shall make the formal decision to close the agency, terminate the Medicare provider agreement, or initiate or accept a change of ownership. The decision shall be documented in Governing Body meeting minutes per policy GV-GB-002. The minutes shall record: (a) the nature of the decision (closure, CHOW, merger); (b) the rationale for the decision; (c) the authorized effective date or anticipated timeline; (d) the designation of the Administrator as the operational lead for the transition process; (e) the direction to engage Legal Counsel per GV-EA-003. | At a regular or special Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.1.2 | Governing Body | Authorize the Administrator to execute all necessary notifications, agreements, and transition activities required by this policy, subject to Governing Body oversight and approval of material transactions. | At the same meeting. |\n| 6.1.3 | Administrator | Engage Legal Counsel with expertise in home health agency regulatory transactions per policy GV-EA-003 immediately upon Governing Body authorization. | Within 3 calendar days of Governing Body authorization. |\n| 6.1.4 | Administrator | Establish a Closure/CHOW Transition Team consisting of: (a) the Administrator (team lead); (b) the Director of Nursing; (c) the Compliance Officer; (d) the CFO / Revenue Cycle Director; (e) the HR Director; (f) Legal Counsel. The team shall meet at least weekly during the transition period. | Within 7 calendar days of Governing Body authorization. |\n\n---",
