        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Administrator | Notify the CMS Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) of the anticipated change of ownership by submitting a CMS-855A Change of Information form. The notification must include: (a) the nature of the ownership change; (b) the anticipated effective date; (c) identification of the acquiring entity; (d) the new owner's proposed management structure. | At least 90 calendar days before the anticipated effective date of the CHOW, or as early as practicable if the transaction timeline is shorter. CMS requires notification in advance of the CHOW effective date. |\n| 6.2.2 | Administrator | Notify the California HCAI of the anticipated change of ownership in compliance with California Health and Safety Code requirements. Submit all required HCAI forms, applications, and supporting documentation as specified by HCAI for the type of ownership change. | Per HCAI requirements; typically at least 90 calendar days before the anticipated effective date. |\n| 6.2.3 | Administrator | Notify the state survey agency (California Department of Public Health) of the anticipated CHOW per CMS and state requirements. | Per CMS and state requirements; concurrent with MAC notification. |\n| 6.2.4 | Administrator | Cooperate with the acquiring entity in completing any CMS or HCAI applications required for the new owner to assume the Medicare provider agreement and state license. Provide all requested documentation, operational data, and access to agency records as needed for the new owner's application process. | Throughout the CHOW process; responsive to requests within 5 business days. |\n| 6.2.5 | Compliance Officer | Verify that the acquiring entity has undergone OIG/SAM exclusion screening for all principals, owners, and managing employees as required by CMS enrollment regulations. Document the screening results. | Before the CHOW effective date. |\n| 6.2.6 | Administrator | If CMS determines that the CHOW results in a new provider agreement (rather than an assignment of the existing agreement), work with Legal Counsel and the acquiring entity to complete the CMS enrollment and survey process required for new certification. | Per CMS determination and timelines. |\n\n---",
