        title: "Patient Notification and Transition",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Director of Nursing | Compile a complete census of all patients currently receiving services from the agency, including: (a) patient name and contact information; (b) primary caregiver contact; (c) current plan of care and services ordered; (d) current episode dates; (e) attending physician; (f) clinical acuity and care needs. | Within 7 calendar days of Governing Body decision. |\n| 6.4.2 | Director of Nursing / Administrator | Notify all current patients and their primary caregivers in writing of: (a) the planned closure or change of ownership; (b) the expected last date of service (for closures); (c) the patient's right to choose any qualified home health agency; (d) assistance available from the agency in identifying and transitioning to alternative providers; (e) the process for transferring medical records; (f) a list of Medicare-certified home health agencies serving the patient's geographic area; (g) contact information for the agency's transition coordinator. The notification shall be provided in the patient's primary language or with interpreter services as required by policy OP-PA-003. | At least 30 calendar days before the planned closure or CHOW effective date. Written notification retained in each patient's clinical record. |\n| 6.4.3 | Director of Nursing | Develop an individualized Patient Transition Plan for each current patient, documenting: (a) the receiving agency selected by the patient (or family/representative); (b) the anticipated transfer date; (c) a clinical summary of the patient's condition, current plan of care, and active orders; (d) any pending physician orders, recertification, or face-to-face encounters; (e) the date clinical records will be transferred to the receiving agency; (f) confirmation that the patient's attending physician has been notified. | Transition plans completed for all patients no later than 14 calendar days before the planned closure or CHOW effective date. |\n| 6.4.4 | Assigned Clinician | Coordinate the clinical transfer of each patient per policy CL-CP-007 (Transfer & Referral Procedures), including: (a) verbal report to the receiving agency's clinical staff; (b) transmission of the clinical summary and current orders; (c) OASIS transfer or discharge assessment as applicable; (d) medication reconciliation; (e) patient and caregiver education on the transition. | Completed before the patient's last visit from Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. |\n| 6.4.5 | Director of Nursing | Notify each patient's attending physician in writing of the planned transfer, including the name of the receiving agency and the transfer date. Obtain physician acknowledgment if possible. | At least 14 calendar days before the planned closure or CHOW effective date; before the transfer date for each patient. |\n| 6.4.6 | Director of Nursing | For patients who decline to transfer to another agency or who cannot be placed, document the refusal or placement difficulty in the clinical record and continue services until the agency's last date of operation. Escalate to the Administrator and Compliance Officer if any patient's safety or access to care is jeopardized. | Ongoing; escalation immediately upon identification of care continuity risk. |\n| 6.4.7 | Administrator | Confirm that all patients have been safely transitioned or discharged before the agency ceases operations. No patient shall be abandoned — services shall continue until each patient has been successfully transferred or appropriately discharged. | Before the agency's last date of operation. |\n\n---",
