        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 489.18 | Change of ownership | Defines CHOW for Medicare-participating providers and the requirements for assignment or transfer of the provider agreement. |\n| 42 CFR § 489.52 | Termination by the provider | Defines the provider's right to voluntarily terminate its Medicare provider agreement with advance written notice. |\n| 42 CFR § 489.53 | Termination by CMS | Defines the conditions under which CMS may involuntarily terminate a provider agreement. |\n| 42 CFR Part 424, Subpart P | Requirements for Medicare enrollment | Governs Medicare enrollment changes, including CHOW reporting requirements. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Governing body accountability for agency operations, including closure and transition decisions. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.50 | Condition of Participation: Patient Rights | Requires patient notification and continuity of care during service transitions. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.110 | Condition of Participation: Clinical records | Requires clinical record maintenance, including during and after agency closure. |\n| 45 CFR Parts 160 and 164 | HIPAA Privacy and Security Rules | Governs clinical record handling, transfer, and patient access rights during and after closure. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Chapter 2 — The Certification Process | Defines the CHOW and voluntary termination processes, notification requirements, and CMS administrative procedures. |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Provides interpretive guidelines for patient care transition during closure or CHOW. |\n| CMS Medicare Enrollment Application (CMS-855A) | The form used to report changes of ownership and other enrollment changes to the MAC. |\n\n### 9.3 State Requirements\n\n| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| California Health and Safety Code, Division 2, Chapter 8 | Establishes state requirements for home health agency closure, change of ownership, and license surrender, including patient notification obligations. |\n| California Code of Regulations, Title 22, Division 5 | Defines HCAI requirements for change of ownership applications and license surrender procedures. |\n| California WARN Act (Labor Code § 1400–1408) | Requires 60-day advance notice to employees before a plant closure or mass layoff affecting 75 or more employees. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-EA-005 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body authorizes and oversees the closure/CHOW process. |\n| GV-GB-002 | Board Meeting & Minutes Requirements | Closure/CHOW decision documented in Governing Body minutes. |\n| GV-OG-005 | Delegation of Authority | Administrator's delegated authority for executing the transition. |\n| GV-EA-001 | Interagency Agreements & Contracts | Contract termination/transfer during closure/CHOW. |\n| GV-EA-003 | Legal Counsel Engagement & Oversight | Legal Counsel engagement for closure/CHOW legal matters. |\n| GV-EA-004 | Agency Licensure & Certification Maintenance | Credential surrender/transfer procedures. |\n| CL-CP-006 | Discharge Planning & Criteria | Patient discharge procedures during closure. |\n| CL-CP-007 | Transfer & Referral Procedures | Patient transfer procedures during closure/CHOW. |\n| CO-HP-001 | HIPAA Privacy Program | PHI protection during record transfer. |\n| CO-HP-002 | HIPAA Security Program | Electronic record security during transition. |\n| CO-HP-006 | Patient Access to Records | Patient record access rights post-closure. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Record retention obligations post-closure. |\n| FN-BC-004 | Overpayment Identification & Refund | Overpayment resolution during financial closeout. |\n| HR-ER-006 | Separation & Exit Process | Employee separation procedures. |\n| IT-SC-006 | Data Classification & Handling | Data handling during system decommissioning. |\n| RM-ER-004 | Liability & Insurance Management | Insurance closeout and tail coverage. |\n| RM-ER-006 | Claims Management & Litigation Support | Post-closure claims management. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n| EN-LC-001 | Policy Lifecycle Management & Version Control | Policy version control and lifecycle management for this policy. |\n\n---",
