        id: "29-training-acknowledgment-requirements",
        title: "10\\. Training & Acknowledgment Requirements",
        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 The Administrator, Director of Nursing, Compliance Officer, CFO, and HR Director shall receive training on this policy within 14 calendar days of appointment. Training shall cover: (a) the types of events that trigger this policy; (b) the regulatory notification requirements and timelines for CMS, HCAI, and DHCS; (c) the patient transition process and the paramount priority of patient safety; (d) the employee notification and WARN Act requirements; (e) the financial closeout process; (f) the record retention and transfer obligations; (g) the post-closure obligations.\n10.2 All Governing Body members shall receive orientation to this policy as part of their governance onboarding per GV-GB-001, Section 10.1, with emphasis on: (a) the Governing Body's exclusive decision-making authority for closure and CHOW; (b) the Governing Body's oversight role during the transition; (c) the regulatory consequences of non-compliance.\n10.3 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new appointment.\n10.4 In the event this policy is activated, the Administrator shall conduct an orientation session for all agency staff within 7 calendar days of the Governing Body's closure/CHOW decision, informing staff of: (a) the nature and timeline of the event; (b) their role in patient transition activities; (c) the employee notification and separation process; (d) confidentiality obligations; (e) the prohibition on patient abandonment.\n\n---",
