        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Administrator / Designated Secretary | Prepare the meeting agenda for each regular quarterly meeting. The agenda shall include the following standing items in the order listed: (a) Call to Order; (b) Confirmation of Quorum; (c) Approval of Prior Meeting Minutes; (d) Administrator Report; (e) Compliance Officer Report; (f) QAPI Report; (g) Financial Report; (h) Old Business — Status of Prior Meeting Directives; (i) New Business; (j) Executive Session (if applicable); (k) Adjournment and Next Meeting Date. | Draft prepared no later than 10 calendar days before the meeting. |\n| 6.3.2 | Governing Body Chair | Review and approve the draft agenda, adding any items requiring Governing Body action that are not captured in standing items. | No later than 8 calendar days before the meeting. |\n| 6.3.3 | Administrator / Designated Secretary | Distribute the approved agenda to all Governing Body members, along with all supporting materials (compliance report, QAPI report, financial report, action item tracker update, and any new business documents requiring advance review). | No fewer than 7 calendar days before the meeting. |\n| 6.3.4 | Administrator | Confirm receipt of the agenda by all Governing Body members. If any member has not confirmed receipt by 3 calendar days before the meeting, the Administrator shall follow up by phone or email and document the follow-up attempt. | Confirmation confirmed by 4 calendar days before the meeting; follow-up by 3 calendar days before. |\n| 6.3.5 | Governing Body Chair | Accept requests from members to add items to the agenda up to 5 calendar days before the meeting. Items requested after that point shall be deferred to New Business at the discretion of the Chair, unless the item constitutes an urgent matter. | Requests accepted through 5 calendar days before the meeting. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
