        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.6.1 | Governing Body Chair | Announce the convening of an executive session, state the general subject matter category, and identify the individuals permitted to remain present. All guests and non-members not specifically authorized shall exit the meeting room or remote session. | At the time executive session is convened. |\n| 6.6.2 | Designated Secretary | Record in the regular meeting minutes: the time executive session commenced, the general subject matter category, and the names of individuals present. | During the meeting. |\n| 6.6.3 | Compliance Officer | Maintain a separate, restricted Executive Session Log (Appendix D) documenting: (a) date and meeting to which the session pertained; (b) subject matter with sufficient specificity to allow future identification; (c) names of all individuals present; (d) any decisions made, motions passed, or directives issued during the executive session; (e) any legal counsel present and the nature of legal advice received (noting attorney-client privilege where applicable). | Executive Session Log entry completed within 7 calendar days of the meeting. |\n| 6.6.4 | Governing Body Chair | Announce the conclusion of the executive session, note the time in the regular meeting, and reconvene the open session. Any formal actions taken during the executive session (motions, votes, directives) that are not legally protected shall be recorded in the regular meeting minutes. | At the conclusion of executive session. |\n| 6.6.5 | Compliance Officer | Maintain the Executive Session Log in a restricted access file separate from the general governance file. Access shall be limited to Governing Body members, the Compliance Officer, and legal counsel. | Ongoing; restricted access enforced continuously. |\n\n---",
