        id: "17-how-compliance-is-measured",
        title: "How Compliance Is Measured",
        level: 3,
        order: 17,
        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Governing Body meets at least quarterly. | Review of meeting minutes confirming date, attendance, and quorum for each quarter. | Four or more meetings per calendar year; quorum confirmed at each. |\n| Meeting agendas are distributed at least 7 days before each meeting. | Review of agenda distribution records and email timestamps. | 100% of agendas distributed within required timeframe; no exceptions without documented cause. |\n| Draft minutes are completed within 14 calendar days of each meeting. | Review of draft completion dates on file. | 100% of drafts completed on time; no draft outstanding beyond 14 calendar days without a documented extension approved by the Chair. |\n| Minutes capture substantive discussion, not just receipt of reports. | Content review of approved minutes for specificity of discussion, questions, responses, and directives. | All minutes include specific discussion summaries, questions raised, Governing Body responses, and directives with named responsible parties and deadlines. |\n| All motions, seconds, and votes are recorded. | Review of motion log within approved minutes. | 100% of formal actions recorded with mover, seconder, vote count, and outcome. |\n| Action items are tracked and reported at each subsequent meeting. | Review of Action Item Tracker and Old Business section of subsequent minutes. | All open directives tracked; status reported at each regular meeting; no item overdue beyond two consecutive quarters without documented escalation. |\n| Supporting reports submitted 7 days before each meeting. | Review of submission dates for compliance, QAPI, financial, and administrator reports. | 100% of reports submitted within required timeframe for at least 90% of meetings in any rolling 12-month period. |\n| Governance file is complete and organized for rapid retrieval. | Physical or electronic file audit conducted quarterly by Administrator. | All required records present, indexed, and retrievable within 1 business day. |\n| Executive Session Logs are maintained for all executive sessions. | Review of restricted executive session file by Compliance Officer. | Log entry completed for 100% of executive sessions within 7 calendar days of each meeting. |\n| Meeting records retained for minimum 7 years. | Review of records retention schedule; audit of governance file index. | All records with a date within the past 7 years present and intact. No premature destruction documented. |\n\n---",
