        level: 3,
        order: 18,
        body: "| Failure Point | Risk | Mitigation |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Minutes reflect only \"report received\" without discussion or directives. | Surveyors cite as passive governance; failure to exercise oversight under 42 CFR § 484.105. | Train Designated Secretary to record specific questions, data points referenced, and Governing Body responses. Chair reviews drafts for substance before distribution. |\n| Draft minutes not completed timely; approved months after the meeting. | Creates audit gap; surveyor may question whether the meeting occurred as recorded. | Enforce 14-calendar-day draft deadline; Chair escalates to Administrator if deadline is missed. |\n| Quorum not documented in minutes. | Surveyor treats meeting as non-compliant even if quorum was in fact present. | Designated Secretary uses Appendix B template which includes quorum as a required field before any agenda item is recorded. |\n| Agendas not distributed 7 days in advance. | Survey finding; evidence of inadequate governance administration. | Administrator sets calendar reminders 10 days before each meeting; tracks distribution dates in governance file. |\n| Action items issued at one meeting never appear in subsequent minutes. | Surveyor cites as evidence of non-functional governance; directives without follow-through. | Maintain Action Item Tracker (Appendix E); include as mandatory Old Business agenda item at every meeting. |\n| No minutes produced for a special meeting. | Surveyor treats the special meeting as not having occurred; any decisions made at the special meeting have no documented basis. | Policy requires minutes for every meeting type; Designated Secretary is responsible for all meeting documentation. |\n| Executive session held with no notation in regular minutes. | Survey finding; creates appearance that Governing Body is conducting undocumented business. | Regular minutes template (Appendix B) includes an executive session field; Chair confirms notation before minutes are finalized. |\n| Governance file incomplete or inaccessible during survey. | Surveyors cannot verify compliance; creates presumption of non-compliance for unverified periods. | Quarterly governance file audit by Administrator; records indexed for same-day retrieval. |\n| Minutes not retained for 7 years. | Violation of record retention requirements under CO-HP-007; inability to demonstrate historical compliance. | Apply 7-year retention schedule to all governance records from the date of the meeting; enforce destruction moratorium. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
