        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Primary regulatory basis requiring a functioning Governing Body; meeting records are the primary evidence of compliance. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(a) | Standard: Governing body | Requires the Governing Body to hold full legal authority for agency operations; meeting minutes document the exercise of that authority. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(b) | Standard: Administrator | Administrator appointment and oversight must be documented in meeting minutes. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(c) | Standard: Clinical manager | Clinical Manager appointment and QAPI oversight documented in meeting minutes. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65 | Condition of Participation: Quality Assessment and Performance Improvement | Governing Body oversight of QAPI must be evidenced in meeting minutes. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with Federal, State, and local laws | Compliance program oversight documented in meeting minutes. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.102 | Condition of Participation: Emergency preparedness | Emergency preparedness plan approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Defines surveyor expectations for Governing Body meeting documentation; establishes what constitutes adequate evidence of active governance oversight. |\n| CMS Survey and Certification Policy and Procedures (S&C Memos) | Provides ongoing guidance on CMS expectations for HHA governance documentation; applicable S&C memos should be reviewed annually by the Compliance Officer. |\n\n### 9.3 OIG Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies (1998; supplemented) | Establishes expectation that the Governing Body actively oversees the compliance program; meeting minutes are the primary evidence of compliance program oversight. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-GB-002 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Parent policy establishing the Governing Body's meeting frequency requirements and oversight obligations documented via this policy. |\n| GV-GB-003 | Conflict of Interest Disclosure | Conflict recusals must be documented in meeting minutes per this policy. |\n| GV-GB-004 | Succession Planning for Key Leadership | Succession plan review and approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-GB-005 | Annual Governance Self-Assessment | Self-assessment results documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-OG-001 | Organizational Structure & Reporting | Governing Body approval of organizational structure documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-OG-003 | Scope of Services Definition | Annual scope of services review and approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-OG-004 | Strategic Planning & Annual Goals | Strategic plan approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-PM-001 | Policy Development & Approval Process | REQUIRED-tier policy approvals documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-PM-002 | Policy Review & Revision Cycle | Policy review cycle approvals documented in meeting minutes. |\n| GV-PM-003 | Policy Acknowledgment & Staff Attestation | Acknowledgment of this policy required for all members within scope. |\n| GV-EA-004 | Agency Licensure & Certification Maintenance | Licensure status reviews documented in meeting minutes. |\n| QA-PG-001 | QAPI Program Establishment & Governance | QAPI program governance documented in meeting minutes. |\n| QA-PG-002 | QAPI Plan Development & Annual Review | Annual QAPI plan approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| QA-SM-004 | Home Health Compare & Star Rating Monitoring | Star Rating trend data presented and documented in QAPI report at each meeting. |\n| QA-AE-003 | Corrective Action Plan Development & Tracking | Escalation of overdue directives per Section 6.7.4; corrective action plans may be initiated via Governing Body directive. |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | Compliance program oversight documented in meeting minutes. |\n| CO-CP-002 | Compliance Officer Designation & Authority | Compliance Officer appointment documented in meeting minutes. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Establishes 7-year minimum retention requirement for all governance meeting records. |\n| FN-FP-005 | Annual Budget & Financial Planning | Budget approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| OP-FM-005 | Emergency Operations & Business Continuity | Emergency plan approval documented in meeting minutes. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n| EN-LC-001 | Enterprise Policy Lifecycle Management | Policy version control and lifecycle management for this policy. |\n\n---",
