        id: "29-training-acknowledgment-requirements",
        title: "10\\. Training & Acknowledgment Requirements",
        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 The Designated Secretary — whether the Administrator or an assigned designee — shall receive orientation to this policy and the agency's meeting documentation standards within fourteen (14) calendar days of assuming the Designated Secretary role. Orientation shall be conducted by the Administrator or Compliance Officer and must cover: (a) required elements of meeting minutes per Section 6.4.2; (b) quorum documentation requirements; (c) agenda preparation and distribution timelines; (d) executive session notation procedures; (e) action item tracking obligations; (f) governance file maintenance and retention requirements.\n10.2 All Governing Body members shall receive orientation to this policy within fourteen (14) calendar days of appointment, as part of the broader Governing Body orientation required by policy GV-GB-001 §10.1. Orientation for members shall cover: (a) what constitutes substantive minutes and why passive documentation creates survey risk; (b) the member's responsibility to raise questions, provide direction, and ensure their participation is reflected in the minutes; (c) the minutes approval process and how to raise corrections at the next meeting.\n10.3 All Governing Body members and senior leadership within the scope of this policy (Section 3) shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix C) within fourteen (14) calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new appointment.\n10.4 The Administrator shall maintain a tracking log of all policy acknowledgments and report any non-compliance to the Governing Body Chair within seven (7) calendar days of the acknowledgment deadline.\n10.5 Annual refresher on meeting documentation standards — including review of any citations or findings from the prior year's survey or internal audit — shall be conducted at the first quarterly meeting of each calendar year and documented in those meeting minutes.\n\n---",
