        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Compliance Officer | Assess each disclosed item against the following materiality criteria: (a) Financial Threshold — any financial interest with a fair market value exceeding $500 annually, or any ownership interest exceeding 1% in a relevant entity, is presumed material absent specific contrary finding; (b) Decision-Making Nexus — any conflict involving a matter on which the disclosing individual exercises or influences agency decision-making is presumed material; (c) Referral Relationship — any financial or professional relationship with a referral source or competitor is presumed material regardless of dollar amount; (d) OIG Sensitivity — any arrangement that could implicate the Anti-Kickback Statute or Stark Law, regardless of dollar value, is automatically material. | Completed for each disclosure within 14 calendar days of receipt. |\n| 6.4.2 | Compliance Officer | Document the materiality assessment in writing. For each disclosed item, record: (a) the disclosure reference number; (b) the nature of the disclosed interest; (c) the materiality determination (material / non-material); (d) the basis for the determination; (e) the recommended management action. | Documented within 14 calendar days of receipt. |\n| 6.4.3 | Compliance Officer | For any disclosure assessed as non-material, file the assessment memo in the individual's conflict of interest file and note the non-material determination in the next regular conflict of interest status report to the Governing Body. No additional Governing Body action is required for non-material disclosures. | Filed within 14 calendar days of receipt; noted in next status report. |\n| 6.4.4 | Compliance Officer | For any disclosure assessed as material, develop a draft Conflict Management Plan (Appendix D) and submit it to the Governing Body for approval. The draft plan must specify: (a) the nature of the conflict; (b) recusal requirements — which specific matters require recusal; (c) monitoring obligations — how the conflict will be monitored over time; (d) review interval — when the plan will be reassessed; (e) termination criteria — conditions under which the conflict is resolved and the plan retired. | Draft submitted to the Governing Body within 14 calendar days of the materiality determination. |\n\n---",
