        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Governing Body Chair / Administrator | Before each Governing Body meeting, review the current conflict of interest file and identify any agenda item that could implicate a disclosed conflict for any member or attendee. Notify the affected individual in writing at least 3 calendar days before the meeting of the specific agenda item requiring their recusal. | At least 3 calendar days before the meeting. |\n| 6.5.2 | Individual Subject to Recusal | At the meeting, when the conflicted agenda item is called: (a) publicly announce the recusal and the general nature of the conflict (without disclosing legally protected details); (b) physically or virtually withdraw from the meeting room or session for the duration of the discussion and vote; (c) not return to the meeting until the conflicted item is fully concluded and the Chair announces the individual may rejoin. | At the time the conflicted agenda item is called. |\n| 6.5.3 | Designated Secretary | Record in the meeting minutes: (a) the name and role of the individual who recused; (b) the agenda item from which they recused; (c) the stated basis for recusal (general description only); (d) the time of withdrawal and return; (e) confirmation that the individual was not present during discussion or voting on the item. | In the meeting minutes for each meeting at which a recusal occurs. |\n| 6.5.4 | Compliance Officer | File a copy of the recusal record in the individual's conflict of interest file within 7 calendar days of the meeting. | Within 7 calendar days of the meeting. |\n| 6.5.5 | Governing Body | If an individual subject to a recusal requirement fails to recuse, the Governing Body Chair shall immediately halt discussion on the affected item, direct the individual to withdraw, and restart the discussion after withdrawal. The failure to recuse shall be documented in the meeting minutes and referred to the Compliance Officer for determination of appropriate corrective action. | Immediately upon identification of failure to recuse. |\n\n---",
