        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.7.1 | Any Individual | Report a suspected undisclosed conflict of interest through any available channel: (a) directly to the Compliance Officer; (b) via the compliance hotline per policy CO-CP-006; (c) in writing to the Governing Body Chair. All reports shall be treated as confidential. Reporters acting in good faith shall be protected from retaliation per policy CO-CP-005. | Upon becoming aware of a suspected undisclosed conflict. |\n| 6.7.2 | Compliance Officer | Upon receipt of a report of suspected undisclosed conflict, initiate a preliminary inquiry within 7 calendar days to assess whether the report has sufficient basis to warrant a formal investigation. The preliminary inquiry shall include: (a) review of all prior disclosure forms from the subject individual; (b) review of relevant meeting minutes for evidence of participation in matters where a conflict may have existed; (c) interview with the reporting party if appropriate. | Preliminary inquiry initiated within 7 calendar days of receipt. |\n| 6.7.3 | Compliance Officer | If the preliminary inquiry supports a reasonable basis for concern, initiate a formal compliance investigation per policy CO-CP-007. Notify the Governing Body Chair in writing within 3 calendar days of determining a formal investigation is warranted. | Within 3 calendar days of the decision to initiate a formal investigation. |\n| 6.7.4 | Governing Body | Upon notification of a formal investigation involving a Governing Body member, direct the subject member to recuse from all Governing Body matters until the investigation is concluded. Document the directive and recusal in meeting minutes. | Immediately upon notification; documented at the next meeting or in a special resolution. |\n| 6.7.5 | Compliance Officer | Complete the investigation per policy CO-CP-007 and present findings and recommendations to the Governing Body in executive session. | Within the timeframe defined in policy CO-CP-007; findings presented at the next Governing Body meeting after investigation completion. |\n| 6.7.6 | Governing Body | Based on investigation findings, determine appropriate action which may include: (a) no action — conflict was disclosed and managed; (b) required retroactive disclosure and enhanced monitoring; (c) removal from the Governing Body; (d) referral to legal counsel; (e) voluntary repayment of improperly obtained benefits; (f) notification to applicable regulatory authorities. Document the determination in executive session minutes. | Determination made at the meeting where findings are presented; documented in executive session log per GV-GB-002. |\n\n---",
