        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Governing Body fiduciary duty and accountability for agency operations, which conflict of interest management directly supports. |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1320a-7b | Anti-Kickback Statute | Financial relationships between Governing Body members and referral sources may implicate AKS; conflict disclosure is a primary safeguard. |\n| 42 U.S.C. § 1395nn | Stark Law (Physician Self-Referral) | Ownership or compensation arrangements disclosed under this policy may implicate Stark Law restrictions. |\n| 31 U.S.C. § 3729–3733 | False Claims Act | Conflicts of interest that result in improper financial decisions may create False Claims Act liability. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Defines surveyor expectations for governing body functioning including the integrity of governance decisions, which conflict management directly supports. |\n\n### 9.3 OIG Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies (1998; supplemented) | Explicitly identifies conflict of interest policies as a required element of an effective compliance program and establishes expectations for governing body conflict management. |\n| OIG General Compliance Program Guidance (2023) | Updated OIG guidance reinforcing conflict of interest disclosure requirements for healthcare governance bodies. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-GB-003 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Parent governance policy; requires conflict of interest disclosure as a component of governing body member obligations. |\n| GV-GB-002 | Board Meeting & Minutes Requirements | Meeting minutes are the primary record of recusal compliance under this policy. |\n| GV-GB-004 | Succession Planning for Key Leadership | Succession candidates may be subject to conflict disclosure requirements upon appointment. |\n| GV-OG-005 | Delegation of Authority | Delegated authority holders may be subject to conflict disclosure requirements under this policy. |\n| GV-PM-003 | Policy Acknowledgment & Staff Attestation | Requires signed acknowledgment of this policy by all in-scope individuals. |\n| GV-EA-001 | Interagency Agreements & Contracts | Vendor and contractor relationships disclosed under this policy may affect contract approval processes. |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | Conflict of interest management is a required element of the corporate compliance program. |\n| CO-CP-004 | Code of Conduct & Ethics | Conflict of interest obligations are a component of the agency's code of conduct. |\n| CO-CP-005 | Whistleblower Protection & Non-Retaliation | Reports of suspected undisclosed conflicts are protected under the whistleblower policy. |\n| CO-CP-006 | Compliance Hotline & Reporting Mechanisms | Available channel for reporting suspected undisclosed conflicts. |\n| CO-CP-007 | Compliance Investigation Process | Governs investigation of suspected undisclosed conflicts under Section 6.7. |\n| CO-FA-001 | Anti-Kickback & Stark Law Compliance | Disclosures implicating referral relationships are assessed for AKS/Stark Law risk under this cross-reference. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Establishes 7-year minimum retention for all conflict of interest records. |\n| HR-TA-003 | OIG/SAM Exclusion Screening | OIG exclusion screening is a parallel obligation for Governing Body members; conducted alongside conflict disclosure review. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n| EN-LC-001 | Policy Lifecycle Management & Version Control | Policy version control and lifecycle management for this policy. |\n\n---",
