        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All individuals within the scope of this policy shall receive orientation to this policy within fourteen (14) calendar days of appointment to a covered role. Orientation shall be conducted by the Compliance Officer and must cover: (a) the definition of a conflict of interest and examples relevant to a home health agency governance context; (b) disclosure obligations — when and how to disclose; (c) recusal requirements and procedures; (d) consequences of non-disclosure or failure to recuse; (e) available reporting channels for suspected conflicts by others; (f) whistleblower protections.\n10.2 All individuals within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within fourteen (14) calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new appointment.\n10.3 Annual refresher on conflict of interest obligations shall be incorporated into the annual conflict of interest disclosure process at the Q1 meeting. The Compliance Officer shall distribute a written summary of key policy requirements and any updates with the annual disclosure forms. The Governing Body Chair shall confirm completion of the refresher in Q1 meeting minutes.\n10.4 The Administrator shall maintain a tracking log of all policy acknowledgments and report any non-compliance to the Governing Body Chair within seven (7) calendar days of the acknowledgment deadline.\n\n---",
