        id: "8-development-and-maintenance-of-the-succession-plan",
        title: "Development and Maintenance of the Succession Plan",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Administrator | Prepare a draft Succession Plan (Appendix A) for all three key leadership positions. For each position, identify: (a) the current role holder's name, qualifications, and tenure; (b) the primary interim designee — name, title, confirmed qualifications, and contact information; (c) the secondary interim designee — same information; (d) a brief notation of any known factors that could affect designee availability (e.g., dual roles, geographic limitations). | Draft prepared no later than 30 calendar days before the Q2 Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.1.2 | Administrator | Verify the qualifications of each identified designee against the minimum qualification standards for the respective role: (a) Administrator designee — per policy GV-OG-002 and applicable California state requirements; (b) Clinical Manager designee — registered nurse license current and active in California; meets supervisory experience requirements under California Code of Regulations and CMS CoP; (c) Compliance Officer designee — sufficient knowledge of healthcare compliance, fraud and abuse, and HIPAA to operate the compliance program independently. | Qualification verification completed before submitting the draft plan. |\n| 6.1.3 | Administrator | Submit the draft Succession Plan and qualification verification documentation to the Governing Body Chair no fewer than 7 calendar days before the Q2 meeting. | At least 7 calendar days before Q2 meeting. |\n| 6.1.4 | Governing Body | Review, discuss, and approve or request revision of the Succession Plan at the Q2 regular quarterly meeting. The Governing Body shall specifically confirm: (a) the adequacy of each designee's qualifications; (b) the realism of designee availability; (c) the adequacy of the activation process. Approval shall be documented in Q2 meeting minutes. | At the Q2 regular quarterly meeting. |\n| 6.1.5 | Administrator | Distribute the approved Succession Plan to the Governing Body Chair and Compliance Officer. File the original in the restricted governance file. Notify each identified designee that they have been named in the plan and confirm their willingness to serve in the interim role if activated. Obtain written confirmation from each designee. | Within 7 calendar days of Governing Body approval. |\n| 6.1.6 | Administrator | Review and update the Succession Plan on a biennial basis in preparation for the Q2 meeting of the biennial review year, or immediately upon any of the following triggering events: (a) a current role holder departs, announces departure, or begins an extended leave; (b) an identified designee is no longer available, willing, or qualified; (c) a material change in the agency's organizational structure affects role definitions or reporting relationships; (d) the Governing Body directs an update. | Biennial review completed before Q2 of the review year; triggering event updates within 14 calendar days. |\n\n---",
