        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Current Role Holder | Provide written notice of an anticipated departure or extended leave to the Administrator and Governing Body Chair as early as possible and no less than 30 calendar days before the effective date of the vacancy, unless exigent circumstances prevent advance notice. | At least 30 calendar days before the vacancy effective date. |\n| 6.2.2 | Administrator | Upon receipt of an anticipated vacancy notice, immediately review the current Succession Plan and confirm the availability and readiness of the primary interim designee for the affected position. | Within 5 calendar days of receiving vacancy notice. |\n| 6.2.3 | Administrator | Notify the Governing Body Chair in writing of the anticipated vacancy, confirming: (a) the position affected; (b) the effective date of the vacancy; (c) the primary interim designee identified in the Succession Plan; (d) confirmation of the designee's current qualifications; (e) the recommended date for interim appointment. | Within 5 calendar days of confirming designee availability. |\n| 6.2.4 | Governing Body | Formally appoint the interim designee by Governing Body resolution or at the next regular or special meeting. Document the appointment in meeting minutes, including the designee's qualifications, the effective date of interim appointment, and the anticipated duration. | No later than the date of the vacancy if an anticipated vacancy allows advance scheduling; otherwise within 14 calendar days of the vacancy effective date. |\n| 6.2.5 | Administrator | Initiate recruitment for the permanent replacement immediately upon confirming the anticipated vacancy. Coordinate the transition plan between the departing role holder, the interim designee, and the recruitment process. | Recruitment initiated within 14 calendar days of confirmed vacancy notice. |\n| 6.2.6 | Departing Role Holder | Complete a knowledge transfer package (Appendix B) for the interim designee covering: (a) active projects and pending matters; (b) regulatory deadlines and upcoming compliance obligations; (c) key external contacts and relationships; (d) location of critical files, records, and passwords (as applicable per IT-SC-002); (e) open corrective actions or investigation matters. | Completed before the effective date of departure; if departure is immediate, completed within 7 calendar days as circumstances permit. |\n\n---",
