        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "CMS surveyors conducting a standard survey under SOM Appendix B will specifically verify:\nEvidence that the Administrator and Clinical Manager positions are continuously filled. Surveyors will confirm no undesignated vacancy exceeds 30 calendar days. They will request appointment documentation and verify interim designees meet minimum qualifications.\nEvidence of a proactive succession plan. Surveyors increasingly look for evidence of governance planning rather than reactive crisis management. A documented, Governing Body-approved succession plan with named and pre-qualified designees demonstrates governance maturity.\nEvidence that interim appointments were timely and documented. Surveyors will cross-reference the date of any vacancy against the date of interim appointment documentation. An undocumented gap is a survey risk even if the vacancy was brief.\nEvidence that interim designees were qualified. Surveyors will request credential documentation for interim designees. An interim Clinical Manager who is not a currently licensed RN in California is a Condition-level deficiency.\nEvidence that permanent replacements were recruited actively. Surveyors expect to see evidence of recruitment activity, not merely passive waiting, during the interim period.\n\n---",
