        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 The Administrator, Governing Body members, and each identified interim designee shall receive orientation to this policy within fourteen (14) calendar days of appointment or designation. Orientation shall cover: (a) the three key leadership positions covered; (b) qualification requirements for each role; (c) activation procedures for anticipated and unanticipated vacancies; (d) the 14-day interim and 90-day permanent appointment deadlines; (e) knowledge transfer expectations.\n10.2 Each identified interim designee shall confirm in writing that they have reviewed this policy and understand their obligations upon plan activation. Written confirmation shall be maintained in the restricted governance file.\n10.3 All individuals within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix D) within fourteen (14) calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new appointment.\n10.4 The Succession Plan shall be reviewed biennially as a standing Q2 agenda item. The review shall include confirmation of designee willingness and qualification currency.\n\n---",
