        title: "Self-Assessment Preparation",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Compliance Officer | Prepare the annual self-assessment materials for distribution to each Governing Body member. Materials shall include: (a) a copy of the Self-Assessment Tool (Appendix A); (b) a copy of the prior year's Governance Self-Assessment Summary Report and Improvement Action Plan for reference; (c) a copy of the current year's policy GV-GB-001 (Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities) for reference; (d) instructions for completing the self-assessment form. | Materials prepared and distributed to all Governing Body members no later than 14 calendar days before the Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.1.2 | Governing Body Chair | Review the prior year's Improvement Action Plan and prepare a brief status summary identifying: (a) improvement actions completed since the prior Q1; (b) improvement actions still in progress; (c) improvement actions not initiated with explanation. This summary will be presented at Q1 before the new self-assessment discussion begins. | Summary prepared no later than 7 calendar days before the Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.1.3 | Administrator | Schedule dedicated time within the Q1 meeting agenda for the self-assessment process. The agenda shall allocate a minimum of 30 minutes for: (a) prior year action plan status review (10 minutes); (b) individual member self-assessment completion if not completed in advance (10 minutes); (c) group discussion of aggregated findings (20 minutes). If members are asked to complete the self-assessment before the meeting, the agenda shall allocate at least 20 minutes for group discussion. | Scheduled and reflected in the Q1 agenda distributed 7 calendar days before the meeting. |\n\n---",
