        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Governing Body Chair | Present the prior year's Improvement Action Plan status summary at the start of the self-assessment agenda item. The Governing Body shall formally acknowledge completed actions and note any actions remaining open. | At the Q1 meeting, before new self-assessment discussion begins. |\n| 6.3.2 | Compliance Officer | Present the aggregated findings from the current year's individual assessments by domain. The presentation shall identify: (a) domains rated as strength (majority of members rated as performing well); (b) domains rated as needing improvement (significant number of members identified gaps or weaknesses); (c) any domain rated critically low by two or more members independently. | At the Q1 meeting, following presentation of the prior year status summary. |\n| 6.3.3 | Governing Body | Discuss the aggregated findings as a group. Discussion shall address: (a) the root causes of any domain rated as needing improvement; (b) whether the identified gaps reflect a training need, a process gap, a resource gap, or a structural governance issue; (c) specific, actionable improvements the Governing Body can make in the coming year; (d) whether any finding requires immediate corrective action (e.g., a gap in QAPI oversight or conflict of interest management that poses regulatory risk). | At the Q1 meeting; minimum 20 minutes allocated. |\n| 6.3.4 | Designated Secretary | Record in Q1 meeting minutes: (a) that the annual governance self-assessment was conducted; (b) the domains identified as strengths; (c) the domains identified as needing improvement (without attribution to individual members); (d) a summary of group discussion; (e) the Governance Improvement Action Plan items identified. Individual scores and individual responses shall not appear in meeting minutes. | In Q1 meeting minutes; completed within 14 calendar days of the meeting. |\n\n---",
