        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Governing Body Chair | Prepare or oversee preparation of the Governance Self-Assessment Summary Report (Appendix B) following the Q1 meeting. The report shall document: (a) the assessment period (calendar year assessed); (b) the number of members who completed individual assessments; (c) aggregated domain ratings — strength, satisfactory, or needs improvement; (d) identified governance strengths; (e) identified improvement priorities with supporting rationale. | Draft completed within 21 calendar days of the Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.4.2 | Governing Body Chair | Develop the Governance Improvement Action Plan as part of the Summary Report. For each domain rated as needing improvement, the plan shall specify: (a) the specific improvement action required; (b) the responsible party (Governing Body Chair, Administrator, or Compliance Officer); (c) the target completion date; (d) the success metric by which completion will be confirmed. | Included in the Summary Report draft within 21 calendar days of the Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.4.3 | Governing Body Chair | Distribute the draft Summary Report and Improvement Action Plan to all Governing Body members for review and comment. Members shall have 7 calendar days to provide written feedback. | Distributed within 21 calendar days of Q1 meeting; feedback period closes 7 days later. |\n| 6.4.4 | Governing Body Chair | Finalize the Summary Report incorporating member feedback and submit the final document to the Compliance Officer for filing. | Finalized within 35 calendar days of the Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.4.5 | Compliance Officer | File the finalized Summary Report and all individual self-assessment forms in the restricted governance file. Maintain individual forms as privileged records accessible only to Governing Body members and the Compliance Officer. | Filed within 3 calendar days of receipt. |\n\n---",
