        title: "Escalation and Exception Handling",
        level: 3,
        order: 13,
        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Fewer than a majority of Governing Body members complete individual self-assessment forms. | Governing Body Chair notifies Administrator in writing. | Chair issues a follow-up request to non-completing members with a 7-calendar-day deadline. If quorum of completed forms is not achieved, the group discussion and action plan are deferred to a special meeting. | Follow-up within 3 calendar days of Q1 meeting; special meeting if needed within 30 calendar days. |\n| Self-assessment identifies a critical regulatory compliance gap (e.g., QAPI oversight failure, conflict of interest management deficiency). | Governing Body Chair immediately escalates to Compliance Officer. | Compliance Officer assesses whether the gap constitutes an active compliance risk requiring corrective action under policy QA-AE-003. If so, a corrective action plan is developed separately from the Improvement Action Plan and tracked through the compliance program. | Compliance Officer assessment within 7 calendar days of Q1 meeting; corrective action plan within 14 calendar days if indicated. |\n| Governing Body declines to conduct the self-assessment in a given year. | Compliance Officer documents the failure in the annual compliance status report to the Governing Body. | Compliance Officer presents the documentation gap to the Governing Body at the next meeting with a recommendation to schedule the deferred assessment. | Documented in next compliance status report; presented at next quarterly meeting. |\n\n---",
