        id: "14-how-compliance-is-measured",
        title: "How Compliance Is Measured",
        level: 3,
        order: 14,
        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Annual self-assessment is conducted at Q1 each year. | Review of Q1 meeting minutes confirming self-assessment was conducted and aggregated findings were discussed. | Self-assessment conducted and documented in Q1 minutes in every calendar year. |\n| Majority of Governing Body members complete individual assessments. | Compliance Officer records number of completed forms received against current member roster. | Minimum 75% completion rate; 100% target; any non-completion documented with reason. |\n| Governance Self-Assessment Summary Report completed within 35 days of Q1 meeting. | Review of report filing date against Q1 meeting date. | Report finalized and filed within 35 calendar days of Q1 meeting in every calendar year. |\n| Governance Improvement Action Plan developed for all domains rated as needing improvement. | Review of Summary Report and Improvement Action Plan for completeness. | Every domain rated as needing improvement has at least one specific, time-bound action item with a named responsible party. |\n| Prior year's action plan reviewed at each Q1. | Review of Q1 meeting agenda and minutes for prior year action plan status item. | Prior year status reviewed at 100% of Q1 meetings; completed actions confirmed; open actions tracked. |\n\n---",
