        id: "10-annual-review-and-update-of-the-organizational-structure",
        title: "Annual Review and Update of the Organizational Structure",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Administrator | Conduct a comprehensive review of the organizational structure at least annually. The review shall assess: (a) whether the current structure supports the agency's defined scope of services (GV-OG-003); (b) whether staffing levels are adequate for each position and department (HR-WM-001); (c) whether all required positions are filled; (d) whether reporting lines are clear, functional, and free of gaps; (e) whether the structure supports regulatory compliance. | Annually; completed prior to the first quarterly Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.3.2 | Administrator | Present the results of the annual organizational structure review to the Governing Body. The presentation must include: (a) the current organizational chart; (b) any recommended changes; (c) identified gaps or risks; (d) staffing adequacy assessment. | At the first quarterly Governing Body meeting of each calendar year. |\n| 6.3.3 | Governing Body | Review, discuss, and approve or direct modification of the organizational structure. Approval or directed modifications must be documented in meeting minutes per GV-GB-002. | At the first quarterly meeting; follow-up within 30 calendar days if modifications are directed. |\n\n---",
