        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Key leadership position (Administrator, Director of Nursing, Compliance Officer) is vacant. | Governing Body per GV-GB-001, Section 6.5. | Governing Body appoints interim designee within 14 calendar days; permanent appointment within 90 calendar days. | Interim: 14 days. Permanent: 90 days. |\n| Organizational chart has not been updated within 14 calendar days of a known change. | Compliance Officer flags the deficiency to the Administrator. | Administrator updates the chart within 7 calendar days of notification. If not corrected, Compliance Officer reports to the Governing Body. | 7 calendar days from notification. |\n| An employee's job description conflicts with the organizational chart regarding reporting relationship. | HR Director escalates to Administrator. | Administrator resolves the discrepancy and updates whichever document is incorrect within 14 calendar days. | Within 14 calendar days. |\n| CMS surveyor identifies a gap or ambiguity in the organizational structure during survey. | Administrator convenes immediate corrective response. | Administrator prepares corrective documentation within the CMS-required timeframe (typically 10 calendar days) and presents to the Governing Body. | Per CMS Plan of Correction deadline. |\n| Organizational structure does not support the agency's scope of services. | Administrator reports to Governing Body. | Governing Body directs restructuring or scope of services modification within 30 calendar days. | Within 30 calendar days. |\n\n---",
