        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "CMS surveyors conducting a standard survey under the State Operations Manual (SOM) Appendix B will specifically verify:\nEvidence that a defined organizational structure exists. Surveyors will request the current organizational chart and review it for completeness, clarity, and evidence of Governing Body approval.\nEvidence that the Administrator is accountable to the Governing Body. Surveyors will look for a clear line of authority from the Governing Body to the Administrator, documented in the organizational chart and Governing Body minutes.\nEvidence that the Clinical Manager has authority over clinical operations. Surveyors will verify that the organizational chart positions the Director of Nursing with direct authority over all clinical services and clinical staff.\nEvidence that reporting relationships are understood by staff. Surveyors may interview staff at various levels to confirm they know their supervisor, chain of command, and escalation path.\nEvidence that the organizational structure supports the scope of services. Surveyors will assess whether positions and departments exist to support all services the agency claims to provide.\nEvidence that the organizational chart is current. Surveyors will compare the chart to actual staff roster and check for recent updates reflecting any changes.\n\n---",
