        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Primary regulatory basis. Requires a governing body with full authority and an organizational structure supporting agency operations. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(a) | Standard: Governing body | Mandates governing body responsibility for agency operations including establishment of organizational structure. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(b) | Standard: Administrator | Requires appointment of a qualified administrator within a defined organizational structure. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(c) | Standard: Clinical manager | Requires designation of a clinical manager with authority over clinical services within the organizational hierarchy. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.115 | Condition of Participation: Personnel qualifications | Defines qualification and scope requirements for personnel within the organizational structure. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.80 | Condition of Participation: Home health aide services | Defines supervision requirements that must be reflected in the organizational structure. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Provides interpretive guidelines for survey of 42 CFR § 484.105 including organizational structure and reporting line expectations. |\n\n### 9.3 State Requirements\n\n| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| California Health and Safety Code, Division 2, Chapter 8 — Home Health Agencies | Establishes state requirements for home health agency organizational structure and leadership. |\n| California Code of Regulations, Title 22, Division 5 — Home Health Agencies | Defines state licensure requirements including organizational and administrative standards. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-OG-001 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body approves organizational structure; appoints key leadership. |\n| GV-GB-002 | Board Meeting & Minutes Requirements | Governing Body approval of organizational chart documented in minutes. |\n| GV-OG-002 | Administrator Qualifications & Responsibilities | Administrator's role and reporting relationship within the structure. |\n| GV-OG-003 | Scope of Services Definition | Organizational structure must support the defined scope of services. |\n| GV-OG-005 | Delegation of Authority | Governs delegation within the organizational hierarchy. |\n| CO-CP-002 | Compliance Officer Designation & Authority | Compliance Officer's dual-reporting relationship within the structure. |\n| HR-TA-005 | Employee Orientation & Onboarding | Organizational chart presented during new employee orientation. |\n| HR-TA-006 | Job Description & Role Definition | Job descriptions must align with organizational chart reporting lines. |\n| HR-WM-001 | Staffing Levels & Workload Management | Staffing must support the organizational structure and scope of services. |\n| HR-JD-001 | Administrator | Job description for the Administrator position. |\n| HR-JD-003 | Director of Nursing / Clinical Manager | Job description for the Director of Nursing position. |\n| OP-FM-002 | Branch Office & Satellite Operations | Branch office reporting lines within the organizational structure. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Retention standards for organizational structure documents. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n\n---",
