        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All personnel within the scope of this policy (Section 3) shall receive orientation to the agency's organizational structure during initial onboarding per HR-TA-005. Orientation shall include: (a) review of the current organizational chart; (b) identification of the employee's position, direct supervisor, and chain of command; (c) explanation of how to escalate concerns through the chain of command; (d) identification of the Compliance Officer and the independent compliance reporting pathway.\n10.2 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix B) within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new hire/appointment.\n10.3 The Administrator shall maintain a tracking log of all policy acknowledgments and report any non-compliance to the Governing Body Chair within 7 calendar days of the acknowledgment deadline. Failure to acknowledge within the required timeframe shall result in written notification with a mandatory completion deadline of 7 additional calendar days.\n10.4 When the organizational structure changes, the Administrator shall communicate the change to all affected personnel in writing per Section 6.5.3. Affected employees shall confirm receipt and understanding in writing within 7 calendar days of notification.\n\n---",
