        id: "10-core-responsibilities-of-the-administrator",
        title: "Core Responsibilities of the Administrator",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "The Administrator of Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. shall fulfill the following responsibilities. While the Administrator may delegate specific tasks in accordance with GV-OG-005, the Administrator retains accountability to the Governing Body for all functions.\n#### 6.3.1 — Agency Operations Management\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1.1 | Administrator | Oversee the day-to-day operations of the agency including all clinical, administrative, financial, and compliance functions. Ensure all operations comply with federal, state, and local laws, the agency's policies, and the directives of the Governing Body. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.1.2 | Administrator | Maintain the agency's organizational structure (GV-OG-001) and ensure all positions are filled with qualified personnel. Report any vacancy in a key leadership position (Director of Nursing, Compliance Officer) to the Governing Body within 48 hours. | Continuous; vacancy reported within 48 hours. |\n| 6.3.1.3 | Administrator | Ensure the agency maintains current and valid: (a) California home health agency license; (b) Medicare certification; (c) Medicaid enrollment (if applicable); (d) accreditation (if applicable), per policy GV-EA-004. Report any lapse or risk of lapse to the Governing Body immediately. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.1.4 | Administrator | Implement and enforce all policies approved by the Governing Body and ensure operational compliance across all departments. | Continuous. |\n\n#### 6.3.2 — Personnel Administration\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.2.1 | Administrator | Ensure that the agency recruits, hires, and retains a sufficient number of qualified personnel to deliver all services within the defined scope of services (GV-OG-003), in compliance with HR domain policies. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.2.2 | Administrator | Ensure that all employees complete required orientation (HR-TA-005), mandatory training (HR-TD-001), and competency evaluations (HR-TD-003) within required timeframes. | Continuous; monitored quarterly. |\n| 6.3.2.3 | Administrator | Ensure compliance with all applicable employment laws including California wage and hour requirements, anti-discrimination laws, and workplace safety regulations. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.2.4 | Administrator | Oversee the agency's human resources functions including performance evaluation (HR-ER-001), disciplinary action (HR-ER-002), and separation processes (HR-ER-006). | Continuous. |\n\n#### 6.3.3 — Financial Management\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.3.1 | Administrator | Prepare the annual operating budget for Governing Body review and approval per FN-FP-005. | Annually; submitted to Governing Body at least 30 calendar days before fiscal year start. |\n| 6.3.3.2 | Administrator | Oversee the agency's revenue cycle including billing, claims submission, denial management, and collections per FN domain policies. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.3.3 | Administrator | Present a quarterly financial performance report to the Governing Body including: (a) revenue vs. budget variance; (b) accounts receivable aging; (c) claims denial rate and trending; (d) cash flow position, per GV-GB-001, Section 6.2.5.2. | Quarterly at each Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.3.3.4 | Administrator | Ensure the agency's financial records are maintained in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles and applicable regulatory requirements. | Continuous. |\n\n#### 6.3.4 — Regulatory Compliance and Quality Oversight\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.4.1 | Administrator | Ensure the agency maintains continuous compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations, CMS Conditions of Participation (42 CFR Part 484), and California home health agency licensure requirements. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.4.2 | Administrator | Support the Compliance Officer in operating the agency's corporate compliance program (CO-CP-001) and ensure the Compliance Officer has the authority, resources, and independence to perform compliance functions. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.4.3 | Administrator | Support the Director of Nursing and QAPI Coordinator in operating the agency's QAPI program (QA-PG-001) and ensure quality improvement activities receive adequate resources and leadership support. | Continuous. |\n| 6.3.4.4 | Administrator | Ensure the agency maintains continuous survey readiness (CO-RA-003) and coordinate the agency's response to any CMS survey, state survey, or accreditation review. | Continuous. |\n\n#### 6.3.5 — Governing Body Reporting and Communication\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.5.1 | Administrator | Attend all regular and special Governing Body meetings and present the Administrator's report including: (a) operational status; (b) key personnel updates; (c) regulatory compliance status; (d) significant incidents; (e) financial performance summary. | At each Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.3.5.2 | Administrator | Report critical events to the Governing Body Chair immediately upon occurrence, including but not limited to: (a) CMS or state survey findings; (b) serious patient safety events; (c) regulatory enforcement actions; (d) key leadership vacancies; (e) media inquiries involving the agency; (f) potential fraud or compliance violations. | Immediately upon occurrence. |\n| 6.3.5.3 | Administrator | Implement all directives issued by the Governing Body within the timeframes specified. Report completion or request an extension in writing to the Governing Body Chair. | Per Governing Body-specified deadline. |\n\n---",
