        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Primary regulatory basis. Requires appointment of a qualified administrator. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(b) | Standard: Administrator | Mandates that the administrator be qualified, authorized by the governing body, and responsible for day-to-day management. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(a) | Standard: Governing body | Governing body responsibility to appoint the administrator. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105(c) | Standard: Clinical manager | Relationship between administrator and clinical manager within organizational structure. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.100 | Condition of Participation: Compliance with Federal, State, and local laws | Administrator responsibility to ensure agency compliance. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Home Health Agencies | Provides interpretive guidelines for survey of 42 CFR § 484.105(b); defines surveyor expectations for administrator qualifications and documentation. |\n\n### 9.3 State Requirements\n\n| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| California Health and Safety Code, Division 2, Chapter 8 | State requirements for home health agency administration and licensure. |\n| California Code of Regulations, Title 22, Division 5 | State licensure requirements for home health agency administrators. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship to GV-OG-002 |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body appoints and evaluates the Administrator. |\n| GV-GB-002 | Board Meeting & Minutes Requirements | Administrator appointment and reports documented in minutes. |\n| GV-GB-004 | Succession Planning for Key Leadership | Succession plan for Administrator position. |\n| GV-OG-001 | Organizational Structure & Reporting | Administrator's position within organizational hierarchy. |\n| GV-OG-003 | Scope of Services Definition | Administrator ensures services align with scope. |\n| GV-OG-005 | Delegation of Authority | Governs Administrator's authority limits and delegation. |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | Administrator supports the compliance program. |\n| CO-CP-002 | Compliance Officer Designation & Authority | Administrator's relationship with Compliance Officer. |\n| HR-TA-002 | Criminal Background Check & Screening | Background check requirement for Administrator. |\n| HR-TA-003 | OIG/SAM Exclusion Screening | Monthly exclusion screening for Administrator. |\n| HR-JD-001 | Administrator | Job description defining Administrator qualifications and duties. |\n| HR-JD-002 | Administrator Designee | Job description for Administrator Designee. |\n| FN-FP-005 | Annual Budget & Financial Planning | Administrator prepares budget for Governing Body approval. |\n| GV-EA-004 | Agency Licensure & Certification Maintenance | Administrator ensures licensure/certification currency. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework under which this policy is classified. |\n\n---",
