        title: "Defined Scope of Services",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. is authorized and provides the following services within its defined scope. This list constitutes the agency's official scope of services and is maintained in detail in Appendix A.\n#### 6.1.1 — Core Services (Directly Provided)\n\n| Service Category | Service | Regulatory / Licensure Basis | Governing Policy |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Skilled Nursing | Comprehensive nursing assessment and skilled nursing care | 42 CFR § 484.75; California HCAI license | CL-SD-001 |\n| Physical Therapy | Physical therapy evaluation and treatment | 42 CFR § 484.115; California PT Board | CL-SD-002 |\n| Occupational Therapy | Occupational therapy evaluation and treatment | 42 CFR § 484.115; California OT Board | CL-SD-003 |\n| Speech-Language Pathology | Speech-language pathology evaluation and treatment | 42 CFR § 484.115; California SLP Board | CL-SD-004 |\n| Medical Social Work | Medical social work assessment and services | 42 CFR § 484.115; California BBS | CL-SD-005 |\n| Home Health Aide | Personal care and supportive services under RN supervision | 42 CFR § 484.80; California HCAI | CL-SD-006 |\n| Medication Management | Medication administration, reconciliation, and management | 42 CFR § 484.60; NPA | CL-SD-012, CL-SD-013 |\n| Wound Care | Wound assessment, treatment, and management | 42 CFR § 484.60; NPA | CL-SD-011 |\n| Patient Education | Individualized patient and caregiver education | 42 CFR § 484.60 | CL-SD-017 |\n\n#### 6.1.2 — Specialty Services (Directly Provided Based on Staffing Competency)\n\n| Service Category | Service | Staffing Requirement | Governing Policy |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| IV Therapy / Infusion | Intravenous therapy and infusion services | RN with demonstrated IV therapy competency | CL-SD-010 |\n| Diabetic Management | Comprehensive diabetic care and monitoring | RN with diabetic care competency | CL-SD-018 |\n| Cardiac Care | Cardiac assessment, monitoring, and management | RN with cardiac care competency | CL-SD-019 |\n| Respiratory Care | Respiratory assessment and oxygen therapy management | RN with respiratory care competency | CL-SD-020 |\n| Palliative Care | Palliative care support and hospice referral coordination | RN with palliative care training | CL-SD-023 |\n| Telehealth | Telehealth and remote patient monitoring | Clinicians trained in telehealth platform | CL-SD-009 |\n| Behavioral Health Screening | Depression and behavioral health screening and referral | Clinicians trained in PHQ screening | CL-SD-022 |\n\n#### 6.1.3 — Services Not Within Scope\nCare Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. does not provide the following services. Patients requiring these services shall be referred to an appropriate provider:\n\n| Service | Reason Not in Scope |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Hospice services | Separate licensure and certification required; agency is not hospice-certified. |\n| Private duty nursing (non-Medicare) | Not covered under Medicare home health benefit; separate licensure may apply. |\n| Durable medical equipment (DME) provision | DME supplier certification required; agency refers to qualified DME suppliers. |\n| Pharmacy / prescription dispensing | Pharmacy licensure required; not within home health scope. |\n| Inpatient or residential services | Home health agency is community-based only. |\n| Pediatric services (under age 18) | Not currently staffed with pediatric-competent clinicians; may be added per Section 6.3 if staffing capability is established. |\n\n---",
