        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Administrator | Conduct an annual review of the scope of services in consultation with the Director of Nursing. The review shall assess: (a) current licensure and certification status; (b) current staffing and competency capabilities; (c) community need and referral patterns; (d) quality and outcome data for each service line; (e) financial viability of each service line; (f) regulatory changes affecting the scope of services. | Annually; completed at least 30 calendar days before the first quarterly Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.2.2 | Administrator | Prepare a written scope of services review report and present it to the Governing Body. The report must include: (a) the current scope of services document (Appendix A); (b) any recommended additions or reductions; (c) supporting rationale for each recommended change; (d) staffing and resource implications; (e) regulatory implications. | Presented at the first quarterly Governing Body meeting or within 30 calendar days of fiscal year start. |\n| 6.2.3 | Governing Body | Review, discuss, and formally approve the scope of services for the upcoming year. Approval must be documented in meeting minutes per GV-GB-002. Any modifications directed by the Governing Body must be implemented by the Administrator within 30 calendar days. | At the first quarterly meeting. |\n| 6.2.4 | Administrator | Update Appendix A and distribute the approved scope of services to all department heads, intake staff, and referral sources within 14 calendar days of Governing Body approval. | Within 14 calendar days of approval. |\n\n---",
