        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Administrator | Initiate the annual strategic planning process by convening a strategic planning session with all department heads (Director of Nursing, Compliance Officer, HR Director, CFO/Revenue Cycle Director, Operations Director, IT Director, Risk Manager, QAPI Coordinator). | Q4 of the current planning period; at least 60 calendar days before the start of the new planning period. |\n| 6.1.2 | Administrator / Department Heads | Conduct an environmental assessment including: (a) SWOT analysis; (b) review of prior year strategic goal achievement; (c) regulatory environment scan (upcoming CMS rule changes, state requirements, OASIS updates); (d) financial performance review; (e) quality data review (Star Ratings, HHCAHPS, QAPI outcomes); (f) workforce analysis; (g) community and market assessment; (h) technology and infrastructure needs. | During strategic planning session(s). |\n| 6.1.3 | Administrator | Develop a draft strategic plan document that includes: (a) reaffirmed or updated mission and vision statement; (b) 3–5 strategic priorities for the upcoming year; (c) operational objectives for each priority (minimum 2 per priority) with KPIs, targets, timelines, and accountable parties; (d) alignment crosswalk to QAPI plan and budget; (e) risk assessment summary. | Within 30 calendar days of the strategic planning session. |\n| 6.1.4 | Administrator | Distribute the draft strategic plan to all department heads for review and comment. Incorporate feedback and finalize the draft. | Review period: 14 calendar days. |\n| 6.1.5 | Administrator | Present the final draft strategic plan to the Governing Body for review and approval. The presentation must include: (a) the full strategic plan document; (b) prior year goal achievement scorecard; (c) resource requirements; (d) risk assessment. | At the first quarterly Governing Body meeting of the planning period. |\n| 6.1.6 | Governing Body | Review, discuss, and formally approve the strategic plan. Approval must be documented in meeting minutes per GV-GB-002. The Governing Body may approve as presented, approve with modifications, or direct revisions with a defined resubmission deadline. | At the first quarterly meeting. |\n| 6.1.7 | Administrator | Distribute the approved strategic plan to all department heads within 7 calendar days of Governing Body approval. Each department head shall communicate relevant goals and expectations to their teams within 14 calendar days. | Distribution: 7 days. Team communication: 14 days. |\n\n---",
