        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Governing Body | Document the delegation of authority to the Administrator in a formal resolution or action recorded in Governing Body meeting minutes. The delegation must specify: (a) the scope of delegated authority; (b) retained authorities (Section 4.3); (c) financial authority limits; (d) reporting requirements; (e) effective date. | At the time of Administrator appointment; renewed annually at the first quarterly meeting. |\n| 6.1.2 | Governing Body Chair | Issue or update a written Delegation of Authority Letter to the Administrator that incorporates the terms approved by the Governing Body. The letter shall reference this policy (GV-OG-005) and the retained authorities in Section 4.3. | Within 7 calendar days of Governing Body action. |\n| 6.1.3 | Administrator | Acknowledge receipt of the Delegation of Authority Letter by signing and returning a copy to the Governing Body Chair. | Within 7 calendar days of receipt. |\n| 6.1.4 | Governing Body | Review the delegation to the Administrator annually. At the first quarterly meeting, the Governing Body shall confirm, modify, or revoke any delegated authority based on: (a) the Administrator's performance; (b) changes in agency operations; (c) regulatory changes. Document the review in meeting minutes. | Annually at the first quarterly meeting. |\n\n---",
