        title: "Administrator Delegation to Department Heads and Designees",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | Administrator | Identify functions that require delegation to department heads or designees to support efficient operations. Ensure the proposed delegatee meets minimum qualifications for the delegated function. | As needed; reviewed annually. |\n| 6.2.2 | Administrator | Complete the Delegation of Authority Form (Appendix A) for each delegation. The form must include: (a) identity of the delegatee; (b) specific function(s) delegated; (c) scope and limitations; (d) duration (standing or temporary); (e) reporting requirements; (f) conditions for revocation; (g) whether sub-delegation is permitted. | Prior to the delegation becoming effective. |\n| 6.2.3 | Administrator | Ensure the delegatee receives a copy of the completed Delegation of Authority Form and acknowledges understanding of the scope and limitations by signing the form. | Prior to the delegation becoming effective. |\n| 6.2.4 | Administrator | Maintain a Delegation of Authority Register (Appendix B) that lists all active delegations, delegatees, scope, effective dates, and expiration dates. | Maintained continuously; updated within 7 calendar days of any change. |\n| 6.2.5 | Administrator | Review all standing delegations at least annually and upon any change of personnel in a delegated role. Revoke, modify, or reissue delegations as necessary. Report active delegations to the Governing Body at the first quarterly meeting. | Annually; upon personnel change. |\n\n---",
