        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "#### 6.3.1 — Administrator Designee\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1.1 | Administrator | Designate a qualified individual to serve as Administrator Designee during planned and unplanned absences per GV-OG-002, Section 6.5 and HR-JD-002. The designee must meet minimum qualifications defined in GV-OG-002. | Prior to any absence; standing designation maintained at all times. |\n| 6.3.1.2 | Administrator | Document the designation using the Delegation of Authority Form (Appendix A). Specify: (a) functions the designee may perform; (b) financial authority limits during the Administrator's absence; (c) decisions that must be deferred until the Administrator's return; (d) reporting requirements to the Administrator during the absence. | Prior to the designation becoming effective. |\n| 6.3.1.3 | Administrator | Notify the Governing Body Chair when the Administrator Designee is activated for any absence exceeding 5 consecutive business days, per GV-OG-002, Section 6.5.2. | At least 7 calendar days before planned absence; within 24 hours for unplanned absence. |\n\n#### 6.3.2 — Clinical Designee (Director of Nursing Designee)\n\n| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.2.1 | Director of Nursing | Designate a qualified registered nurse to serve as Clinical Designee during absences per HR-JD-004. The designee must hold a current California RN license and demonstrate competency in clinical oversight functions. | Prior to any absence; standing designation maintained at all times. |\n| 6.3.2.2 | Director of Nursing / Administrator | Document the designation using the Delegation of Authority Form (Appendix A). The Clinical Designee's scope must clearly define authority over clinical operations, clinical staff supervision, and OASIS oversight. | Prior to the designation becoming effective. |\n\n---",
