        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. shall require documented acknowledgment of all agency policies by all individuals within scope of each policy, as a condition of employment, contract, and Governing Body membership.\n4.2 Policy acknowledgment shall occur:\nWithin 14 calendar days of initial hire or new appointment for all policies applicable to the individual's role\nWithin 14 calendar days of the effective date of any new policy applicable to the individual's role\nWithin 14 calendar days of the effective date of any substantive revision to an existing applicable policy\nWithin 14 calendar days of any role change that expands the scope of policies applicable to the individual\n4.3 Acknowledgment shall be documented using the standardized Policy Acknowledgment Form (see Appendix A of the applicable policy, or the general acknowledgment form in Appendix A of this policy). Electronic acknowledgment through the agency's designated platform is an acceptable alternative to paper forms, provided the system captures the individual's identity, date, and a confirmation of receipt and understanding.\n4.4 The Administrator shall maintain a centralized policy acknowledgment tracking log for all agency policies and all individuals within scope. This log shall be current at all times and available for CMS survey review.\n4.5 Non-compliance with acknowledgment requirements shall be escalated per Section 6.4 of this policy. Failure to acknowledge assigned policies within required timeframes may result in corrective action, up to and including suspension from patient care duties pending completion.\n4.6 Acknowledgment of a policy does not substitute for training. Where a policy requires training in addition to acknowledgment, both requirements must be independently satisfied and documented.\n4.7 Governing Body members and senior leadership shall acknowledge all REQUIRED-tier and Tier 4 — Privileged policies within 14 calendar days of appointment and within 14 calendar days of any revision.\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "module",
