        id: "6-definitions",
        title: "5\\. Definitions",
        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Policy Acknowledgment | The documented confirmation by an individual that they have received, read, and understood a specific policy and accept accountability for compliance with its requirements. |\n| Attestation | A formal declaration, signed or electronically confirmed, affirming that the individual understands and will comply with the obligations stated in the policy. |\n| Substantive Revision | A change to policy content that alters requirements, procedures, responsibilities, or compliance expectations. Formatting corrections and typographical fixes are non-substantive and do not require re-acknowledgment unless the Administrator determines otherwise. |\n| Electronic Acknowledgment | A digitally captured confirmation through an approved platform, containing the individual's identity credentials, timestamp, and affirmative confirmation of receipt and understanding. |\n| Acknowledgment Tracking Log | The centralized record maintained by the Administrator or designee documenting each individual's acknowledgment status for every assigned policy, including date completed and method of acknowledgment. |\n| Role-Based Policy Assignment | The process by which specific policies are assigned to individuals based on their position, scope of duties, and access tier, as governed by policy EN-LC-003. |\n\n---",
