        body: "| Escalation Level | Condition | Escalation Path | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Level 1 — Staff to Supervisor | Clinical concern, patient safety issue, or operational problem identified by frontline staff. | Staff notifies direct supervisor or Director of Nursing. | Immediately; no later than 1 hour after discovery. |\n| Level 2 — Supervisor to Administrator | Supervisor cannot resolve, issue has compliance or regulatory implications, or adverse event has occurred. | Supervisor or Director of Nursing notifies Administrator. | Within 2 hours of Level 1 escalation. |\n| Level 3 — Administrator to Compliance Officer | Issue has legal, regulatory, billing, or HIPAA implications. | Administrator notifies Compliance Officer. | Within 4 hours of Administrator notification. |\n| Level 4 — Administrator / Compliance Officer to Governing Body Chair | Condition-level survey finding, serious adverse event, key leadership vacancy, regulatory enforcement action, or fraud concern. | Administrator or Compliance Officer notifies Governing Body Chair. | Within 24 hours; immediately for imminent patient safety threats. |\n| Level 5 — Emergency Escalation | Imminent threat to patient or staff safety requiring emergency response. | Any staff member may directly contact 911 and/or the Administrator simultaneously, bypassing normal escalation hierarchy. | Immediately. |\n\n---",
