        title: "Investigation and Resolution",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Grievance Coordinator / Assigned Investigator | Investigate each grievance by: (a) reviewing relevant clinical records, billing records, scheduling records, or personnel files as applicable; (b) interviewing involved staff (ensuring non-retaliation); (c) consulting the Director of Nursing for clinical grievances; (d) consulting the Compliance Officer for compliance-related grievances; (e) documenting all investigative steps and findings. | Investigation initiated within 5 business days of receipt; completed within 30 calendar days. |\n| 6.3.2 | Grievance Coordinator | For grievances requiring longer than 30 days to resolve (complex clinical investigations, multi-party disputes, pending regulatory review), provide the complainant with an interim written status update every 14 calendar days until resolution. | Every 14 calendar days until resolution. |\n| 6.3.3 | Grievance Coordinator | Document the investigation findings and determination in the Grievance Register, including: (a) findings of fact; (b) determination (substantiated, unsubstantiated, or partially substantiated); (c) corrective actions taken or recommended; (d) responsible party and timeline for corrective action. | Within 5 business days of completing the investigation. |\n| 6.3.4 | Grievance Coordinator | Notify the complainant in writing of the investigation outcome, including: (a) the determination; (b) any corrective actions taken; (c) the complainant's right to escalate to external regulatory bodies if not satisfied with the agency's response, including contact information for HCAI, CMS, and the California ombudsman as applicable. | Within 5 business days of determination; no later than 30 calendar days from original receipt (or with interim updates per 6.3.2). |\n| 6.3.5 | Administrator | For grievances resulting in corrective actions, enter the corrective action into the agency's corrective action tracking system per policy QA-AE-003 and monitor completion. | Within 5 business days of determination; monitor per QA-AE-003 timelines. |\n\n---",
