        id: "8-tb-screening",
        title: "TB Screening",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | HR Director | Conduct TB risk assessment for all new employees using the CDPH-approved risk assessment tool. If the risk assessment indicates testing is warranted, arrange TB test (TST or IGRA). | Prior to first patient contact. |\n| 6.1.2 | HR Director | For employees with positive TB test results: (a) refer for chest X-ray within 5 business days; (b) if chest X-ray is normal, document baseline and conduct annual symptom screening (no repeat X-ray unless symptomatic); (c) if chest X-ray is abnormal, refer for medical evaluation and do not permit patient contact until clearance is obtained. | Within 5 business days of positive result. |\n| 6.1.3 | HR Director | Conduct annual TB risk assessment for all employees. Arrange repeat testing if indicated by risk assessment or known exposure. | Annually; per risk assessment results. |\n| 6.1.4 | HR Director | Track all TB screening results in the Employee Health Tracking System. Maintain records per OSHA medical records retention (duration of employment plus 30 years). | At each screening event. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
