        id: "11-fit-for-duty-and-return-to-work",
        title: "Fit-for-Duty and Return-to-Work",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Supervisor | When concern arises about an employee's fitness for duty, document the specific observations and consult with HR Director before initiating a fit-for-duty referral. | At the time of concern. |\n| 6.4.2 | HR Director | If a fit-for-duty evaluation is warranted, arrange evaluation with the agency's occupational health provider. Provide the provider with the job description and essential functions. | Within 5 business days of determination. |\n| 6.4.3 | Returning Employee | Provide written medical clearance to the HR Director specifying: (a) clearance for full or modified duty; (b) specific restrictions (if any); (c) duration of restrictions; (d) follow-up requirements. | Prior to return to duty. |\n| 6.4.4 | HR Director / Supervisor | If modified duty is recommended, evaluate whether reasonable accommodation can be provided per ADA/FEHA. Document the interactive process. | Within 5 business days of receiving clearance with restrictions. |\n| 6.4.5 | HR Director | Clear the employee for return to duty in the Employee Health Tracking System. Notify the supervisor. | At the time of clearance. |\n\n---",
