        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | HR Director | Issue a Conditional Offer Letter (Appendix E) to the selected candidate. The letter must clearly state that: (a) the offer is contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screening requirements; (b) the candidate may not perform any work duties until all screenings are completed and cleared; (c) a disqualifying result will result in rescission of the offer. | Within 2 business days of approved hiring recommendation. |\n| 6.4.2 | Candidate | Sign and return the Conditional Offer Letter acknowledging acceptance and providing written consent for all pre-employment screening activities. | Within 5 calendar days of offer issuance. If not returned within 5 days, the HR Director shall follow up; if not returned within 10 calendar days, the offer is automatically rescinded. |\n| 6.4.3 | HR Director | Initiate and coordinate completion of all required pre-employment screening: (a) Criminal background check per HR-TA-002; (b) OIG LEIE and SAM exclusion screening per HR-TA-003; (c) Professional licensure and certification verification per HR-TA-004; (d) Employment reference verification — minimum 2 professional references contacted and documented; (e) I-9 Employment Eligibility Verification — completed on or before the first day of employment per USCIS requirements; (f) Pre-employment health screening and immunization verification per HR-WM-003; (g) Drug screening per HR-ER-005 (if applicable under current agency policy); (h) Verification of education credentials as required by the job description; (i) Driving record check for any position requiring driving for agency business per RM-SS-003. | All screening initiated within 2 business days of signed conditional offer; all results received and documented prior to start date. |\n| 6.4.4 | HR Director | Document all screening results on the Pre-Employment Screening Checklist (Appendix F). Every screening item must show: (a) date initiated; (b) date result received; (c) result (pass/fail/pending); (d) reviewer initials. All results must be verified and documented before the candidate is cleared to begin work. No exceptions. | Completed and signed off before employee's first day of work. |\n| 6.4.5 | HR Director | If any screening result is disqualifying: (a) notify the candidate in writing per applicable fair chance/ban-the-box requirements (California Fair Chance Act); (b) provide required individualized assessment for criminal history results, considering the nature of the offense, time elapsed, and nature of the job; (c) allow the candidate the required response period before making a final adverse decision; (d) document the decision and rationale in the recruitment file. | Notification within 2 business days of disqualifying result; final decision after legally required response period. |\n| 6.4.6 | HR Director | For candidates not selected, send a professional declination notification. Retain all application materials and screening records in the recruitment file per CO-HP-007 (minimum 3 years or as required by applicable state law, whichever is longer). | Declination sent within 5 business days of position fill. |\n\n---",
