        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Requires the agency to employ qualified personnel and maintain organized personnel functions. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.80 | Condition of Participation: Home Health Aide Services | Defines qualifications, training, and competency requirements for home health aides. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.115 | Condition of Participation: Personnel Qualifications | Defines qualification requirements for clinical staff. |\n| 42 USC § 1320a-7 | Exclusion of Certain Individuals and Entities from Participation in Medicare and State Health Care Programs | Prohibits employment of excluded individuals. |\n| 8 USC § 1324a | I-9 Employment Eligibility Verification | Requires verification of employment eligibility. |\n\n### 9.2 State Regulations\n\n| Citation | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| California Health and Safety Code § 1725-1796.6 | Home Health Agency licensing requirements including personnel standards. |\n| California Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) | Prohibits employment discrimination; defines protected classes. |\n| California Fair Chance Act (AB 1008) | Restricts use of criminal history in hiring decisions; requires individualized assessment. |\n| California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) | Governs collection and use of personal information of applicants and employees. |\n\n### 9.3 OIG Guidance\n\n| Document | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| OIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies | Requires screening of employees and contractors against exclusion lists. |\n\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| HR-TA-002 | Criminal Background Check & Screening | Pre-employment background check requirements. |\n| HR-TA-003 | OIG/SAM Exclusion Screening | Pre-employment and ongoing exclusion screening. |\n| HR-TA-004 | Licensure & Certification Verification | Pre-employment and ongoing licensure verification. |\n| HR-TA-005 | Employee Orientation & Onboarding | Onboarding handoff from recruitment. |\n| HR-TA-006 | Job Description & Role Definition | Job descriptions required before recruitment. |\n| HR-WM-003 | Employee Health & Immunization Requirements | Pre-employment health screening. |\n| HR-WM-005 | Employee Personnel File Management | Personnel file establishment at hire. |\n| HR-WM-007 | Personnel File Content & Compliance Requirements | Mandatory personnel file contents. |\n| HR-ER-002 | Disciplinary Action & Progressive Discipline | Consequences for bypassing hiring process. |\n| HR-ER-004 | Anti-Harassment & Non-Discrimination | EEO compliance in hiring. |\n| HR-ER-005 | Substance Abuse & Drug-Free Workplace | Pre-employment drug screening. |\n| CO-HP-005 | Business Associate Agreement Management | BAA required for staffing agencies accessing PHI. |\n| CO-HP-007 | Record Retention & Destruction | Retention of recruitment records. |\n| CO-FA-003 | Fraud, Waste & Abuse Prevention | Response to excluded individual discovery. |\n| RM-SS-003 | Motor Vehicle Safety & Accident Reporting | Driving record check for driving positions. |\n| IT-UP-003 | Social Media & Public Communications | Standards for social media recruitment. |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing body appointments excluded from this policy. |\n| HR-JD-001 through HR-JD-011 | Job Descriptions | Position-specific qualification requirements. |\n\n---",
