        title: "Review of Background Check Results",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | HR Director | Upon receipt of background check results, review for: (a) criminal convictions (felony or misdemeanor); (b) pending charges; (c) sex offender registry matches; (d) discrepancies between applicant-provided information and screening results. Document the review on the Background Check Review and Determination Form (Appendix B). | Within 2 business days of receiving results. |\n| 6.3.2 | HR Director | If the background check is CLEAR (no convictions, no pending charges, no registry matches, no disqualifying discrepancies): mark the Pre-Employment Screening Checklist as PASS and proceed with remaining screening items. | Same day as review. |\n| 6.3.3 | HR Director | If the background check reveals a criminal history finding, proceed to Section 6.4 (Individualized Assessment) before making any employment decision. Do NOT automatically rescind the offer (except for automatic disqualifiers per Section 6.3.4). | Individualized assessment initiated within 3 business days. |\n| 6.3.4 | HR Director | If the background check reveals an automatic disqualifier (sex offender registration, abuse/neglect/exploitation of a minor, elderly, or dependent adult, healthcare fraud, or current federal program exclusion): the conditional offer is rescinded immediately. Issue a Pre-Adverse Action Notice, allow the required response period (minimum 5 business days per FCRA), then issue a Final Adverse Action Notice. Document on Appendix B. | Pre-Adverse Action Notice within 2 business days; Final Adverse Action after response period. |\n\n---",
