        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | HR Director | For criminal history findings that are NOT automatic disqualifiers, conduct an individualized assessment considering: (a) Nature and gravity of the offense(s); (b) Time elapsed since the offense or completion of sentence (including probation/parole); (c) Nature of the position sought and its relationship to the offense (e.g., access to vulnerable adults, financial responsibilities, driving requirements); (d) Evidence of rehabilitation (employment history, education, references, certifications obtained since offense); (e) Number and pattern of offenses; (f) Age of the applicant at the time of the offense. Document the assessment on the Individualized Assessment Worksheet (Appendix C). | Completed within 5 business days of receiving results. |\n| 6.4.2 | HR Director | If the individualized assessment results in a preliminary decision to rescind the offer: (a) Issue a Pre-Adverse Action Notice to the applicant providing a copy of the background check report and a written explanation of the preliminary decision per California Fair Chance Act requirements; (b) Provide the applicant at least 5 business days to respond with additional information, context, or evidence of rehabilitation. | Pre-Adverse Action Notice within 2 business days of preliminary decision. |\n| 6.4.3 | HR Director | If the applicant responds during the response period, review the additional information and update the Individualized Assessment Worksheet. If the additional information changes the determination, document the revised decision. | Updated assessment within 3 business days of receiving response. |\n| 6.4.4 | HR Director | If the final determination is to rescind the offer: issue a Final Adverse Action Notice informing the applicant of the decision, the specific conviction(s) that are the basis for the decision, and the applicant's right to file a complaint with the California Civil Rights Department (CRD). Document on Appendix B. | Final notice within 2 business days of final determination. |\n| 6.4.5 | HR Director | If the final determination is that the criminal history does not disqualify the applicant: document the rationale on Appendix C, mark the screening as PASS with conditions (if applicable), and proceed with remaining screening items. Retain the individualized assessment permanently in the confidential background check file. | Same day as determination. |\n| 6.4.6 | HR Director | For all adverse action decisions, consult with the Administrator and, if the case involves complex legal considerations, legal counsel per GV-EA-003, before issuing the Final Adverse Action Notice. | Prior to issuing Final Adverse Action Notice. |\n\n---",
