        body: "10.1 The HR Director and all HR staff responsible for initiating, reviewing, or acting upon background checks shall receive training on: (a) FCRA requirements including disclosure, authorization, pre-adverse action, and adverse action processes; (b) California Fair Chance Act individualized assessment requirements; (c) automatic disqualifiers; (d) confidentiality and record security requirements; (e) use of all appendix forms. Training shall be completed within 14 calendar days of assignment and refreshed annually.\n10.2 All hiring managers shall receive awareness training that: (a) background checks are mandatory and may not be bypassed; (b) no employee may begin work before clearance; (c) background check results are confidential and will not be shared with hiring managers (only PASS/FAIL). Training shall be part of the interviewer training required by HR-TA-001.\n10.3 All personnel within scope shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix D) within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date or new assignment.\n\n---",
