        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | HR Director | Upon confirming that a current employee, contractor, or Governing Body member is excluded: (a) immediately remove the individual from all duties — the individual may not provide any services, access any systems, or be present at any patient encounter; (b) notify the Compliance Officer in writing within 24 hours; (c) notify the Administrator within 24 hours. | Immediate removal; notification within 24 hours. |\n| 6.3.2 | Compliance Officer | Conduct a preliminary investigation to determine: (a) the effective date of the exclusion; (b) how long the individual has been working while excluded; (c) the scope of items and services furnished by the excluded individual during the exclusion period; (d) the total amount of any claims submitted to federal healthcare programs for items/services furnished by the excluded individual. Document on the Exclusion Incident Report (Appendix D). | Investigation initiated within 48 hours; completed within 14 calendar days. |\n| 6.3.3 | Compliance Officer | Calculate the agency's potential CMP exposure: up to $100,000 per item/service furnished by the excluded individual, plus treble damages on amounts claimed. Document the exposure calculation on Appendix D. | Concurrent with investigation. |\n| 6.3.4 | Compliance Officer | Report the finding and investigation results to the Governing Body Chair and Administrator in writing. Recommend whether self-disclosure to the OIG is warranted (generally recommended for any period exceeding a single pay period). | Within 14 calendar days of confirmed exclusion. |\n| 6.3.5 | Administrator / Governing Body | Direct the appropriate employment action. If the individual is excluded, employment must be terminated. Coordinate with legal counsel per GV-EA-003 regarding self-disclosure to the OIG under the OIG Self-Disclosure Protocol. | Employment action within 48 hours of confirmation. Self-disclosure decision within 30 calendar days per OIG guidance. |\n| 6.3.6 | HR Director | Terminate the excluded individual's employment effective immediately. Process separation per HR-ER-006. Revoke all system access per IT-SC-002. Document in personnel file. | Immediate upon direction from Administrator. |\n| 6.3.7 | Compliance Officer | If self-disclosure is directed, prepare and submit the self-disclosure to the OIG per the OIG Provider Self-Disclosure Protocol. Retain all documentation. Report status to the Governing Body at each quarterly meeting until resolution. | Self-disclosure submitted within 60 calendar days of discovery per OIG guidance. |\n| 6.3.8 | Compliance Officer | Conduct a root cause analysis to determine how the excluded individual was hired or how the exclusion was not detected earlier. Implement corrective actions per QA-AE-002 and QA-AE-003. | Root cause analysis completed within 30 calendar days. |\n\n---",
