        id: "8-pre-employment-licensure-verification",
        title: "Pre-Employment Licensure Verification",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | HR Director | Upon receipt of the signed Conditional Offer Letter (HR-TA-001), identify all licenses and certifications required for the position per the approved job description (HR-JD series). | Within 1 business day of conditional offer acceptance. |\n| 6.1.2 | HR Director | Conduct primary source verification for each required license/certification: (a) Access the issuing board's electronic verification system; (b) Verify: license number, license type, licensee name, issuance date, expiration date, status (active/inactive/expired), and any disciplinary actions or encumbrances; (c) Print or save a screenshot of the verification result with the date of verification visible. | Within 3 business days of conditional offer acceptance. |\n| 6.1.3 | HR Director | Document verification results on the Licensure Verification Record (Appendix B), including: (a) license type and number; (b) issuing state/board; (c) verification method (website URL, phone, written confirmation); (d) verification date; (e) status confirmed (Active/Unrestricted, Active/Restricted, Expired, Suspended, Revoked); (f) expiration date; (g) verifier's name and signature. Attach primary source evidence. | Completed concurrent with verification. |\n| 6.1.4 | HR Director | If the license is ACTIVE and UNRESTRICTED: mark the Pre-Employment Screening Checklist (HR-TA-001, Appendix F) as PASS and proceed. | Same day as verification. |\n| 6.1.5 | HR Director | If the license is RESTRICTED (active with conditions): notify the Director of Nursing. The DON shall review the specific restrictions and determine whether the individual can perform the essential functions of the position within the restrictions. If yes, document the determination and any practice limitations. If no, rescind the conditional offer. | DON review within 3 business days. |\n| 6.1.6 | HR Director | If the license is EXPIRED, SUSPENDED, or REVOKED: the individual is ineligible for employment in the licensed position. Rescind the conditional offer in writing. | Immediate upon verification. |\n| 6.1.7 | HR Director | For Home Health Aides: verify HHA certification or training completion per 42 CFR § 484.80. Acceptable documentation includes: (a) state-approved HHA training program completion certificate; (b) competency evaluation documentation; (c) if previously employed as HHA, verification from prior employer of completed training and competency evaluation. | Within 3 business days of conditional offer acceptance. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
