        id: "9-ongoing-licensure-monitoring",
        title: "Ongoing Licensure Monitoring",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | HR Director | Maintain a Licensure Expiration Tracking System (Appendix A) listing every licensed/certified employee, their license type(s), license number(s), and expiration date(s). | Ongoing; updated within 5 business days of any hire, separation, or renewal. |\n| 6.2.2 | HR Director | At least 90 calendar days before each license expiration date, send a License Renewal Reminder Notice (Appendix C) to the employee reminding them of: (a) the upcoming expiration; (b) their obligation to renew timely; (c) the requirement to provide evidence of renewal to HR; (d) the consequence of practicing on an expired license (immediate removal from clinical duties). | 90 days before expiration. |\n| 6.2.3 | HR Director | At 60 calendar days before expiration, if the employee has not yet provided evidence of renewal initiation, send a second reminder with copy to the employee's supervisor and the Director of Nursing. | 60 days before expiration. |\n| 6.2.4 | HR Director | At 30 calendar days before expiration, if renewal is still not confirmed, the Director of Nursing shall meet with the employee to confirm renewal status. If the employee indicates they will not or cannot renew, initiate workforce planning per HR-WM-001. | 30 days before expiration. |\n| 6.2.5 | HR Director | Upon expiration date: if the employee has not provided evidence of a current, renewed license: (a) immediately remove the employee from all clinical duties; (b) notify the employee in writing that they may not perform any clinical services until the renewed license is verified; (c) the employee may be placed on unpaid administrative leave or reassigned to non-clinical duties (if available) at the Administrator's discretion. | On the expiration date; no exceptions. |\n| 6.2.6 | HR Director | When the employee provides a renewed license: conduct primary source verification per Section 6.1.2 and update the Licensure Verification Record (Appendix B) and the Tracking System (Appendix A). Clear the employee to return to clinical duties only upon confirmed verification. | Verification within 2 business days of receiving renewal evidence. |\n| 6.2.7 | HR Director | Conduct an annual primary source re-verification of all licenses for all currently employed licensed staff, regardless of expiration dates, to identify any disciplinary actions, restrictions, or encumbrances that may have been imposed since the last verification. | Annually; completed within the first quarter of each calendar year. |\n\n---",
