        title: "Pre-Orientation Preparation",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | HR Director | Before the new employee's first day, prepare the orientation packet containing: (a) orientation schedule; (b) General Agency Orientation Checklist (Appendix A); (c) Role-Specific Orientation Checklist (Appendix B or C); (d) Employee Handbook; (e) key policy acknowledgment forms (compliance, HIPAA, safety, abuse reporting); (f) IT system access request form per IT-SC-002; (g) benefits enrollment materials; (h) emergency contact form. | At least 2 business days before start date. |\n| 6.1.2 | HR Director | Assign a preceptor for clinical staff orientation. The preceptor must: (a) hold the same or supervising licensure/discipline; (b) have at least 1 year of experience with the agency; (c) have no active disciplinary actions. Notify the preceptor and provide the Role-Specific Orientation Checklist. | At least 3 business days before start date. |\n| 6.1.3 | Hiring Manager / Supervisor | Prepare the new employee's workspace, equipment, supplies, and system access credentials (coordinated with IT per IT-SC-002). | Completed before start date. |\n\n---",
