        title: "Job Description Development",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Hiring Manager / Department Head | When a new position is created or an existing position requires a new/revised job description, draft the job description using the Job Description Template (Appendix A). | Prior to recruitment or upon triggering event. |\n| 6.1.2 | HR Director | Review the draft for: (a) ADA-compliant essential functions language; (b) FLSA classification accuracy; (c) alignment with applicable regulatory requirements; (d) consistency with agency organizational structure; (e) appropriate minimum qualifications. | Within 5 business days of receiving draft. |\n| 6.1.3 | Director of Nursing | For clinical positions: review and co-approve ensuring alignment with applicable professional practice acts, CMS CoP requirements, and HR-JD series policies. | Within 5 business days. |\n| 6.1.4 | Administrator | Provide final approval. Sign and date the job description. | Within 5 business days of DON/HR review. |\n| 6.1.5 | HR Director | File the approved job description in the master job description file. Distribute to the hiring manager. | Within 2 business days of approval. |\n\n---",
