        id: "10-outgoing-correspondence",
        title: "Outgoing Correspondence",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.3.1 | Originating Staff / Department | Prepare all outgoing official correspondence using agency letterhead. The correspondence must include: (a) agency name, address, and contact information; (b) date; (c) recipient name and address; (d) subject line; (e) body content; (f) signature of authorized representative; (g) enclosure notation if applicable. | At time of preparation. |\n| 5.3.2 | Originating Staff / Department | Obtain required approval before sending: REGULATORY correspondence — Administrator and Compliance Officer approval; LEGAL correspondence — Administrator approval; coordinate with legal counsel per GV-EA-003; CLINICAL correspondence — Clinical Manager approval; FINANCIAL correspondence — CFO approval; GENERAL correspondence — Department Head approval. | Prior to sending. |\n| 5.3.3 | Designated Mail Handler | Log all outgoing official correspondence in the Outgoing Mail Log (Appendix C). Record: (a) date sent; (b) recipient; (c) classification; (d) brief description; (e) method of delivery (USPS, courier, certified mail, fax); (f) tracking number (if applicable); (g) copy retained. | At time of sending. |\n| 5.3.4 | Designated Mail Handler | For correspondence requiring proof of delivery (regulatory responses, legal notices, appeal submissions), use certified mail, return receipt requested, or courier with tracking and signature confirmation. | At time of sending. |\n| 5.3.5 | Originating Staff / Department | Retain a copy of all outgoing correspondence in the appropriate departmental file and/or patient record as applicable. | At time of sending. |\n\n---",
