        id: "8-emergency-preparedness-plan-development-and-maintenance",
        title: "Emergency Preparedness Plan Development and Maintenance",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.1.1 | Operations Director | Develop and maintain the Emergency Preparedness Plan (EPP) addressing all four CMS-required elements: (a) risk assessment and planning (based on HVA); (b) policies and procedures; (c) communication plan; (d) training and testing program. | Initial development prior to Medicare certification; maintained continuously. |\n| 5.1.2 | Operations Director | Conduct or update the Hazard Vulnerability Analysis (HVA) annually using the HVA Worksheet (Appendix A). Evaluate at minimum: (a) earthquakes (California-specific); (b) wildfires; (c) power outages; (d) flooding; (e) severe weather; (f) pandemic/infectious disease; (g) cyberattack/data breach; (h) workplace violence; (i) civil unrest; (j) supply chain disruption. For each hazard, assess: probability, human impact, property impact, business impact, internal preparedness, and external preparedness. | Annually; updated within 30 days of any significant new hazard identification. |\n| 5.1.3 | Emergency Management Team | Review the EPP annually. Incorporate findings from: (a) the updated HVA; (b) after-action reviews from exercises and actual events; (c) regulatory changes; (d) community resource changes; (e) patient population changes. | Annually; minimum 30 days before Governing Body review. |\n| 5.1.4 | Governing Body | Review and approve the EPP annually at the third quarterly meeting per GV-GB-001. | Annually at Q3 meeting. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
