        title: "Emergency Activation and Response",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.3.1 | Any Staff Member / Incident Commander | Activate the Emergency Preparedness Plan when any of the following occurs: (a) a federal, state, or local emergency is declared affecting the agency's service area; (b) an event occurs that threatens the immediate safety of patients or staff; (c) the agency's ability to deliver essential services is disrupted; (d) the agency office becomes inaccessible or uninhabitable; (e) the IT/EHR system is down for more than 4 hours; (f) a public health emergency is declared (also activates OP-SL-006). | Immediately upon triggering event. |\n| 5.3.2 | Incident Commander | Upon activation: (a) assess the scope and severity of the event; (b) activate the EMT; (c) establish a command post (physical or virtual); (d) assign the emergency level: LEVEL 1 — WATCH: Potential threat identified; heightened awareness; no operational changes yet. LEVEL 2 — ALERT: Probable impact; modified operations initiated; patient prioritization begins. LEVEL 3 — EMERGENCY: Active impact; essential functions only; all non-essential operations suspended. | Within 1 hour of activation. |\n| 5.3.3 | Clinical Operations Lead | Activate the Patient Safety Priority Protocol: (a) Triage all active patients using the Patient Acuity Triage Tool (OP-SL-006 Appendix A); (b) ensure Priority 1 and 2 patients are contacted within 4 hours; (c) ensure all patients with life-sustaining needs (IV therapy, wound vac, insulin-dependent) have a care continuity plan; (d) coordinate with on-call clinicians for emergency coverage. | Within 4 hours of LEVEL 2 or 3 activation. |\n| 5.3.4 | Communications Lead | Activate the Emergency Communication Plan: (a) notify all staff of the activation and their instructions; (b) notify all patients per RM-EP-003; (c) notify the Governing Body; (d) coordinate with local emergency management if applicable; (e) notify CMS/State if required. | Within 2 hours of activation. |\n| 5.3.5 | Logistics Lead | Assess and secure: (a) staff availability and safety; (b) transportation and access routes; (c) supply inventory and access; (d) communication system functionality; (e) office/facility status. Report findings to Incident Commander. | Within 2 hours of activation. |\n| 5.3.6 | IT/Systems Lead | Assess IT system status: (a) EHR system availability; (b) communication systems; (c) data backup integrity; (d) remote access capability. If EHR is down, activate downtime procedures per OP-SL-005 Appendix B. If cyberattack suspected, activate IT-DR-005 Security Incident Response. | Within 1 hour of activation. |\n\n---",
