        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.7.1 | Incident Commander | Deactivate the EPP when: (a) the triggering event has resolved; (b) the agency can safely resume normal operations; (c) all essential functions have been restored. | When conditions warrant. |\n| 5.7.2 | Incident Commander | Upon deactivation: (a) notify all staff of return to normal operations; (b) notify all patients of service restoration; (c) notify external entities previously contacted; (d) begin recovery operations. | Within 4 hours of deactivation decision. |\n| 5.7.3 | Operations Director | Coordinate recovery: (a) restore all services to normal levels; (b) reschedule all missed visits within 48 hours per OP-SL-001; (c) complete all paper documentation data entry per OP-SL-005; (d) verify all patient care needs are addressed; (e) assess and replace damaged equipment or supplies. | Within 72 hours of deactivation. |\n| 5.7.4 | Operations Director | Conduct after-action review per Section 5.6.5. | Within 30 days of deactivation. |\n\n---",
