        id: "9-intake-screening-administrative",
        title: "Intake Screening — Administrative",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Intake Coordinator | Verify patient resides within the agency's defined service area per OP-IM-003. If outside the service area, proceed to Section 5.6 (Declination). | Within 2 hours (Urgent) / 8 hours (Routine). |\n| 5.2.2 | Intake Coordinator | Verify insurance/payer information: (a) confirm active coverage; (b) verify home health benefit eligibility; (c) identify prior authorization requirements; (d) confirm Medicare beneficiary status if applicable; (e) document verification results in the referral record. | Within 4 hours (Urgent) / 24 hours (Routine). |\n| 5.2.3 | Intake Coordinator | Collect and verify all required referral documentation: (a) physician face-to-face encounter documentation (if available); (b) hospital discharge summary (if applicable); (c) current medication list; (d) relevant medical history and diagnoses; (e) any existing orders or plan of care; (f) advance directive status; (g) emergency contact information. Document any missing items and initiate retrieval. | Within 24 hours of receipt. |\n| 5.2.4 | Intake Coordinator | Verify that the patient does not have an active episode with another Medicare-certified home health agency. If dual certification is identified, coordinate with the other agency and document resolution. | Within 24 hours. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
