        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.4.1 | Intake Coordinator | Upon clinical eligibility confirmation and payer verification, update referral status to ACCEPTED. | Immediately upon approval. |\n| 5.4.2 | Intake Coordinator | Notify the referral source of acceptance verbally and in writing. Provide: (a) estimated SOC date; (b) agency contact information; (c) after-hours contact number. | Within 2 hours of acceptance (Urgent) / within 24 hours (Routine). |\n| 5.4.3 | Intake Coordinator | Notify the patient and/or family/caregiver of acceptance: (a) introduce the agency; (b) provide the estimated SOC visit date and time window; (c) advise of patient rights notification (to be delivered at SOC); (d) collect any additional information needed for the SOC visit. | Within 4 hours of acceptance (Urgent) / within 24 hours (Routine). |\n| 5.4.4 | Intake Coordinator | Prepare and transmit the complete intake packet to the assigned SOC clinician: (a) referral documents; (b) clinical screening results; (c) payer/authorization information; (d) patient demographics and contact information; (e) advance directive status; (f) medication list; (g) any special instructions (interpreter needs, access instructions, safety concerns). | Prior to SOC visit; minimum 12 hours before scheduled visit. |\n| 5.4.5 | Operations Director / Scheduling | Schedule the SOC visit per CMS requirements: (a) URGENT — within 24 hours of acceptance or as medically indicated; (b) ROUTINE — within 48 hours of physician order date. Coordinate with the assigned clinician and confirm with the patient. | Per urgency and CMS requirements. |\n\n---",
