        title: "Acceptance Criteria Evaluation",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.1.1 | Intake RN | Evaluate the patient against each acceptance criterion using the Patient Acceptance Criteria Checklist (Appendix A). All criteria must be evaluated; no criterion may be omitted. | During clinical eligibility screening per OP-IM-001. |\n| 5.1.2 | Intake RN | For each criterion, document one of three findings: MET, NOT MET (with explanation), or PENDING (with action plan). | At time of evaluation. |\n| 5.1.3 | Intake RN | If all criteria are MET, recommend acceptance and proceed to admission per OP-IM-001 §5.4. | Immediately upon determination. |\n| 5.1.4 | Clinical Manager | If any criterion is NOT MET or if the case involves clinical complexity, the Clinical Manager shall review the determination and make the final acceptance/declination decision. | Within 4 hours of referral. |\n| 5.1.5 | Operations Director | If acceptance requires staffing redistribution or service area exception, obtain approval from the Operations Director prior to confirming acceptance. | Within 24 hours. |\n\n---",
