        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Criterion | Evaluation Standard | Documentation Required |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Skilled need | At least one qualifying skilled service (SN, PT, OT, ST) must be identified from referral documentation. If MSW or HHA only, must have a qualifying skilled service ordered concurrently. | Specific skilled need documented on Appendix A. |\n| Homebound status | Indicators of homebound status present in referral information (e.g., mobility limitations, cognitive impairment, assistive device use, medical restrictions). Full homebound determination completed at SOC assessment. | Homebound indicators documented; full determination deferred to SOC per CL-CA-005. |\n| Physician certification | Referring or attending physician identified and willing to certify the home health plan of care. Physician must be a Medicare-enrolled provider (for Medicare patients). | Physician name, NPI, and contact documented. |\n| Agency competency | The required services are within the agency's approved scope of services (GV-OG-003) and the agency has clinicians with appropriate training and credentials. | Verification against scope of services; competency confirmation. |\n| Staffing adequacy | The agency has available clinical staff within the patient's geographic area to initiate and maintain the ordered visit frequency. | Scheduling confirmation or Operations Director approval. |\n| Service area | Patient's residence is within the agency's defined service area per OP-IM-003. | Address verified against service area map. |\n| Payer coverage | Insurance verification completed; coverage for home health confirmed; authorization obtained if required. Self-pay patients must acknowledge financial responsibility. | Payer verification documentation; authorization number if applicable. |\n| Patient/caregiver consent | Patient (or legal representative) has been informed of services and has consented to receive home health care from the agency. | Verbal consent documented; written consent obtained at SOC. |\n\n---",
