        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Intake Coordinator | When a referral is received for a patient outside the defined service area, document the request and escalate to the Operations Director. | Within 4 hours of identifying out-of-area status. |\n| 5.2.2 | Operations Director | Evaluate the exception request considering: (a) distance from nearest agency clinician; (b) staffing availability; (c) ability to meet visit frequency requirements; (d) after-hours coverage feasibility; (e) patient acuity and safety. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.2.3 | Operations Director | Approve or deny the exception using the Service Area Exception Request Form (Appendix B). If approved, specify the duration and any conditions. | Within 24 hours of evaluation. |\n| 5.2.4 | Operations Director | Track all exceptions quarterly. If exceptions for a geographic zone exceed 5 per quarter, evaluate whether the service area should be formally expanded. | Quarterly tracking; expansion evaluation at threshold. |\n\n---",
