        title: "On-Call Schedule and Staffing",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.1.__ | Operations Director | Establish and maintain the on-call rotation schedule. The schedule must ensure: (a) a licensed RN is available on call at all times; (b) therapy on-call is available based on active caseload needs; (c) no clinician is assigned more than 7 consecutive on-call days without relief__ | Monthly schedule published by the 20th of the prior month. |\n| 5.1.2 | Operations Director | Distribute the on-call schedule to: (a) all clinical staff; (b) the answering service or call routing system; (c) the Administrator__ | Upon publication and with any changes. |\n| 5.1.3 | On-Call Clinician | Verify access to: (a) the on-call phone/device; (b) the EHR for patient records; (c) the emergency supply kit; (d) agency emergency contact list before each on-call shift begins__ | At start of each on-call shift. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
