        title: "RCA Report",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | RCA Lead | Prepare the RCA Report (Appendix A) documenting: (a) event summary; (b) RCA team composition; (c) data sources reviewed; (d) interviews conducted; (e) event timeline; (f) methodology used; (g) analysis findings; (h) identified root cause(s) with supporting evidence; (i) contributing factors; (j) system strengths identified; (k) recommended corrective actions with rationale, responsible parties, and measurable outcomes; (l) recommended monitoring plan to verify effectiveness. | Draft report completed within 30 calendar days of RCA initiation. |\n| 6.3.2 | QAPI Committee | Review and approve the RCA Report at the next QAPI Committee meeting. Committee may request additional investigation, modify recommendations, or approve as submitted. Document review in committee minutes. | At next QAPI Committee meeting following report completion; within 45 calendar days of event identification. |\n| 6.3.3 | RCA Lead | For sentinel events: prepare a preliminary findings summary for the Governing Body within 14 calendar days of event identification. The summary must include: (a) event description; (b) initial findings; (c) anticipated corrective actions; (d) expected RCA completion date. | Preliminary summary to Governing Body within 14 calendar days. |\n| 6.3.4 | QAPI Coordinator | Submit the final approved RCA Report to the Governing Body as part of the quarterly QAPI Performance Report. For sentinel events, provide the full report at the next Governing Body meeting following committee approval. | Per quarterly report schedule; sentinel event reports at next Governing Body meeting. |\n\n---",
