        title: "How Compliance Is Measured",
        level: 3,
        order: 14,
        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Patient Safety Program formally established and documented. | Review of QAPI Program Description. | Program documented and current. |\n| Patient safety indicators monitored monthly. | Review of QAPI dashboard. | All standing focus area indicators on dashboard; reviewed monthly. |\n| Proactive safety assessments conducted. | Review of assessment reports. | Minimum 2 per year. |\n| Safety culture assessed. | Review of assessment records. | Assessment completed at least every 2 years. |\n| Safety Huddles conducted monthly. | Review of Huddle documentation. | Monthly documentation with topics and attendance. |\n| Patient safety reported to Governing Body quarterly. | Review of QAPI Performance Report. | Included in all quarterly reports. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
