        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Establish and maintain the QAPI Committee with the following minimum composition: (a) QAPI Coordinator (Chair); (b) Director of Nursing / Clinical Manager; (c) Administrator or designee; (d) at least one representative from each active clinical discipline (nursing, therapy, aide services); (e) Compliance Officer or designee (standing invitation). Additional members may include intake, scheduling, billing, and HR representatives as needed for specific agenda items. | Committee established within 30 calendar days of program establishment; membership roster updated within 7 calendar days of any change. |\n| 6.2.2 | QAPI Coordinator | Convene QAPI Committee meetings no fewer than monthly. Meeting schedule for the upcoming quarter must be established and distributed to all members at least 14 calendar days before the start of the quarter. | Monthly; schedule distributed quarterly. |\n| 6.2.3 | QAPI Coordinator | Prepare and distribute the meeting agenda to all QAPI Committee members no fewer than 5 business days before each meeting. The agenda must include standing items: (a) review of prior meeting minutes and action items; (b) quality indicator dashboard review; (c) active PIP status updates; (d) adverse event and incident summary; (e) infection surveillance summary; (f) patient satisfaction data; (g) regulatory/survey update; (h) new business. | 5 business days before each meeting. |\n| 6.2.4 | QAPI Coordinator | Record formal minutes for each QAPI Committee meeting. Minutes must document: (a) date, time, and attendees; (b) each agenda item discussed with key findings; (c) all decisions and directives issued; (d) assigned responsible parties and deadlines for each action item; (e) follow-up items carried forward from prior meetings. | Draft minutes completed within 7 calendar days of the meeting; distributed to all committee members and filed in QAPI records. |\n| 6.2.5 | QAPI Committee | Review and act upon the quality indicator dashboard at each meeting. For any indicator that falls below the defined performance threshold for 2 consecutive reporting periods: (a) determine whether a root cause analysis is required; (b) assign a responsible party for investigation; (c) establish a deadline for findings and recommended action; (d) document the committee's analysis and decision in meeting minutes. | At each monthly meeting. |\n| 6.2.6 | QAPI Coordinator | Maintain a QAPI Action Item Tracker that documents all open and closed action items, including: assigned party, deadline, current status, completion date, and outcome. Present the tracker at each committee meeting. | Updated continuously; presented monthly. |\n\n---",
