        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Prepare and submit a written QAPI Performance Report to the Governing Body no fewer than 7 calendar days before each quarterly Governing Body meeting. The report must include: (a) quality indicator trends with comparison to prior quarter and national benchmarks; (b) status of all active PIPs including progress against measurable goals; (c) adverse event summary with root cause analysis findings; (d) patient satisfaction data and HHCAHPS trends; (e) Star Rating / Home Health Compare trends; (f) infection surveillance summary; (g) open corrective action plans with status; (h) recommendations for Governing Body action. | 7 calendar days before each quarterly Governing Body meeting. |\n| 6.3.2 | Governing Body | Review, discuss, and document its response to the quarterly QAPI Performance Report per policy GV-GB-001, Section 6.2.4. If any quality indicator falls below threshold for 2 consecutive quarters, the Governing Body shall direct corrective action, assign accountability, and establish a resolution deadline. | At each quarterly meeting; corrective directives within 14 calendar days if thresholds are breached. |\n| 6.3.3 | Governing Body | Review and approve the annual QAPI plan per policy QA-PG-002 at the first quarterly meeting of each calendar year. | Annually at Q1 meeting. |\n| 6.3.4 | QAPI Coordinator | Report any patient safety event classified as a sentinel event or any adverse event resulting in patient death, hospitalization, or permanent harm to the Governing Body within 72 hours of agency awareness. Interim report may be verbal with written follow-up within 7 calendar days. | Within 72 hours of agency awareness; written follow-up within 7 calendar days. |\n\n---",
