        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | QAPI Coordinator / Compliance Officer | Establish a defined coordination protocol between the QAPI program and the Compliance program (CO-CP-001) to ensure: (a) compliance audit findings that indicate quality or patient safety implications are referred to the QAPI Committee; (b) QAPI findings that indicate potential regulatory non-compliance are referred to the Compliance Officer; (c) duplicative investigation is avoided through joint review when appropriate. | Protocol established within 60 days of program establishment; reviewed annually. |\n| 6.4.2 | QAPI Coordinator / Risk Manager | Establish a defined coordination protocol between the QAPI program and the Risk Management program (RM-ER-001) to ensure: (a) incident reports are routed to the QAPI Committee for trending and pattern analysis; (b) risk assessment findings inform QAPI priority-setting; (c) corrective action plans developed under either program are tracked centrally. | Protocol established within 60 days of program establishment; reviewed annually. |\n| 6.4.3 | QAPI Coordinator / Director of Nursing | Ensure the QAPI program encompasses all clinical service lines including: (a) skilled nursing; (b) physical therapy; (c) occupational therapy; (d) speech-language pathology; (e) medical social work; (f) home health aide services; (g) any specialty programs (telehealth, infusion, wound care). No clinical program shall operate outside QAPI monitoring. | Ongoing; verified annually during QAPI plan review. |\n| 6.4.4 | QAPI Coordinator | Maintain a QAPI Data Source Inventory documenting all data inputs to the program including: source system, data type, frequency of collection, responsible party, and quality indicator(s) derived. Data sources must include at minimum: (a) OASIS outcome data; (b) claims/billing data; (c) incident/adverse event reports; (d) patient satisfaction surveys/HHCAHPS; (e) infection surveillance data; (f) staff competency records; (g) Home Health Compare / Star Rating data; (h) documentation audit results; (i) compliance audit findings. | Inventory established within 90 days of program establishment; updated annually or when data sources change. |\n\n---",
