        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Condition | Escalation Path | Corrective Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| QAPI Committee fails to meet for 2 consecutive months | QAPI Coordinator notifies Administrator and Compliance Officer in writing. | Administrator directs immediate scheduling of a meeting. If pattern persists for a third month, Compliance Officer documents the deficiency and initiates corrective action per QA-AE-003. The deficiency is reported to the Governing Body at the next quarterly meeting. | Make-up meeting within 14 calendar days of missed month. |\n| QAPI Coordinator position vacant for more than 30 calendar days | Administrator escalates to Governing Body. | Governing Body designates an interim QAPI Coordinator within 14 calendar days of vacancy. Permanent appointment within 90 calendar days. Interim designee must meet minimum qualifications in Section 6.1.2. | Interim: 14 days. Permanent: 90 days. |\n| Quality indicator falls below defined threshold for 3 consecutive reporting periods without documented corrective action | QAPI Coordinator escalates to Governing Body via special written report. | Governing Body directs immediate development of a corrective action plan per QA-AE-003 with a designated lead, measurable goals, and resolution deadline not to exceed 90 calendar days. Governing Body receives monthly status updates until resolved. | CAP initiated within 14 calendar days; resolved within 90 days. |\n| CMS survey identifies QAPI-related deficiency | Administrator convenes QAPI Committee within 48 hours of survey exit. | QAPI Committee develops Plan of Correction within CMS-required timeframe (typically 10 calendar days). Governing Body receives immediate notification and weekly status updates until resolution confirmed. | Committee convened within 48 hours; POC per CMS deadline. |\n| Staff non-participation in QAPI activities (failure to report events, submit data, or attend required meetings) | Department supervisor documents non-participation and reports to QAPI Coordinator. | QAPI Coordinator notifies the employee's supervisor. Repeated non-participation (3 or more instances within a 12-month period) is addressed through progressive discipline per HR-ER-002. | Notification within 5 business days of identified non-participation. |\n\n---",
