        id: "14-surveyor-expectations",
        title: "Surveyor Expectations",
        level: 3,
        order: 14,
        body: "CMS surveyors conducting a standard survey under SOM Appendix B will specifically verify:\nEvidence that a QAPI program exists and functions. Surveyors will request the QAPI plan, QAPI Program Description, and committee meeting minutes. An agency that cannot produce these documents will face an immediate Condition-level inquiry under 42 CFR § 484.65.\nEvidence that the QAPI program is agency-wide. Surveyors will verify that all service lines — not just nursing — are monitored by the QAPI program. A program limited to a single discipline will be cited as non-compliant.\nEvidence that the QAPI program is data-driven. Surveyors will look for measurable indicators, dashboards, trending data, and documented analysis. Programs that rely solely on anecdotal discussion without data will be cited.\nEvidence that the Governing Body exercises oversight. Surveyors will cross-reference QAPI Committee reports with Governing Body minutes to verify that the Governing Body receives, reviews, discusses, and acts upon quality data. Passive receipt of reports without documented discussion or action is a common deficiency.\nEvidence that performance improvement projects exist. Surveyors will request documentation of active and completed PIPs including methodology, data, and results. An agency with no active PIPs will be cited.\nEvidence that adverse events are identified, reported, and acted upon. Surveyors will review the adverse event reporting process, investigation records, and corrective action documentation.\nEvidence that the QAPI program leads to measurable improvement. Surveyors will look for documented improvement trends, not just identification of problems. A program that identifies issues but shows no improvement over time will be cited for ineffectiveness.\n\n---",
