        id: "24-references",
        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations (42 CFR Part 484)\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65 | Condition of Participation: Quality Assessment and Performance Improvement | Primary regulatory basis for this policy. Requires an effective, ongoing, agency-wide, data-driven QAPI program. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65(a) | Standard: Program scope | Requires QAPI program to reflect complexity of organization and services; maintain quality through ongoing programs for improvement. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65(b) | Standard: Program data | Requires use of quality indicator data including patient care, OASIS, and other relevant data to monitor effectiveness of care. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65(c) | Standard: Program activities | Requires performance improvement projects focused on high-priority areas; tracking indicators over time. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65(d) | Standard: Performance improvement projects | Mandates PIPs proportionate to scope/complexity; requires measurable goals and sustained improvement. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65(e) | Standard: Executive responsibilities | Governing body responsible for QAPI program; ensuring adequate resources; approving QAPI plan. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration of Services | Governing body oversight of all agency programs including QAPI. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.70 | Condition of Participation: Infection Prevention and Control | Infection surveillance as QAPI data source. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.60 | Condition of Participation: Care planning, coordination, and quality of care | Clinical care quality as QAPI monitoring target. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.50 | Condition of Participation: Patient rights | Patient experience and rights as QAPI monitoring target. |\n\n### 9.2 CMS Guidance\nCMS State Operations Manual, Appendix B — Guidance to Surveyors: Provides interpretive guidelines for survey of 42 CFR § 484.65 compliance; defines surveyor expectations for QAPI program evidence, data use, and governing body involvement.\nCMS OASIS-E2 Guidance Manual: OASIS outcome data serves as a primary data source for the QAPI program.\nCMS Home Health Quality Reporting Program (HH QRP): Defines quality measures reported publicly on Home Health Compare; QAPI program must monitor these measures.\n### 9.3 OIG Guidance\nOIG Compliance Program Guidance for Home Health Agencies: Establishes expectation that quality monitoring is integrated with the compliance program and that the governing body receives regular quality performance reports.\n### 9.4 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body oversight of QAPI program; quarterly report review. |\n| QA-PG-002 | QAPI Plan Development & Annual Review | Annual QAPI plan governed by this program framework. |\n| QA-PG-003 | QAPI Committee Structure & Meeting Requirements | Detailed committee operations under this governance structure. |\n| QA-PI-001 | Performance Improvement Project Management | PIP methodology and management within QAPI program. |\n| QA-PI-002 | Quality Indicator Monitoring & Reporting | Quality indicator dashboard and monitoring procedures. |\n| QA-AE-001 | Adverse Event Identification & Reporting | Adverse event reporting within QAPI framework. |\n| QA-AE-002 | Root Cause Analysis Process | RCA methodology for adverse events. |\n| QA-AE-003 | Corrective Action Plan Development & Tracking | CAP process for QAPI-identified deficiencies. |\n| QA-AE-004 | Patient Safety Program | Patient safety program integration with QAPI. |\n| QA-SM-001 | Utilization Review & Management | Utilization data as QAPI input. |\n| QA-SM-002 | Infection Surveillance & Trending | Infection data as QAPI input. |\n| QA-SM-003 | Patient Satisfaction Survey & Analysis | Patient satisfaction data as QAPI input. |\n| QA-SM-004 | Home Health Compare & Star Rating Monitoring | Star Rating data reported to Governing Body through QAPI. |\n| QA-SM-005 | Policy Effectiveness Monitoring and Outcome Validation | Policy outcome measurement integrated with QAPI. |\n| CO-CP-001 | Corporate Compliance Program | QAPI-Compliance coordination protocol. |\n| RM-ER-001 | Enterprise Risk Management Program | QAPI-Risk Management coordination protocol. |\n| CL-SD-016 | Infection Prevention & Control | Infection prevention program integration. |\n| HR-TD-003 | Clinical Staff Competency Evaluation | Competency data as QAPI input. |\n| HR-ER-002 | Disciplinary Action & Progressive Discipline | Escalation for staff non-participation. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework classification of this policy. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "module",
