        title: "Annual QAPI Plan Development",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Initiate the annual QAPI plan development process by conducting a comprehensive year-end quality assessment that includes: (a) review of all quality indicator trends for the current plan year; (b) analysis of PIP outcomes and sustainability; (c) review of adverse event and incident data; (d) review of patient satisfaction and HHCAHPS results; (e) review of Star Rating trends and Home Health Compare data; (f) review of infection surveillance data; (g) review of compliance audit findings and CMS survey results; (h) review of staff competency evaluation results; (i) feedback from QAPI Committee members and department heads; (j) assessment of new or changing regulatory requirements. | Begin no later than October 1 of each year; year-end assessment completed by November 30. |\n| 6.1.2 | QAPI Coordinator | Based on the year-end assessment, identify and prioritize quality improvement focus areas for the upcoming plan year. Selection criteria must include: (a) areas where performance is below national benchmarks or internal thresholds; (b) areas with adverse event patterns; (c) areas where regulatory changes require focused attention; (d) areas identified by the Governing Body or Administrator as strategic priorities; (e) areas where prior PIPs require sustainment monitoring. Present proposed priorities to the QAPI Committee for discussion and input. | Draft priorities presented to QAPI Committee by November meeting. |\n| 6.1.3 | QAPI Coordinator | Develop the draft QAPI plan for the upcoming year. The plan must contain all elements specified in Section 6.2 (Required Plan Content). | Draft completed by December 1. |\n| 6.1.4 | QAPI Committee | Review the draft QAPI plan at the December meeting. Provide feedback, request modifications, and approve the final draft for submission to the Governing Body. | December QAPI Committee meeting. |\n| 6.1.5 | QAPI Coordinator | Submit the final QAPI plan to the Governing Body no later than December 15, along with a written summary of the year-end assessment findings and the rationale for selected priorities. | Submitted by December 15. |\n| 6.1.6 | Governing Body | Review and approve the QAPI plan at the first quarterly meeting of the plan year. Approval must be documented in Governing Body meeting minutes and must include: (a) confirmation that the plan reflects the agency's scope and complexity; (b) confirmation that adequate resources are allocated; (c) any modifications directed by the Governing Body. | Q1 Governing Body meeting (per GV-GB-001 §6.2.4.1). |\n\n---",
