        level: 2,
        order: 5,
        body: "4.1 Care Indeed Home Health Care, Inc. shall maintain a standing multidisciplinary QAPI Committee that serves as the primary operational body for quality assessment and performance improvement activities.\n4.2 The QAPI Committee shall be chaired by the QAPI Coordinator. In the absence of the QAPI Coordinator, the Director of Nursing shall serve as acting chair.\n4.3 The QAPI Committee shall meet no fewer than 12 times per calendar year (monthly). Special meetings shall be convened when urgent quality or safety matters arise.\n4.4 Committee membership shall include representation from all active clinical disciplines, administration, and compliance to ensure agency-wide perspective in quality monitoring.\n4.5 All committee decisions, directives, and action items shall be documented in formal meeting minutes with assigned responsible parties, deadlines, and follow-up requirements.\n4.6 The QAPI Committee shall serve as the primary conduit for escalating quality and safety concerns to the Governing Body through the quarterly QAPI Performance Report prepared by the QAPI Coordinator.\n4.7 Committee attendance shall be monitored. Members who miss 3 or more meetings within a 12-month period without documented cause shall be replaced.\n4.8 Only the most current approved version of this policy shall be considered valid.\n\n---",
