        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | PIP Lead | Upon achieving the measurable goal, prepare a PIP Completion Report that includes: (a) final data compared to baseline and target; (b) summary of all interventions implemented and PDSA cycles completed; (c) analysis of what worked and what did not; (d) lessons learned; (e) sustainment plan with monitoring schedule (minimum 3-month sustainment monitoring period); (f) recommendation for formal closure or transition to ongoing monitoring. | Within 30 calendar days of goal achievement. |\n| 6.4.2 | QAPI Committee | Review the PIP Completion Report. If the committee confirms the goal was achieved and the sustainment plan is adequate, approve formal closure. If sustainment monitoring reveals regression, the committee may reopen the PIP or initiate a new PIP. Document in committee minutes. | At QAPI Committee meeting following report submission. |\n| 6.4.3 | PIP Lead | During the 3-month sustainment monitoring period, collect data per the sustainment plan schedule and report results to the QAPI Committee. If performance declines below the achieved target by more than 10%, notify the QAPI Coordinator immediately for committee review. | Monthly during 3-month sustainment period. |\n| 6.4.4 | QAPI Coordinator | Archive the completed PIP file including: charter, all monthly reports, data tracking document, completion report, and sustainment data. Completed PIPs serve as evidence for CMS survey review. | Within 14 calendar days of formal closure. |\n\n---",
