        id: "10-reporting",
        title: "Reporting",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Present the complete Quality Indicator Dashboard to the QAPI Committee at each monthly meeting. Presentation must include: current data, trend analysis, flagged indicators, recommended actions, and status of previously triggered corrective actions. | Monthly at each committee meeting. |\n| 6.3.2 | QAPI Committee | Review dashboard data and take action: (a) for indicators at or above threshold — acknowledge and document; (b) for indicators in caution zone — identify contributing factors and preventive measures; (c) for indicators below threshold — initiate corrective action analysis per Section 6.4; (d) for indicators requiring escalation — direct escalation per Section 6.5. Document all discussion and decisions in committee minutes. | At each monthly meeting. |\n| 6.3.3 | QAPI Coordinator | Include dashboard summary in the quarterly QAPI Performance Report to the Governing Body per QA-PG-001 Section 6.3.1. Highlight: (a) indicators below threshold; (b) indicators showing improvement; (c) indicators requiring Governing Body attention. | Quarterly per GV-GB-001 schedule. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
