        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.2.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Analyze competency data alongside quality indicators, adverse event data, and patient outcome data to identify potential competency-quality correlations. Examples: (a) wound care competency deficiencies correlating with declining wound healing outcome rates; (b) OASIS competency deficiencies correlating with coding accuracy issues; (c) medication management competency deficiencies correlating with medication error incident reports; (d) fall prevention competency deficiencies correlating with increased fall rates. | Quarterly following receipt of Competency Summary Report. |\n| 6.2.2 | QAPI Committee | Review the competency-quality correlation analysis. For each identified correlation: (a) validate the correlation with additional data if needed; (b) determine root cause (individual skill gap, training gap, process gap, resource gap); (c) determine the appropriate system-level response (targeted education, process redesign, PIP, supervision enhancement, tool/template modification). Document analysis and decision in committee minutes. | At the quarterly QAPI Committee meeting. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
