        id: "10-system-level-response",
        title: "System-Level Response",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | QAPI Committee | When a systemic competency pattern (per Section 4.3) is identified, assign one of the following responses: (a) Targeted Education — develop and deliver focused training on the identified competency area, with post-training reassessment; (b) Process Redesign — modify the work process, template, or tool to reduce reliance on the deficient competency area; (c) PIP — initiate a formal PIP per QA-PI-001 if the competency pattern correlates with a significant quality gap; (d) Enhanced Supervision — increase supervisory oversight for the affected competency area. Assign a responsible lead and timeline. | At the QAPI Committee meeting where pattern is identified; response initiated within 30 calendar days. |\n| 6.3.2 | Assigned lead | Implement the assigned response and report results to the QAPI Committee. Measure effectiveness by tracking: (a) competency reassessment pass rates; (b) quality indicator trend in the correlated area; (c) adverse event rate in the correlated area. | Per assigned timeline; progress reported monthly to committee. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
