        level: 2,
        order: 29,
        body: "10.1 All LUPA Prevention Team members shall receive orientation to this policy, the LUPA Risk Dashboard, root cause classification methodology, and intervention protocols within 14 calendar days of appointment. Orientation shall be conducted by the QAPI Coordinator or CFO designee.\n10.2 All clinical staff (RNs, LVNs, therapists, MSWs, HHAs) shall receive training during annual mandatory training (per HR-TD-001) on: (a) the relationship between visit delivery and patient outcomes; (b) their responsibility to deliver ordered visits and document barriers; (c) the prohibition against non-clinically-justified visit front-loading; (d) how to report scheduling conflicts or barriers to the scheduling coordinator.\n10.3 All scheduling and intake staff shall receive training on LUPA risk identification, dashboard alert response procedures, and their role in proactive rescheduling within 14 calendar days of hire and annually thereafter.\n10.4 All personnel within scope of this policy shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form within 14 calendar days of the policy effective date, any revision, or new assignment.\n10.5 The QAPI Coordinator shall maintain a training tracking log documenting all LUPA-related training including attendee name, topic, date, trainer, and completion status.\n\n---",
