        id: "11-retrospective-utilization-review-post-episode-analysis",
        title: "Retrospective Utilization Review (Post-Episode Analysis)",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Monthly, generate the Retrospective Utilization Analysis Report for all episodes closed in the prior month. The report must include: (a) total episodes closed; (b) episodes by PDGM clinical grouping; (c) average visits per episode by discipline and diagnosis group; (d) frequency variance distribution; (e) LUPA rate (cross-reference QA-PI-006); (f) episodes exceeding high-utilization threshold; (g) average episode length by clinical group; (h) visit counts by clinician. | Monthly; within 10 business days of month end. |\n| 6.4.2 | QAPI Coordinator | Analyze retrospective data for patterns. Flag for UR Committee review: (a) any clinician whose average visits per episode for a diagnosis group exceeds agency average by more than 30%; (b) any clinician whose average visits per episode falls below agency average by more than 30% (potential under-serving); (c) any diagnosis group showing increasing average visits without corresponding clinical acuity change; (d) any referral source whose episodes consistently show outlier utilization patterns. | Monthly as part of report generation. |\n| 6.4.3 | UR Committee / QAPI Committee | Review the Retrospective Utilization Analysis Report at the monthly QAPI Committee meeting. For each pattern identified: (a) review supporting clinical documentation for a sample of episodes (minimum 10% or 5 records, whichever is greater); (b) determine root cause (clinical, documentation, training, systemic); (c) assign corrective action with responsible party and timeline. Document review and decisions in QAPI Committee minutes. | Monthly at QAPI Committee meeting. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
