        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | QAPI Coordinator | Generate a Clinician Utilization Profile quarterly for each active clinical staff member. The profile must include: (a) total episodes managed in the quarter; (b) average visits per episode by discipline; (c) LUPA rate for the clinician's episodes; (d) frequency variance rate; (e) high-utilization outlier rate; (f) documentation timeliness rate (from CL-CD-004 monitoring). | Quarterly; distributed to DON within 10 business days of quarter end. |\n| 6.5.2 | DON / Clinical Supervisor | Review each Clinician Utilization Profile. For any clinician whose profile shows a pattern of outlier utilization (high or low) in 2 or more consecutive quarters: (a) review a sample of the clinician's clinical records for medical necessity documentation adequacy; (b) provide individual education and coaching; (c) if pattern persists for a third consecutive quarter, initiate corrective action per HR-ER-002. Document all reviews and actions. | Within 14 calendar days of profile receipt. |\n\n---",
