        title: "9\\. References",
        level: 2,
        order: 24,
        body: "### 9.1 Federal Regulations\n\n| Citation | Title | Relevance |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 42 CFR § 484.65 | Condition of Participation: QAPI | Utilization data as QAPI input. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.60 | Condition of Participation: Care planning, coordination, and quality of care | Appropriate services per plan of care. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.55 | Condition of Participation: Comprehensive assessment | Assessment drives visit frequency. |\n| 42 CFR § 484.105 | Condition of Participation: Organization and Administration | Governing Body oversight. |\n\n### 9.2 Cross-Referenced Agency Policies\n\n| Policy ID | Policy Title | Relationship |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| QA-PG-001 | QAPI Program Establishment & Governance | Parent framework. |\n| QA-PG-002 | QAPI Plan Development & Annual Review | UR data informs QAPI plan. |\n| QA-PI-001 | Performance Improvement Project Management | PIP triggered by UR patterns. |\n| QA-PI-002 | Quality Indicator Monitoring & Reporting | UR indicators on QAPI dashboard. |\n| QA-PI-006 | Visit Utilization & LUPA Risk Management Program | LUPA monitoring integration. |\n| CL-CP-001 | Plan of Care Development & Approval | Visit frequency orders. |\n| CL-SD-025 | Ordered Visit Frequency Compliance & Monitoring | Visit compliance tracking. |\n| FN-BC-001 | Medicare Billing & Claims Submission | Billing integrity. |\n| FN-CM-003 | Medical Necessity Documentation | Medical necessity standards. |\n| FN-CM-005 | LUPA Prevention & Monitoring | Financial LUPA monitoring. |\n| CO-FA-001 | Anti-Kickback & Stark Law Compliance | Referral pattern monitoring. |\n| CO-RA-002 | Internal Compliance Auditing Program | Audit triggered by UR findings. |\n| HR-ER-002 | Disciplinary Action & Progressive Discipline | Escalation for clinician patterns. |\n| GV-GB-001 | Governing Body Authority & Responsibilities | Governing Body oversight. |\n| EN-TG-001 | Enterprise Policy Taxonomy & Classification Governance | Framework classification. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "module",
