        title: "Monthly Infection Surveillance Summary",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | IPC Designee | Compile the Monthly Infection Surveillance Summary Report (Appendix C) for all infections and exposures reported in the prior month. The report must include: (a) total patient infections by category; (b) infection rates calculated per 100 episodes; (c) 12-month rolling trend for each infection category; (d) comparison to performance thresholds; (e) comparison to prior month; (f) staff occupational exposures; (g) potential clusters identified; (h) process compliance indicator results; (i) corrective actions in progress; (j) external reports filed. | Monthly; completed within 10 business days of month end. |\n| 6.4.2 | IPC Designee / QAPI Coordinator | Present the Monthly Infection Surveillance Summary to the QAPI Committee as a standing agenda item. The presentation must include trend graphs for each infection category, identification of any below-threshold indicators, and recommendations for action. | Monthly at each QAPI Committee meeting. |\n| 6.4.3 | QAPI Committee | Review the infection surveillance summary and: (a) acknowledge categories at or below threshold; (b) for any infection rate exceeding threshold for 2 consecutive months, direct a root cause analysis or contributing factor analysis and corrective action; (c) for any identified cluster, direct a formal investigation per Section 6.5; (d) document all analysis and decisions in committee minutes. | At each monthly QAPI Committee meeting. |\n\n---",
