        id: "12-infection-cluster-investigation",
        title: "Infection Cluster Investigation",
        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | IPC Designee | Declare a cluster when 2 or more cases of the same infection type occur within 30 days that share a potential common exposure factor. Notify the DON, QAPI Coordinator, and Administrator immediately. | Within 1 business day of cluster identification. |\n| 6.5.2 | IPC Designee / QAPI Coordinator | Convene a special cluster investigation meeting within 3 business days. The investigation must: (a) review all cases for commonalities (clinician, visit dates, geographic area, wound type, equipment used); (b) collect additional information from involved clinicians; (c) review process compliance for infection prevention protocols; (d) determine likely transmission mode; (e) implement immediate containment measures. | Within 3 business days of cluster declaration. |\n| 6.5.3 | IPC Designee | Develop and implement a Cluster Response Plan including: (a) immediate corrective actions (re-education, equipment inspection, PPE audit); (b) enhanced monitoring of the affected patient population; (c) any required external reporting (CDPH if disease is reportable); (d) follow-up surveillance plan to verify resolution. Document the plan and submit to QAPI Coordinator. | Within 7 calendar days of cluster declaration. |\n| 6.5.4 | QAPI Committee | Review cluster investigation findings and response plan at the next QAPI Committee meeting (or at a special meeting if urgency requires). Direct development of a formal Corrective Action Plan per QA-AE-003. | At next committee meeting; within 14 calendar days of cluster declaration. |\n\n---",
