        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | QAPI Committee | When any HHCAHPS composite measure falls below the national average for 2 consecutive quarters, the committee shall: (a) identify the specific survey items driving the low composite score; (b) conduct a root cause analysis of the low-scoring items (possible causes: communication skills, timeliness, responsiveness, care quality, education effectiveness); (c) develop a targeted corrective action plan per QA-AE-003 with specific interventions, responsible parties, measurable targets, and timeline; (d) document analysis and plan in committee minutes. | At the committee meeting where the second consecutive below-average quarter is confirmed; CAP within 14 calendar days. |\n| 6.4.2 | Assigned CAP Lead | Implement corrective interventions which may include: (a) staff communication skills training; (b) enhanced patient education protocols; (c) care coordination process improvements; (d) after-hours responsiveness improvements; (e) specific clinical discipline-targeted education. Report progress to QAPI Committee monthly. | Per CAP timeline; monthly progress reports. |\n| 6.4.3 | QAPI Coordinator | Monitor HHCAHPS scores following intervention implementation to assess effectiveness. If no improvement is observed within 2 subsequent quarters, escalate to Governing Body for enhanced intervention or resource allocation. | Monitored each quarterly data release; escalation if no improvement in 6 months. |\n\n---",
