        title: "What Surveyors and Auditors Will Look For",
        level: 3,
        order: 15,
        body: "CMS surveyors conducting an Emergency Preparedness survey under the State Operations Manual Appendix B will specifically verify:\n\n1. That a single, integrated EP program document exists covering all four required elements — not four separate policies. Surveyors are trained to ask for \"your Emergency Preparedness Plan\" and will note fragmentation as a program deficiency.\n2. That the risk assessment was based on the agency's specific geographic service area — not a generic template. For agencies in Southern California, surveyors know the region's hazards (earthquake, wildfire, Santa Ana winds, PSPS events) and will probe whether the plan addresses them.\n3. That the patient vulnerability assessment is documented for all active patients and that an Essential Patients list is maintained in real-time.\n4. That two exercises were conducted in the prior calendar year, with written AARs. Missing an exercise year, or conducting an exercise without an AAR, is a common citation.\n5. That staff can describe their role in the EP plan consistently with what's documented.\n6. That the communication plan is written, tested, and includes all required external contacts.\n7. Governing Body approval of the EP plan is documented in board minutes.\n\n---",
