        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Risk Manager | Implement a multi-source risk identification process that incorporates: (a) incident and near-miss reports (RM-ER-002); (b) complaint and grievance data (OP-PA-001); (c) QAPI findings (QA-PG-001); (d) compliance audit results (CO-RA-002); (e) financial variance analysis (FN-FP-003); (f) staff safety reports (RM-SS-001); (g) patient safety data (QA-AE-004); (h) regulatory change monitoring (CO-RA-001); (i) environmental safety assessments (RM-PS-001); (j) external benchmarking data. | Continuous; formally compiled quarterly. |\n| 5.2.2 | All Staff | Report identified or suspected risks through the agency's incident reporting system within 24 hours of identification, per RM-ER-002. | Within 24 hours of identification. |\n| 5.2.3 | Department Directors | Submit a departmental risk identification summary to the Risk Manager at the close of each quarter, documenting all risks identified within their domain during the period. | Within 10 calendar days of quarter end. |\n| 5.2.4 | Risk Manager | Conduct an annual comprehensive risk assessment (enterprise-wide risk survey) across all 10 policy domains, engaging department directors and key personnel. | Annually; completed within 60 calendar days of fiscal year start. |\n| 5.2.5 | Risk Manager | Conduct an ad hoc risk assessment within 72 hours of any of the following triggering events: (a) sentinel event; (b) CMS survey deficiency at Condition level; (c) significant regulatory change; (d) natural disaster or public health emergency; (e) data breach or security incident; (f) key leadership vacancy; (g) significant financial variance. | Within 72 hours of triggering event. |\n\n---",
