        id: "10-risk-assessment-and-prioritization",
        title: "Risk Assessment and Prioritization",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.3.1 | Risk Manager | Assess each identified risk using the agency's standardized Risk Assessment Matrix (Appendix A) evaluating: (a) Likelihood of occurrence (1–5 scale); (b) Severity of impact (1–5 scale); (c) Risk Score = Likelihood × Severity. | Within 14 calendar days of risk identification. |\n| 5.3.2 | Risk Manager | Categorize each assessed risk by domain: Clinical, Compliance/Regulatory, Financial, Operational, Technology, Human Resources, Reputational, Legal/Litigation, Environmental/Safety. | Concurrent with assessment. |\n| 5.3.3 | Risk Manager | Classify each risk by priority level per the Risk Assessment Matrix: Critical (20–25), High (12–19), Moderate (6–11), Low (1–5). | Concurrent with assessment. |\n| 5.3.4 | Risk Management Committee | Review and validate all Critical and High priority risk assessments. Validate that risk scores, categorizations, and priority classifications are accurate and consistent. | At each quarterly meeting; within 48 hours for Critical risks. |\n| 5.3.5 | Risk Manager | Escalate all Critical priority risks to the Administrator immediately upon identification and to the Governing Body within 72 hours, with a preliminary mitigation recommendation. | Immediately to Administrator; within 72 hours to Governing Body. |\n\n---",
