        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.4.1 | Risk Manager | Develop a Risk Mitigation Plan (Appendix B) for each Critical and High priority risk, documenting: (a) risk description and root cause; (b) current controls in place; (c) proposed mitigation actions; (d) responsible party (Risk Owner); (e) implementation timeline; (f) success metrics; (g) residual risk assessment; (h) monitoring frequency. | Within 7 calendar days for Critical; within 14 calendar days for High. |\n| 5.4.2 | Risk Owner (Assigned) | Implement approved mitigation actions per the plan timeline and report progress to the Risk Manager at defined intervals. | Per plan timeline; progress reports at minimum monthly. |\n| 5.4.3 | Risk Manager | Develop mitigation recommendations for Moderate priority risks. Low priority risks shall be documented in the Risk Register with accepted status and monitored for escalation. | Within 30 calendar days of assessment for Moderate risks. |\n| 5.4.4 | Risk Management Committee | Review and approve all Critical and High priority mitigation plans. Approve or modify Risk Owner assignments. | At next scheduled meeting; within 48 hours for Critical risks. |\n| 5.4.5 | Governing Body | Review and approve mitigation plans for Critical priority risks. Confirm risk appetite alignment. | At next quarterly meeting; within 7 calendar days for imminent patient safety risks. |\n\n---",
