        title: "Immediate Response",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.1.1 | Reporting Staff Member | Ensure immediate safety of all persons involved. Provide first aid or emergency medical care as needed. Call 911 if life-threatening emergency exists. | Immediately upon incident occurrence. |\n| 5.1.2 | Reporting Staff Member | Notify the immediate supervisor verbally of the incident. | Within 1 hour of incident occurrence. |\n| 5.1.3 | Supervisor | For sentinel events or serious adverse events: Notify the Risk Manager, Director of Nursing, and Administrator immediately by phone. | Within 1 hour of notification. |\n| 5.1.4 | Director of Nursing | For patient-related incidents: Assess the patient's current condition and ensure appropriate clinical intervention is initiated. Notify the attending physician as clinically indicated. | Within 2 hours of notification. |\n\n---",
