        id: "11-investigation-process",
        title: "Investigation Process",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.4.1 | Risk Manager | For Level 3–5 incidents, initiate a formal investigation. Preserve all relevant evidence including: (a) clinical records; (b) staff schedules; (c) equipment involved; (d) photographs (if applicable); (e) witness statements; (f) electronic system logs. | Investigation initiated within 24 hours for Level 4–5; within 72 hours for Level 3. |\n| 5.4.2 | Risk Manager | Interview all involved parties and witnesses. Document interviews using the Witness Statement Form (Appendix D). Interviews shall be conducted individually in a private setting. | Within 7 calendar days of incident for Level 3; within 48 hours for Level 4–5. |\n| 5.4.3 | Risk Manager | For Level 4–5 incidents, convene an Investigation Team comprising: Risk Manager (lead), Director of Nursing (for clinical incidents), department director of involved area, and Compliance Officer (if regulatory implications). | Within 48 hours of incident. |\n| 5.4.4 | Investigation Team | Conduct root cause analysis per QA-AE-002 for all Level 4–5 incidents. Document findings using the Root Cause Analysis template. | Completed within 30 calendar days of incident. |\n| 5.4.5 | Risk Manager | Complete the Investigation Summary Report (Appendix E) for all Level 3–5 incidents, documenting: (a) incident summary; (b) investigation methodology; (c) findings of fact; (d) root cause(s) identified; (e) contributing factors; (f) recommendations; (g) corrective actions required. | Within 14 calendar days for Level 3; within 30 calendar days for Level 4–5. |\n| 5.4.6 | Risk Manager | For Level 1–2 incidents, the supervisor completes a brief investigation summary on the Incident Report Form (Appendix A, Section 3) and submits to Risk Manager for trending. | Within 7 calendar days of incident. |\n\n---",
