        body: "9.1 All new employees shall receive incident reporting training during orientation, within 14 calendar days of hire, covering: (a) what constitutes a reportable incident; (b) how to complete the Incident Report Form; (c) to whom and when to report; (d) non-retaliation protections; (e) distinction between incident report and clinical documentation.\n9.2 All staff shall receive annual refresher training on incident reporting.\n9.3 All supervisory staff shall receive additional training on: (a) Incident Report review and completion oversight; (b) immediate response and escalation protocols; (c) evidence preservation.\n9.4 The Risk Manager and Investigation Team members shall receive training on investigation methodology and root cause analysis.\n9.5 All in-scope personnel shall sign the Policy Acknowledgment Form (Appendix G) within 14 calendar days of effective date, revision, or new hire.\n\n---",
