        id: "9-trending-analysis",
        title: "Trending Analysis",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Risk Manager | Conduct monthly trending analysis of incident data by: (a) incident type; (b) severity level; (c) location/setting; (d) time of day/day of week; (e) staff role; (f) patient demographics (de-identified); (g) contributing factors. | Monthly. |\n| 5.2.2 | Risk Manager | Compare current period data to: (a) prior month; (b) same month prior year; (c) rolling 12-month average (baseline). Identify statistically significant increases or decreases. | Monthly. |\n| 5.2.3 | Risk Manager | Analyze leading indicators monthly: (a) staffing vacancy rates; (b) training compliance rates; (c) documentation deficiency rates; (d) complaint volume; (e) equipment maintenance overdue items; (f) policy acknowledgment compliance. | Monthly. |\n| 5.2.4 | Risk Manager | Prepare the Quarterly Risk Trending Report (Appendix B) including: (a) incident volume and severity trends; (b) risk category trends; (c) leading indicator analysis; (d) cluster identification; (e) risk mitigation effectiveness assessment; (f) comparative benchmarking (if available); (g) recommendations. | Quarterly. |\n\n---",
