        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Claim | A demand for compensation or other relief arising from alleged injury, harm, or loss attributed to the agency's services or operations. |\n| Demand Letter | A written communication from a claimant or attorney asserting a claim and demanding resolution. |\n| Litigation Hold | A directive to preserve all documents, records, electronic data, and communications related to anticipated or pending litigation. |\n| Reservation of Rights | A notice from an insurance carrier that it will investigate and defend a claim while reserving the right to deny coverage. |\n| Settlement | Resolution of a claim through negotiated agreement without trial. |\n| Discovery | The legal process of exchanging relevant information between parties in litigation. |\n\n---",
