        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Risk Manager | Conduct a comprehensive workplace hazard assessment of all work environments including: (a) main office; (b) any branch/satellite offices; (c) generic home environment hazards applicable to all patient home visits (e.g., slips, biological exposures, violence, physical demands, heat). Document findings in the Hazard Assessment Report (Appendix B). | Annually; initial assessment within 30 days of IIPP adoption. |\n| 6.4.2 | Risk Manager | Conduct unannounced and periodic office safety inspections at least quarterly. Inspection scope: physical hazards (trip/slip, fire exits, ergonomics), biological hazard controls, PPE availability, emergency equipment. Use the Office Safety Inspection Checklist (Appendix C). | Quarterly; document in inspection log. |\n| 6.4.3 | Clinical Staff (field employees) | Before entering any patient residence, perform a brief visual safety assessment using the Field Visit Safety Checklist (Appendix D): (a) presence of animals/pets that pose injury risk; (b) obvious structural hazards (broken stairs, inadequate lighting); (c) presence of firearms or weapons in view; (d) behavioral/mental health indicators affecting safety; (e) temperature extremes. | Before each visit. |\n| 6.4.4 | Risk Manager | Review all completed Field Visit Safety Checklist reports monthly to identify trending hazards across the patient population and geographic area. Adjust hazard controls accordingly. | Monthly review; documented in IIPP log. |\n| 6.4.5 | Risk Manager | When a new job task, patient population, service type, or geographic area is added to the agency's operations, conduct a targeted hazard assessment for the new activity before the first employee performs that task in that capacity. | Before introduction of new activities. |\n\n---",
