        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Director of Nursing / Risk Manager | Conduct and document an ATD Exposure Determination that identifies, by job classification, all employees with potential occupational ATD exposure without regard to personal protective equipment. Attach the Exposure Determination Table (Appendix A) to this ECP. | At ECP adoption; reviewed and confirmed annually. |\n| 6.1.2 | Director of Nursing | For each identified job classification, document the specific ATD exposure pathways: (a) direct patient care involving respiratory assessment; (b) aerosol-generating procedures (suctioning, nebulizer, oxygen therapy, CPR); (c) presence in confined spaces (small rooms) with ATD patients without adequate ventilation; (d) transport of patients with ATD. | At ECP adoption; reviewed and confirmed annually. |\n| 6.1.3 | Risk Manager | When a new clinical role or service line is established, conduct a supplemental Exposure Determination within 30 days of service introduction to assess ATD exposure risk for the new role. Update Appendix A accordingly. | Within 30 days of new service introduction. |\n\n---",
