        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.3.1 | Risk Manager / Agency Supply | Provide all BBP-applicable PPE to employees at no cost: (a) exam gloves (non-latex option available for employees with latex sensitivity); (b) fluid-resistant gowns or aprons for procedures with splash risk; (c) face shields or safety glasses + mask for procedures with OPIM splash/spray risk; (d) surgical masks; (e) CPR barrier devices; (f) portable sharps containers for field use. | PPE available before any employee begins duties with exposure risk; replenished as needed. |\n| 6.3.2 | All Clinical Staff | Wear gloves for all anticipated direct contact with blood, OPIM, mucous membranes, non-intact skin, or contaminated surfaces or items. Replace gloves that are torn, punctured, or significantly contaminated. Double-glove when performing procedures with high sharps risk (e.g., complex wound care, IV removal from agitated patient). | Every patient contact involving exposure risk. |\n| 6.3.3 | All Clinical Staff | Wear appropriate face and eye protection (face shield or goggles + mask) when performing procedures that create splash or spray of blood or OPIM: suctioning, wound irrigation, IV access in high-pressure lines, bleeding control of arterial sites. | During AGP-type or splash-risk procedures. |\n| 6.3.4 | All Clinical Staff | If PPE is penetrated (e.g., glove puncture) or if another mechanism creates potential exposure, report as an Exposure Incident per Section 6.6 immediately. | Immediately. |\n| 6.3.5 | Director of Nursing | Evaluate the adequacy of PPE type and availability at least annually by reviewing exposure incident patterns, sharps injury log, and employee feedback. Update the PPE supply protocol accordingly. | Annually. |\n\n---",
