        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | HR / Risk Manager | Offer the HBV vaccine series at no cost to all employees with occupational exposure, as identified in Appendix A. The offer shall be made after BBP training and within 10 working days of initial assignment to an occupationally exposed position. | Within 10 working days of assignment. |\n| 6.4.2 | HR | Document the HBV vaccination offer and employee response on the HBV Vaccine Offer/Declination Form (Appendix B). If the employee declines the vaccine, obtain a signed declination statement. Employees who decline may later request vaccination at no cost while still employed in an exposure-risk position. | At time of offer; update if employee later accepts. |\n| 6.4.3 | HR | Maintain proof of HBV vaccination series completion (or documented immunity via titer) and signed declination statements in the employee's confidential medical file. | At time of vaccination or declination. |\n| 6.4.4 | HR / Risk Manager | After completion of the 3-dose HBV series, offer post-vaccination serology testing (anti-HBs) to verify immune response if employee requests, or in the event of a subsequent occupational HBV exposure (non-immune employees require expedited evaluation). | Per employee request or post-exposure determination. |\n| 6.4.5 | HR | Offer HBV booster or revaccination per current CDC guidance when new guidance recommends it, or if a non-immune employee is identified after a prior completed series. | Per CDC/ACIP guidance updates. |\n\n---",
