        title: "Housekeeping and Decontamination",
        level: 3,
        order: 12,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.5.1 | Clinical Staff | After any clinical procedure in a patient home involving blood or OPIM: (a) discard all single-use contaminated sharps in the portable sharps container; (b) discard all single-use contaminated PPE in a biohazard waste bag; (c) clean any surface contaminated with blood or OPIM using an appropriate disinfectant (EPA-registered hospital-grade disinfectant active against HIV and HBV) from the agency's approved supply list; (d) seal and return biohazard waste bag from the patient home per agency waste disposal protocol. | After each procedure. |\n| 6.5.2 | Risk Manager | Maintain an approved list of EPA-registered disinfectants suitable for blood/OPIM decontamination that field staff are authorized to use. Post the list in the agency office and include in field supply kits. | Maintained continuously; reviewed annually. |\n| 6.5.3 | Clinical Staff | Never transport contaminated sharps in soft bags, pockets, or any container not specifically designated as a sharps container. Transport full portable sharps containers sealed per manufacturer instructions to the agency office for proper disposal per agency biomedical waste disposal agreement. | Continuous. |\n\n---",
