        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.4.1 | Supervisor / HR | Implement the acclimatization schedule for: (a) all new employees during their first 14 calendar days of outdoor work in heat conditions; (b) any employee returning from an absence of ≥14 calendar days who will be working in heat conditions. The progressive acclimatization schedule for new employees: Day 1–3: max 50% of normal heat-exposure duty; Day 4–7: max 70%; Day 8–14: max 90%; Day 15+: full duty. | Starting from first day of heat-exposed work for new employees; from first day back for returning employees. |\n| 6.4.2 | Supervisor | Monitor all newly acclimatizing employees with increased supervisory contacts during the first 14 days: check-in by phone at a minimum at the start and end of each shift. Document check-ins on Acclimatization Monitoring Log (Appendix B). | Daily during first 14 days. |\n| 6.4.3 | All Employees | Alert supervisor if experiencing heat illness symptoms during acclimatization period. The risk of heat illness is highest during the first days of heat exposure. Do not dismiss early symptoms, and escalate to emergency response if a co-worker or patient reports an employee appearing confused, not sweating in high heat, or unresponsive. | Continuously during acclimatization period. |\n\n---",
