        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 6.1.1 | Risk Manager | Maintain the written IIPP document per 8 CCR § 3203. Review and update at least annually and whenever new hazards are identified. | Annual review; updated within 14 calendar days of any new hazard identification. |\n| 6.1.2 | Risk Manager | Conduct workplace hazard assessments: (a) agency office — at least annually; (b) patient home environments — at each admission and when conditions change (per RM-PS-001); (c) whenever new equipment, processes, or substances are introduced. | Per schedule defined above. |\n| 6.1.3 | Risk Manager | Investigate all work-related injuries, illnesses, and exposure incidents within 72 hours of report. Document: (a) description; (b) root cause; (c) corrective action; (d) responsible party; (e) completion date. | Investigation initiated within 72 hours; corrective action implementation tracked per QA-AE-003. |\n| 6.1.4 | Risk Manager | Maintain a safety communication system: (a) safety committee meetings (quarterly); (b) posted safety information; (c) mechanism for employees to report hazards anonymously without fear of reprisal. | Continuous; safety committee quarterly. |\n| 6.1.5 | Risk Manager | Correct identified hazards in a timely manner. Imminent hazards: immediately remove employees from the area and correct before resuming work. Non-imminent hazards: correct within 30 calendar days with interim controls if needed. | Imminent: immediately. Non-imminent: 30 calendar days. |\n\n---",
