        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | All Visiting Clinicians | Observe the home environment at each visit for new or changed hazards. Document any new hazard identified. | Every visit. |\n| 5.2.2 | All Visiting Clinicians | If a new hazard is identified: (a) document on the Environmental Safety Update Form (Appendix B); (b) provide patient/caregiver education; (c) notify the primary nurse/case manager; (d) notify the supervisor if HIGH severity. | At time of identification. |\n| 5.2.3 | Primary Nurse / Case Manager | Complete a formal reassessment of the home environment using Appendix A at each recertification period. | At each recertification. |\n| 5.2.4 | Primary Nurse / Case Manager | Complete a formal reassessment within 7 calendar days of any of the following: (a) patient fall in the home; (b) report of injury in the home; (c) change in patient mobility or functional status; (d) change in medical equipment; (e) change in household members; (f) report from any clinician of new hazard. | Within 7 calendar days of trigger. |\n\n---",
