        id: "11-pharmaceutical-waste-disposal",
        title: "Pharmaceutical Waste Disposal",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.4.1 | All Clinical Staff | Educate patients and caregivers on safe disposal of unused or expired medications per FDA guidelines: (a) medication take-back programs; (b) DEA-authorized collection sites; (c) FDA flush list (select medications); (d) household trash method (mix with coffee grounds/kitty litter, seal in container). | At SOC; at discharge; as needed. |\n| 5.4.2 | All Clinical Staff | Do not accept or transport patient medications. If medication disposal is necessary during a visit (e.g., contaminated medication), document the disposal, amount, and method. | As needed. |\n| 5.4.3 | Director of Nursing | For controlled substance disposal witnessed in the home, ensure two staff members are present and both sign the disposal documentation. | As applicable. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
