        level: 2,
        order: 20,
        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Staff use PPE appropriately | Supervisory observation; staff self-report; patient feedback | Zero observed non-compliance. |\n| Sharps disposed of in approved containers | Audit of supply usage; incident reports | Zero sharps injuries from improper disposal. |\n| Biohazardous waste properly contained and labeled | Audit of waste storage area | 100% compliance. |\n| Exposure incidents reported within 24 hours | Incident report timestamps | 100% compliance. |\n| Post-exposure medical evaluation completed | Medical records review | 100% of exposed employees evaluated. |\n| Waste hauler contract current | Contract file review | Current at all times; no lapse. |\n| Sharps Injury Log maintained | Log review | Current; entries within 14 days of incident. |\n| Training current for all staff | Training log review | 100% within 14 days of hire; annual refresher. |\n\n#### Common Failure Points\n\n| Failure Point | Risk | Mitigation |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| Recapping of needles by staff. | Needlestick injury; bloodborne pathogen exposure. | Enforce prohibition; include in annual training; zero tolerance. |\n| No sharps container carried to visit. | Improper sharps disposal; injury risk. | Supply management; pre-visit checklist; supervisory monitoring. |\n| Exposure incident not reported. | No medical evaluation; compliance violation. | Enforce reporting; emphasize in training; non-punitive reporting culture. |\n| Medical waste disposed in household trash. | Environmental contamination; regulatory violation. | Train on proper segregation; supply biohazard bags. |\n| Waste hauler contract lapsed. | Medical waste accumulation; regulatory violation. | Risk Manager/Operations Director tracks expiration; 90-day renewal lead time. |\n\n---",
