        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Product Recall | A notification from a manufacturer, the FDA, or other regulatory body that a medical product, device, or equipment has been found to be defective, dangerous, or non-compliant and must be removed from use, returned, repaired, or replaced. |\n| FDA Safety Alert | A notification issued by the FDA regarding safety concerns with a specific product or device that may not require recall but warrants monitoring and precautions. |\n| Class I Recall | A recall where there is a reasonable probability that the use of or exposure to a product will cause serious adverse health consequences or death. |\n| Class II Recall | A recall where the use of or exposure to a product may cause temporary or medically reversible adverse health consequences. |\n| Class III Recall | A recall where the use of or exposure to a product is not likely to cause adverse health consequences. |\n| Affected Product | Any product, device, or equipment in the agency's possession or in use by agency patients that is subject to a recall or safety alert. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "module",
