        id: "9-recall-response-agency-held-products",
        title: "Recall Response — Agency-Held Products",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Risk Manager | Upon identification of a recall affecting products in agency inventory: (a) determine the recall classification (Class I, II, or III); (b) identify all affected product by lot number, serial number, or model; (c) log the recall in the Recall Tracking Log (Appendix A). | Within 24 hours for Class I; within 72 hours for Class II/III. |\n| 5.2.2 | Risk Manager / Operations Director | Immediately remove all affected products from active inventory. Segregate and label \"DO NOT USE — RECALL.\" Secure in a designated area. | Within 24 hours for Class I; within 72 hours for Class II/III. |\n| 5.2.3 | Operations Director | Follow manufacturer/FDA instructions for disposition: (a) return to manufacturer; (b) repair/replacement; (c) destroy per instructions. Document disposition. | Per manufacturer/FDA instructions. |\n| 5.2.4 | Risk Manager | Notify the Director of Nursing and Administrator of the recall and actions taken. | Within 24 hours for Class I; within 72 hours for Class II/III. |\n\n---",
        scormChunkHint: "lesson",
