        body: "| Compliance Indicator | Measurement Method | Acceptable Standard |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| High-risk medications identified and flagged in patient record | Clinical record audit | 100% compliance. |\n| High-Risk Medication Safety Assessment completed at SOC/ROC | Clinical record audit | 100% completion. |\n| Monitoring parameters established in plan of care | Plan of care audit | 100% for patients on high-risk meds. |\n| Medication-specific assessments performed at each visit | Visit documentation audit | ≥95% compliance. |\n| Patient/caregiver education documented with teach-back | Education record audit | ≥95% for patients on high-risk meds. |\n| Adverse events involving high-risk medications reported | Incident report review | 100% compliance. |\n| Quarterly QAPI reporting on high-risk medication safety | QAPI meeting minutes | 4 reports per year. |\n\n#### Common Failure Points\n\n| Failure Point | Risk | Mitigation |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| High-risk medications not identified in patient record. | Enhanced monitoring not initiated; adverse events. | Enforce §5.1.2 identification at SOC/medication reconciliation. |\n| Monitoring parameters not established. | Inadequate surveillance; delayed detection of adverse effects. | Enforce §5.2.2; include in care plan audit. |\n| Laboratory results not followed up timely. | Therapeutic failure or toxicity. | Enforce §5.2.4; 4-hour notification standard. |\n| Education insufficient; patient does not understand medication risks. | Non-adherence; self-medication errors; adverse events. | Enforce teach-back method per §5.4.2. |\n\n---",
