        title: "Duress Communication",
        level: 3,
        order: 11,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.4.1 | Risk Manager | Establish and communicate an agency-wide duress code — a specific word or phrase that staff can use during a phone call to indicate they are in danger without alerting a threatening person. | At program establishment; refreshed annually. |\n| 5.4.2 | All Staff | If unable to leave safely, use the duress code during any phone communication. | As needed. |\n| 5.4.3 | Office/On-Call Staff | Upon hearing the duress code: (a) do NOT acknowledge the code verbally; (b) keep the caller on the line; (c) immediately contact law enforcement and provide the staff member's location; (d) notify the Administrator. | Immediately upon hearing duress code. |\n\n---",
