        title: "3\\. Definitions",
        level: 2,
        order: 6,
        body: "| Term | Definition |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Workplace Violence | Any act or threat of physical violence, harassment, intimidation, bullying, or other threatening disruptive behavior that occurs at any work location. |\n| Type I Violence | Violence by persons with no relationship to the agency (e.g., stranger, intruder during a home visit). |\n| Type II Violence | Violence by patients, family members, or caregivers. |\n| Type III Violence | Violence by current or former employees. |\n| Type IV Violence | Violence by persons with a personal relationship with an employee (e.g., domestic violence that follows employee to work). |\n| Threat Assessment | A structured evaluation of a reported threat to determine credibility, immediacy, and appropriate response. |\n| Workplace Violence Incident Log | The record of all workplace violence incidents as required by Cal/OSHA. |\n\n---",
