        id: "8-workplace-violence-prevention-plan-wvpp",
        title: "Workplace Violence Prevention Plan (WVPP)",
        level: 3,
        order: 8,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.1.1 | Risk Manager | Develop and maintain a written Workplace Violence Prevention Plan (Appendix A) in compliance with Cal/OSHA requirements (Labor Code § 6401.9). The Plan shall include: (a) persons responsible for implementation; (b) procedures for employee involvement; (c) methods for coordination with other employers (if shared worksites); (d) procedures for accepting and responding to reports; (e) procedures to ensure no retaliation; (f) procedures for response and investigation; (g) training requirements; (h) workplace violence incident log procedures; (i) emergency response procedures; (j) plan review frequency. | Within 30 days of policy effective date; reviewed annually. |\n| 5.1.2 | Risk Manager | Conduct an annual workplace violence hazard assessment identifying: (a) types of violence to which staff are exposed; (b) specific risk factors (home visits, after-hours, high-risk patients); (c) environmental risk factors; (d) history of workplace violence incidents. | Annually; updated upon any violent incident. |\n| 5.1.3 | Risk Manager | Implement corrective measures to address identified hazards including: (a) safety equipment; (b) administrative controls (scheduling, buddy system per RM-SS-001); (c) training; (d) communication systems. | Within 30 days of hazard identification. |\n\n---",
