        title: "Incident Reporting and Response",
        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | Any Staff Member | Immediately remove yourself from imminent danger. Call 911 if physical violence is occurring or imminent. | Immediately. |\n| 5.2.2 | Any Staff Member | Report the incident to your immediate supervisor and the Risk Manager as soon as safely possible. | Within 2 hours of incident. |\n| 5.2.3 | Any Staff Member | Complete an Incident Report per RM-ER-002, Appendix A. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.2.4 | Risk Manager | Log the incident in the Workplace Violence Incident Log (Appendix B) as required by Cal/OSHA. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.2.5 | Risk Manager | Conduct a threat assessment for any credible threat, evaluating: (a) specificity of threat; (b) history of violence; (c) access to weapons; (d) behavioral indicators; (e) current emotional state; (f) proximity to the threatened person. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.2.6 | Risk Manager | Based on threat assessment, implement appropriate response: ☐ Low Risk: Document; monitor; adjust safety measures. ☐ Moderate Risk: Implement protective measures (reassignment, buddy system, law enforcement notification). ☐ High Risk: Immediately suspend visits; notify law enforcement; obtain protective order if warranted; provide staff with EAP referral and safety planning. | Immediately upon assessment completion. |\n\n---",
