        level: 3,
        order: 9,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.2.1 | All Driving Staff | Comply with all applicable traffic laws at all times when driving for agency business. | At all times. |\n| 5.2.2 | All Driving Staff | Wear a seatbelt at all times while the vehicle is in motion. Ensure all passengers wear seatbelts. | At all times. |\n| 5.2.3 | All Driving Staff | Do not operate a handheld electronic device while driving. If a call must be made or answered, pull over safely and stop the vehicle before using the device. Hands-free use is permitted only if the device is mounted and requires only a single tap to activate; no texting or emailing by any method is permitted while driving. | At all times. |\n| 5.2.4 | All Driving Staff | Do not drive while under the influence of alcohol, illegal drugs, or any prescription/over-the-counter medication that impairs driving ability. | At all times. |\n| 5.2.5 | All Driving Staff | Conduct a brief pre-trip vehicle inspection before the first driving assignment of each workday: (a) tires (visual condition); (b) lights and signals; (c) windshield wipers; (d) mirrors; (e) fuel level adequate for planned routes. | Before first trip each day. |\n| 5.2.6 | All Driving Staff | Exercise increased caution during adverse driving conditions including rain, fog, darkness, construction zones, and unfamiliar areas. Delay or reschedule non-urgent visits if conditions create significant danger, with supervisor notification. | As conditions warrant. |\n| 5.2.7 | Supervisors | Do not require staff to drive in conditions that present a clear and significant danger to safety (e.g., severe weather, road closures). Follow OP-SL-007 for inclement weather decisions. | As conditions warrant. |\n\n---",
