        id: "10-motor-vehicle-accident-response",
        title: "Motor Vehicle Accident Response",
        level: 3,
        order: 10,
        body: "| Step | Responsible Party | Action | Timeframe |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 5.3.1 | Involved Driver | If involved in a motor vehicle accident while on agency business: (a) Stop the vehicle immediately. Do not leave the scene. (b) Check for injuries to self and others. (c) Call 911 if there are injuries, significant property damage, or road hazard. (d) Move vehicles out of traffic if safe to do so and no injuries. (e) Exchange information with other parties: name, insurance, license, vehicle registration. (f) Obtain names and contact information of witnesses. (g) Take photographs of the scene, vehicle damage, and road conditions if safely possible. (h) Do not admit fault or make statements beyond exchanging required information. | Immediately at scene. |\n| 5.3.2 | Involved Driver | Notify the immediate supervisor by phone as soon as safely possible after the accident. | As soon as safely possible; within 1 hour. |\n| 5.3.3 | Involved Driver | Complete the Motor Vehicle Accident Report Form (Appendix B) documenting all details of the accident. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.3.4 | Supervisor | Notify the Risk Manager of the accident. | Within 2 hours of being notified. |\n| 5.3.5 | Risk Manager | Log the accident in the Incident Tracking Log per RM-ER-002. Obtain the police report number. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.3.6 | Risk Manager | Notify the agency's automobile insurance carrier per RM-ER-004 policy terms. | Within 24 hours. |\n| 5.3.7 | Risk Manager | If the driver or any other person was injured, ensure appropriate medical treatment and complete workers' compensation reporting per HR-WM-004 and OSHA requirements per 29 CFR § 1904. | Within 24 hours; OSHA reporting per regulatory timeframes. |\n| 5.3.8 | Risk Manager | Determine if the patient visit schedule requires adjustment due to vehicle availability, driver injury, or driver distress. Coordinate with scheduling per OP-SL-001. | Within 24 hours. |\n\n---",
